{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse","id":288755,"title":"[OOC] Rage Across the Delaware Valley- Werewolf: the Apocalypse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-21T12:24:17-07:00","id":288755,"title":"[OOC] Rage Across the Delaware Valley- Werewolf: the Apocalypse","content":"<u>Character Creation</u><br /> <br /> Herein are the rules for Character Creation. As the ST, I, of course, retain the right to modify these at any time at need to make the game more fun for us all. We will primarily be using the W20 ruleset, but if there is a particular rite or gift or whatever that you seek to draw from an older source, feel free to ask. The following post will include a template for the character sheet; please use it. It makes my life much easier if I can easily reference the character stats in the same format for everyone. In that same post, I will reserve space for each individual character sheet to be stored. These will be the official copies of your character sheets. They will always be right here, on page 1 of the thread, for easy reference.<br /> <br /> Also, please feel free to make suggestions to improve the character sheet template, if you feel I\u2019ve left anything out.<br /> <br /> You will notice that this means all of you can see the other\u2019s character sheets. This is intentional. I believe the best, and longest lasting, RPGs are those where the players work cooperatively, not competitively. While there may be some rare aspects of a character\u2019s information that should be kept secret for dramatic reasons, this is not usually the case. If there is any part of your character sheet that you feel should be kept hidden from your fellow players, PM me and make your case. I am always open to discussion.<br /> <br /> Please remember also that I am, as I have stated, a very hands-on ST. Please consider your character sheets to be first drafts for us to work on together.<br /> <br /> <u>Step One: Character Concept</u><br /> <br /> We have already discussed our concepts at length, and I see no need to further belabor the point. Step one is complete! See? We\u2019re further along than you thought.<br /> <br /> <u>Step Two: Attributes</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">We will be using the standard 7/5/3 split among attributes, with each character starting with 1 in each attribute. Remember that a rating of 2 is considered the human average! Ratings of 2-4 will not elicit special comment from me, provided they are not directly contradicted by your character\u2019s history. A rating of 1 or 5, however, will need to be justified. None of the characters seem to be so deficient in any area that a rating of 1 would be justified, but if you think it is appropriate for your character, make your case. A rating of 5 is more easily understood for some traits for some of these characters, but I would still like to know your justification for placing your character at the pinnacle of human attributes at character creation. Also, remember to choose a specialty for every attribute rated above 4 dots. Custom specialties are welcome, subject to my approval!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Step Three: Abilities</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Once again, standard 13/9/5 spread. However, know that I pay much closer attention to abilities. There should be something in your background to justify each ability on some level or another. Remember also the three dot limitation on starting abilities. This can be raised higher with freebie points; however, there should be a good justification for raising an ability to 4 at character creation. Ratings of 5 are generally off-limits to starting characters- there would have to be a phenomenally good explanation for why your character is, as a cub, considered one of the world\u2019s greatest experts in their field. I am slightly more lenient with Talents than I am with Skills and Knowledges, but not by much. Remember also to choose a specialty for any ability rated 4 or higher, or for any ability which requires a specialty at any level, such as Crafts or Science. Remember also the Lupus starting ability restrictions.<br /> <br /> A few minor house rules- first, I treat Expression the same ways as Academics, Crafts or Science are treated in W20. A specialty must be chosen as soon as the ability is purchased.<br /> <br /> Kailindo, Klaiveskar, Iksakku and other similarly esoteric abilities are off-limits at character creation. Finding a mentor for these abilities (or specialties) later is certainly possible, but these disciplines are not taught to cubs in my setting.<br /> <br /> All Lupus characters must purchase at least one dot of Primal Urge, to represent their lives as wolves.<br /> <br /> All Metis characters must purchase at least one dot of Rituals, to represent their upbringing within Garou society (unless their backstory precludes this for some reason).<br /> <br /> Any character that takes one or more levels in Rituals will start with knowledge of one or more appropriate Rites, chosen by me, for free. This is above and beyond any rites gained from the Rites background.<br /> <br /> Remember that your choices in abilities represent the sum total of your character\u2019s skills, talents and knowledge as of their First Change. I encourage you to keep this in mind and create well rounded individuals. The Hobby Talent, Professional Skill and Expert Knowledge abilities are all excellent ways to model this, but even the standard abilities involve a lot of ways to express your characters\u2019 unique interests and training.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Step Four: Advantages</u><br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As normal, each character will begin with five dots of backgrounds. These can be raised as high as five with no restrictions, beyond the need to justify any levels in any background in your character\u2019s history.<br /> <br /> We will not be using pooled backgrounds (except for totems, of course).<br /> <br /> Backgrounds may not be raised with experience- they can only be gained (and lost) through play. The exception is Totem, which may be increased at a cost of 3 xp per dot.<br /> <br /> Fate: We will not be using the Fate background in this game.<br /> <br /> Fetish: Talens and low level fetishes are acceptable, within reason and subject to my approval. However, cubs are not entrusted with level 4 or 5 fetishes, nor will any character begin play with a Klaive or tribal signature weapon such as a Labrys or Jarlhammer. I may make an exception if they are an integral part of the character history, but even then I would prefer not.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk: Characters do not necessarily have to spend dots to represent kinfolk of their immediate family if those family members are covered in the backstory. However, spending the points makes it more likely for said kinfolk to be both available and useful to the character. Especially useful kinfolk, immediate family or no, should instead be purchased as Allies or Contacts.<br /> <br /> Mentor: Any mentor should be a part of the backstory. Ratings in the mentor background can be flexible. For example, a Rank 5 mentor that is rarely available and often busy or away would cost fewer dots than normal.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed: Bear in mind the purity of your character\u2019s lineage when purchasing this trait, as per your backstory. Remember that Pure Breed is tribe-specific. I warn you now, I am extremely critical of high levels of Pure Breed unless it is a vital part of the backstory.<br /> <br /> Resources: Be sure to consider the source of your character\u2019s resources when making a selection; it is hard to keep a steady job and be a member of a globe-trotting Garou pack.<br /> <br /> Rites: I reserve the right to approve all rite selections. Certain high level rites, such as the Rite of Caern Building, are simply not taught to cubs. This is especially true of tribe-specific rites.<br /> <br /> Totem: Every character must purchase at least one dot of Totem at character creation, to represent basic ties to the pack. The more dots spent collectively, the more powerful the totem will be. The totem will be chosen after the rite of passage. Unlike other backgrounds, the Totem background is not limited to five dots. It may be raised as much as the player desires and can afford (within reason). Personal totems are not permitted at character creation, though I am not totally opposed to the idea of them coming up later as the result of a suitable quest.<br /> <br /> Pack Status: We will not be using the Pack Status background.<br /> <br /> Sept Standing: We will not be using the Sept Standing background.<br /> <br /> I am open to certain other backgrounds from older sources, within reason. If there is a background from a revised source that was not translated to W20, but which you feel is necessary or appropriate for your character, feel free to run it by me.<br /> <br /> Regarding tribal restrictions on backgrounds, I have my own ideas about those (if you\u2019re curious about my rationale, feel free to ask):<br /> <br /> Black Furies: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Pure Breed is restricted; Resources is discouraged<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Fianna: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: Pure Breed and Ancestors are discouraged<br /> <br /> Red Talons: Resources is discouraged; Kinfolk may only be wolves; Allies and Contacts are almost never humans<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Ancestors is restricted (and no getting around it with funny merits, either)<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: Minimum Pure Breed 3<br /> <br /> Stargazers: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Uktena: No Restrictions<br /> <br /> Wendigo: No Restrictions</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The following Level One gifts have relevant House Rules:<br /> <br /> Smell of Man: Effect can be suppressed for a scene by spending a Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Open Seal: When used against something sealed with magic, the difficulty may be increased above that of the local Gauntlet rating at the discretion of the ST, in addition to requiring the expenditure of a Gnosis point.<br /> <br /> Spirit Speech: Totem Spirits, Incarnae, Celestines, Ancestor Spirits and others with frequent dealings with the Garou may make themselves understood even in the absence of this gift, if they so desire. However, anyone attempting to influence or negotiate with spirits who does not possess this gift increases all difficulties involved by three; the only exception to this rule is Garou ancestor spirits, who are perfectly comfortable conversing in the Garou tongue.<br /> <br /> Man\u2019s Skin: Ugh. Seriously, whoever stuck this in the Black Fury gifts deserves to be drawn and quartered. This gift is now called \u201cGender Swap,\u201d and it is a Ragabash gift, NOT a Black Fury gift.<br /> <br /> Aura of Confidence: The effects of this gift can be suppressed for a scene by spending a Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Camouflage: The effects of this gift can be suppressed at will.<br /> <br /> And here are two \u201cnew\u201d level one gifts:<br /> <br /> Sense Weaver: This gift functions exactly as Sense Wyrm, except that it detects emanations of the Weaver. It is considered \u201cIn Breed/Auspice/Tribe\u201d for Homids, Theurges and Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> Sense Wyld: This gift functions exactly as Sense Wyrm, except that it detects emanations of the Wyld. It is considered \u201cIn Breed/Auspice/Tribe\u201d for Lupus, Theurges, Black Furies and Red Talons.<br /> <br /> Gifts from other sources may be acceptable; just run them by me first. Some may require some tweaking for balance.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I\u2019m not going to house rule individual rites at this time, except for one: the Rite of Talisman Dedication does not exist. In brief, when it is dramatically appropriate for a werewolf to shred clothing and such when shifting forms, it will happen. When it is not dramatically appropriate for a werewolf to shred clothing and such when shifting forms, it will not happen. I can\u2019t be bothered to keep track of what is and is not dedicated, and since the number of dedicated objects is limited, your characters would all start to smell pretty bad wearing the same underwear every day.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Rank &amp; Renown</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">All characters will start at Rank 1, with the appropriate permanent renown for their Auspice. Ragabash may assign their three dots of starting renown at will.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Step Five: Finishing Touches</u><br /> <br /> Nature/Demeanor<br /> <br /> We will be using the optional Nature/Demeanor rules. I am definitely open to custom natures and demeanors, or natures and demeanors from other sources, within reason.<br /> <br /> Tribal Weaknesses<br /> <br /> We will not be using tribal weaknesses. However, if you want to choose a flaw, or create a custom flaw, that reflects your traditional tribal weakness, I am totally open to that.<br /> <br /> Metis Deformities<br /> <br /> Besides those listed in the various books, I am absolutely open to designing with you custom deformities for metis characters.<br /> <br /> Rage<br /> <br /> Starting Rage is based on Auspice. There is no limit to how high a character may raise their Rage with freebies, but remember that high Rage can have unfortunate consequences.<br /> <br /> Willpower<br /> <br /> Starting Willpower is based on Tribe. Willpower may not be raised higher than 8 at character creation through the use of freebie points under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> Gnosis<br /> <br /> Starting Gnosis is based on Breed. Gnosis may not be raised higher than 8 at character creation through the use of freebie points under any circumstances.he more powerful the totem will be. The totem will be chosen after the rite of passage. Unlike other bacific rites.<br /> l to the<br /> <br /> Freebie Points<br /> <br /> Freebie points may be spent as per the costs on the chart, subject to restrictions noted in the sections above.<br /> <br /> <u>Merits &amp; Flaws</u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Characters may purchase as many merits as they can afford, subject to ST approval. Characters may only take up to 7 points worth of flaws, receiving additional freebie points for them as usual. Merits and flaws from other sources (especially tribebooks and Rage Across the Heavens) may be acceptable with my approval, though some may need to be tweaked for balance (especially the ones from tribebooks and Rage Across the Heavens).<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t be afraid to work with me on custom merits and flaws.<br /> <br /> Remember, all flaws MUST BE ROLEPLAYED. I will enforce this requirement strictly, so do not choose a flaw simply for the points, expecting me to ignore it. You have been warned.<br /> <br /> The following Merits and Flaws from W20 have relevant house rules:<br /> <br /> Common Sense: This merit is not in use.<br /> <br /> Calm Heart: The increased difficulty only involves rage rolls to specifically determine whether a character enters frenzy. Intentional rage rolls, such as to activate gifts or to survive incapacitating wounds, are not affected. This means that rage rolls from those sources may cause frenzy normally, despite a calm heart.<br /> <br /> Untamable: This merit costs 7 points.<br /> <br /> Nightmares: Seriously, you\u2019re going to roll every time you wake up. I will enforce it.<br /> <br /> Driving Goal: I am very careful with this one, as it can easily derail a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Dark Secret: Obviously, the nature of the Dark Secret is one of those things that we should discuss in PM.<br /> <br /> Mark of the Predator: A garou with this flaw may not take the gift \u201cSmell of Man.\u201d They may take \u201cBeast Speech,\u201d but I\u2019m not sure why they\u2019d want to. Other gifts that affect animal behavior will be evaluated on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> Dark Fate: This flaw is not being used. Remember, I intend to run this game straight through to the Apocalypse. The entire world has a Dark Fate in store. ;-)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:25:37-07:00","id":288763,"title":"","content":"<u>Hannah Dawnstar (Mark, AKA MrMarkers)<br /> <br /> <br /> Scott Caldwell, &quot;Bridge-Between-the-People&quot; (James, AKA DeathmatchFM)<br /> <br /> <br /> Narasimha-Vallabha (Josh, AKA Al-Haleem)<br /> <br /> <br /> Geoff Bolen (Flo, AKA Evilmarmelade)<br /> <br /> <br /> Stir of Echoes (Eve, AKA Stir of Echoes)<br /> <br /> <br /> Jon Blaszczyk (Bashir, AKA Rall Bashir)<br /> <br /> <br /> Character Sheet Template<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Name: </div></div> </div> </div></u><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Player:</u> [Screen Name is sufficient, but feel free to put your first name if you care to share. I\u2019m Jim.]<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> <u>Breed:</u><br /> <u>Auspice:</u><br /> <u>Tribe:</u><br /> <u>Camp:</u> [If any]<br /> <u>Sept:</u><br /> <u>Pack Name:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <u>Pack Totem:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <br /> <u>Nature:</u><br /> <u>Demeanor:</u><br /> <u>Concept:</u> [Optional]<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: [Record attributes and abilities with a numeral, not a series of dots]<br /> Dexterity: [If there is a specialty, include it after the relevant numeral in parentheses]<br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> Manipulation:<br /> Appearance:<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> Intelligence:<br /> Wits:<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u> [Feel free to add Hobbies/Professional Skills/Expert Knowledges to each category.]<br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness:<br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Empathy:<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Leadership:<br /> Primal-Urge:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law:<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult:<br /> Rituals:<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u> [Just names and numbers here; details go below.]<br /> _____:<br /> _____:<br /> Totem:<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u> [If not Metis, please write \u201cN/A\u201d]<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> X (X) [Permanent, then temporary in parentheses, which will be the same at the start]<br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> X (X)<br /> <u>Willpower:</u> X (X)<br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Rank:</u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Name (Type; Level; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Name (Type; Level; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> [Any background that requires an explanation, such as the identity of an Ally or the nature of a Fetish, should have a listing here.]<br /> <br /> <u>Age:</u><br /> <u>Apparent Age:</u> [For Metis and Lupus, it will be the age your homid form appears.]<br /> <u>Sign:</u> [For Garou Astrology. If you\u2019re unfamiliar, leave blank for now.]<br /> <u>Race:</u> [Racial phenotype of the character\u2019s homid form. Use whatever descriptor you like.]<br /> <u>Sex:</u> [By which I mean their anatomy]<br /> <u>Gender:</u> [Use whatever descriptor you like, or leave blank if you prefer]<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> [Use whatever descriptor you like, or leave blank if you prefer]<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u><br /> <u>Fur Color:</u> [Obviously this applies to Crinos, Hispo and Lupus forms]<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u><br /> <u>Height:</u> [Homid form]<br /> <u>Weight:</u> [Homid form]<br /> <u>Build:</u> [Whatever descriptor you like, just a one or two word blurb to help us envision.]<br /> <u>Distinctive Features:</u> [Any particular features useful in identifying your character, be they visual, auditory or olfactory.]<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> [Give a general description of your character\u2019s appearance in Homid, Crinos and Lupus forms. If you\u2019re feeling especially industrious, you can do so for Glabro and Hispo as well. For homid form, include a brief description of the clothing that the character is most often wearing.]<br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u><br /> [Any particular or distinctive equipment that your character owns that you want to record. The make, model and color of her car, for example, or her heirloom pocket watch. Bear in mind the resources rating and be reasonable. Remember, this is not D&amp;D- not every piece of equipment needs to be accounted for. Unless you really, REALLY want to be sure your character has that 10 foot pole and 50 ft of hemp rope.]<br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> [Just a few sentences of summation of what the character is like, on the level of personal interactions. If you were this character\u2019s friend, and had to describe what she is like to someone who had never met her, what would you say?]<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u><br /> [The character\u2019s history and backstory, in your own words. Most of this will be what we discussed in the recruitment thread, but here is the chance to fill in some blanks and put it all in one place, for easier reference for all of us.]<br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u><br /> [Any notes you want to jot down about your character to have readily available for easy reference. Names of family members living or dead, particular goals, aspirations or fears, etc.]<br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u><br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Experience Details</u><br /> [This space is for me to record the details of experience granted and spent, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 11-13-2014, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:27:38-07:00","id":288767,"title":"","content":"And now we can get down to the mechanical nitty gritty. :-) Sorry about all the delays, guys, but now we're ready to begin in earnest. Let's try to keep all future conversation here, and save the old recruitment thread for any further recruitment we might try to do, should we see a need further down the line. :-)<br /> <br /> I'm going to take a nap now; I'm beat. What was I thinking, vowing not to sleep until I got this done? ;-) You guys are a bad influence on me. :-P<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T22:59:43-07:00","id":289277,"title":"","content":"Name: Hannah Dawnstar<br /> Player: MrMarkers, Mark<br /> Chronicle: Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> Breed: Homid<br /> Auspice: Ahroun<br /> Tribe: Silver Fangs<br /> Camp: House Wyrmfoe; Sun Lodge<br /> Sept: Sept of the New World's Glory<br /> Pack Name:<br /> Pack Totem:<br /> <br /> Nature: Thrill-Seeker<br /> Demeanor: Alpha<br /> Concept: Queen Bitch turned Garou<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Strength: 3<br /> Dexterity: 4 (Preternatural Grace)<br /> Stamina: 3<br /> <br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 2<br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 2<br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> Talents<br /> Alertness: 1<br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation: 1<br /> Leadership: 3<br /> Primal-Urge:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive: 1<br /> Etiquette: 1<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee: 1<br /> Performance: 3 (Dance)<br /> Stealth: 1<br /> Survival: 1<br /> Professional Skill: Cooking: 1<br /> <br /> Knowledges<br /> Academics: 1 (History)<br /> Computer: 1<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law: 1<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 1<br /> Rituals: 1<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> Backgrounds<br /> Pure Breed: 5<br /> Resources: 2<br /> Allies: 2<br /> Ancestors: 3<br /> Totem: 1<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Persuasion (Homid; Level 1; W20 pg 153)<br /> Inspiration (Ahroun; Level 1; W20 pg 171)<br /> Sense Wyrm (Silver Fangs; Level 1; W20 pg 156)<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> Metis Deformity: N/A<br /> <br /> Rage: 5 (5)<br /> Gnosis: 2 (2)<br /> Willpower: 7 (7)<br /> <br /> Renown<br /> Glory<br /> Permanent: 2<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Honor<br /> Permanent: 1<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Wisdom<br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Rank: 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Double-Jointed (Physical; 1; W20 pg 472)<br /> Perfect Balance (Physical; 1; W20 pg 472)<br /> Natural Leader (Social; 2; W20 pg 480)<br /> Notable Heritage (Social; 2; W20 pg 480)<br /> Ancestor Ally (Supernatural; 1; W20 pg 482)<br /> <br /> Flaws<br /> Nightmares (Mental; 1; W20 pg 477)<br /> Overconfident (Mental; 1; W20 pg 477)<br /> Foe From the Past (Supernatural; 3; W20 pg 484)<br /> Dark Secret (Social; 1; W20 pg 480)<br /> Compulsion (Mental; 1; PgtG pg 164)<br /> <br /> Background Descriptions<br /> <br /> Double-Jointed &amp; Perfect Balance<br /> Hannah is a classicly trained Gymnast, and has been doing Cheerleading since she was a small Child<br /> <br /> Natural Leader, &amp; Notable Heritage<br /> Hannah is a born leader, and palpably regal, especially considering her impecable breeding. &quot;Heavy rests the crown,&quot; or so they say, and as a Dawnstar, she knows she has a lot of responsiblity, but being around her makes her seem like maybe, just maybe she can pull it off.<br /> <br /> Ancestor Ally<br /> Isaiah Morningkill; the Cowboy that haunts Hannah's dreams. He's always guided her, and she looks to him for Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Nightmares<br /> Hannah isn't naive, and knows that the expectations on her are massive, unfair even. She knows that the Vampires hate her family. And she knows she's eaten people before. These thoughts plague her mind, awake she can shut them out, asleep she runs from them in terror.<br /> <br /> Foe From the Past<br /> The Warlord, the Sabbat, nuff said<br /> <br /> Dark Secret:<br /> Durring her first change Hannah ate the flesh of man. While a small circle of Silver Fangs, and one kinfolk outside of the Tribe know, the story has been flatly denied, and suppressed by the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> Compulsion &amp; Overconfident:<br /> Hannah sometimes has borderline delusions of granduer, if not full blown delusions of granduer. Maybe she has that bad Fang blood, maybe it's the Cowboy guiding her, but she does not back down easy. She simply can't help but brag about what she has accomplished, and has a hard time being humble, especially when she thinks shes right.<br /> <br /> Allies &amp; Resources<br /> The Dawnstar Family especially her mother and father, support her. She has ample money, and through her father excellent legal representation if she needs it. On top of a few kinfolk who will always be happy to pitch in and help her out. Most notably of any real influence, cousin Charles resident physician in the Department of Emergency Medicine at Cooper Hospital in Camden. Whom she's always seen as a older brother figure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Age: 16<br /> Apparent Age: 16<br /> Sign: Hyperion<br /> Race: Caucasian<br /> Sex: Female<br /> Gender: Female<br /> Sexuality: Bisexual<br /> Hair Color: Ash Blond, almost Silvery<br /> Fur Color: Silvery White<br /> Eye Color: Ice Blue<br /> Height: 5' 2''<br /> Weight: 105 lbs<br /> Build: Athletic and Slender, a Gymnast's Physique<br /> Distinctive Features: Confidence, Blond Silvery Hair.<br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> Hannah is a small girl, slender and athletic, but what she lacks in raw size is made up for in a confidence that's palpable, and a suprising ammount of toned lean muscle. She has ice blue eyes; long blond, near silver hair that falls to the small of her back; and angular royal features. A small sleek nose, full ruby lips, and a strong jawline. Her youth downplays raw allure somewhat, but she is obviously going to break a lot of hearts somday. She moves with extreme grace, and practiced poise. She is by no means meek, and tends to stand out in a crowd.<br /> <br /> On any given day she tends to wear blue jeans, and a fashionable top, with stylish but practical shoes. On those days she tends to put her hair into a simple ponytail, with minimal makeup. She almost always wears a few rings, a gold locket, and simple stud earrings. Sometimes she'll wear a sundress if the weather is nice enough, something with soft colors, and floral patterns, when she does wear a dress she tends to tease her hair into ringlets and let it cascade down her back untamed. If she is training or planning on a fight, she tends to wear yoga pants, and a sports bra with a windbreaker jacket, or occasionally wears her old cheerleading outfit, which she's used to moving in.<br /> <br /> In lupus form she is a lean white, almost silver wolf. Every part of her coat is full and well care for. Even her teeth appear bone white and perfect. Her eyes are still a haunting ice blue, and she has strong powerful paws. She retains her natural grace, and easy stride, but when she moves you can almost see the toned muscles moving under her beautiful fur.<br /> <br /> In Chrinos, Hannah's silver white fur is shorter than most Garou, which inadvertantly shows off the way her muscles ripple under it while she moves, if you ever doubted just how strong and athletic she is, it becomes shockingly evident. This contrasts with her long hair, which now falls wildly in ringlets all around her, giving her a silver mane. She stands nearly 8 foot tall, and has a beautiful unblemished coat, perfect white teeth and long claws, and serious ice blue eyes, that seem at once both too clever and too deadly. While she maintains her natural poise and grace she seems to impact the world more than the way she breezes through it in her other forms.<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> 2013 powder blue Honda Prius<br /> Fencing Gear stored in the trunk of her car<br /> A purse full of makeup and miscellaneous<br /> Iphone 5<br /> Macbook Air<br /> Mace on her keyring<br /> <br /> Personality<br /> Hannah has a strong personality that is very confident, but can also be seen as arrogant. Despite this, she is generally good natured, but can be a bit selfish and hedonistic. To be blatant, if you don't know her, she comes off as a spoiled bitch. If you do, she is spoiled, and a bitch, but she generally cares about her friends and family.<br /> <br /> Character History<br /> Hannah Dawnstar, born to a line of heroes even she's not sure she can live up to. Spoiled, rich, and arrogant. Completely not ready to be a Warrior of Gaia. But she has to be. The only Surviving Garou Grandchild of Dark-Eye Drawnstar. Heir to the Sept of the New World's Glory, possibly the Silver Crown itself, even if she doesn't know it, she feels it somewhere in her heart. She never wanted any of this, she still doesn't, but some part of her knows in a sideways sense that it is what she deserves.<br /> <br /> While not a perfect personality to be a Warrior of Gaia, she is in ways more prepared than some for her first change. She spent years being honed into an athlete and a gymnast. She spent years being an alpha to a pack of teenage girls. She made people see her way. She has always been a leader, and she has always been a fighter, but is that enough? Does any of that matter when you've eaten people, when you've already disappointing so many around you?<br /> <br /> Maybe the only way for Hannah Dawnstar to be what she was meant to, is to be reforged, to be something new. Or maybe she's been what she's needed to be the whole time.<br /> <br /> (The rest of the details are in the original thread.)<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> <br /> Family Tree<br /> <br /> Grandfather - High Lord William Dawnstar<br /> Grandmother - Lady Annabelle Dawnstar<br /> <br /> Mother - Leslie Dawnstar<br /> Father - Joseph Dawnstar (took wife's last name, orignal last name Speelman)<br /> <br /> Aunts and Uncles (all deceased)<br /> William - Ahroun<br /> Anne - Theurge<br /> Bradley - Ragabash<br /> <br /> Cousins -<br /> Charles, alive, resident physician in the Department of Emergency Medicine at Cooper Hospital in Camden.<br /> <br /> Goals<br /> Become an accepted member of the Tribe and Sept<br /> Get back Dawns's Pride<br /> <br /> Renown Details<br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> Experience<br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> Experience Details<br /> [This space is for me to record the details of experience granted and spent, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> Freebies Spent:<br /> 2 on Resources<br /> 2 on Allies<br /> 3 on Ancestors<br /> 1 on Totem<br /> 1 on Merits after Flaws are Subtracted<br /> 2 on Gnosis<br /> 4 on Willpower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 11-06-2014, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T08:17:41-07:00","id":289611,"title":"","content":"Complete. Updated as of 11/17<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Name:</u> Scott Cadwell, &quot;Bridge-Between-the-People&quot;<br /> <u>Player:</u> James W.<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> <u>Breed:</u> Homid<br /> <u>Auspice:</u> Galliard<br /> <u>Tribe:</u> Stargazers<br /> <u>Sept:</u><br /> <u>Pack Name:</u><br /> <u>Pack Totem:</u><br /> <br /> <u>Nature:</u> Caregiver<br /> <u>Demeanor:</u> Idealist<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Spiritual Mediator<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 4 (encouraging)<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 3<br /> Intelligence: 3<br /> Wits: 2<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u><br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness: 1<br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Empathy: 3<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation: 0<br /> Leadership: 0<br /> Primal-Urge: 3<br /> Streetwise: 0<br /> Subterfuge: 1<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken: 1<br /> Crafts: 0<br /> Drive: 0<br /> Etiquette: 1<br /> Firearms: 1<br /> Larceny: 0<br /> Melee: 0<br /> Performance: 2 (mantras)<br /> Stealth: 0<br /> Survival: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics: 1 (astrology)<br /> Computer: 1<br /> Enigmas: 2<br /> Investigation: 0<br /> Law: 0<br /> Medicine: 1<br /> Occult: 2<br /> Rituals: 1<br /> Science: 1 (biology)<br /> Technology: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u><br /> Allies 1 (kinfolk doctor)<br /> Mentor 3 (Threefold Path)<br /> Resources 1<br /> Rites: 1<br /> Totem: 1<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Master of Fire (Homid; Level 1; W20 pg 152)<br /> Perfect Recall (Galliard; Level 1; W20 pg 169)<br /> Channeling (Stargazer; Level 1; W20 pg 195)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> The Rite of Meeting (Accord; Level 1; Stargazers Tribebook pg 74)<br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u> N/A<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> 6/6<br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> 4/4<br /> <u>Willpower:</u> 6/6<br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent: 2<br /> Temporary: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent: 0<br /> Temporary: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent: 1<br /> Temporary: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Rank:</u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Berserker (Mental; 2; W20 pg 476)<br /> Calm Heart (Mental; 3; W20 pg 476)<br /> Language (x2) (Mental; 1; W20 pg 475)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Persistent Parents (Social; 2; W20 pg 481)<br /> Reluctant Warrior (Mental; 2; Rage Across the Heavens pg 127)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> <br /> Allies: Scott lost his job at the hospital as a nurse when he was convicted of killing and eating over a dozen pets. However, while the Stargazer Tribe may have very few Garou worldwide, and in the West especially, there are a stable number of kinfolk. One local kinfolk is a doctor with a private practice that is local, who Scott works for whenever he has the available time. She's generous with helping him out more than she would any other co-worker, and Scott feels bad to get the special treatment. The doctor is married with a daughter in high school who she hopes Scott would consider as a marriage partner someday.<br /> <br /> Mentor: Scott was trained by Threefold Path, one of the most influential members of the Stargazers in the West, and who is considered to be the face of the Stargazers to many communities. While Threefold Path qualifies for the highest level of Mentor, he has left for a deep part of the spirit world on a mystic quest from which he will never return. However, many of his teachings for Scott were designed to make sense with age and experience, and Scott still meditates on the lessons he received. He also does experience dreams sometimes that feel like they guide him, though whether that is actually Threefold Path's current doing, or more training meant to blossom at a later time, Scott does not know. This Background represents the seeds for great knowledge that Threefold Path granted, as well as his inaccessibility and the cryptic and vague nature of his teachings.<br /> <br /> Resources: Scott has a little apartment that's in an okay neighborhood. He doesn't have a lot of space cash as he isn't able to regularly work at the clinic, but he does at least make enough to support himself. Scott usually doesn't spend much money, since he saves in the event that he'll have to go away for a long period of time and not be able to work. Hopefully, he should be able to still cover his rent so his scarce few possessions are where he left them when he gets back.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed: The Stormlords are a family that has carefully monitored breeding for centuries, inbreeding to create strengths and introducing new blood when necessary. In addition, there are many great heroes in Scott's bloodline, and the Stormlords earned respect from many fellow tribes with their bravery. Were Scott a member of the Silver Fangs, he would have Pure Breed 4. However, due to his abandonment of his family's tribe, he has no Pure Breed at all.<br /> <br /> Berserker: While Scott usually seems calm, he represses a lot of anger and resentment, which has only intensified after his First Change. He's non-confrontational and abhors violence, but would be able to just release the built up tension if he so desired. This Merit lets Scott enter berserk frenzy with no need for a roll.<br /> <br /> Calm Heart: Scott is naturally pretty calm and relaxed, and is in good control of his emotions. He also meditates regularly on Threefold Path's teachings. More so, he has great self-control and despite all of the fury that is inside of him, he fights hard each day to keep it from surfacing. This Merit increases the difficulty of rage rolls by two for the purposes of involuntarily entering frenzy. The penalty doesn't apply for intentional applications of rage.<br /> <br /> Persistent Parents: The Stormlords want Scott back. They always need more Garou, and see Scott deciding not to return as an insult to their decision to send him away to learn skills to help his family. Perhaps even worse is the embarrassment the Stormlords feel, that one of a proud and strong bloodline would choose to join a strange and dying tribe such as the Stargazers. Scott also has a mate chosen by the family back in West Virginia who did not accept his engagement to another woman or his refusal to return. While distance keeps the Stormlord werewolves from being able to directly interfere, his family will do whatever they can to rip him away from his life in the Delaware Valley and return him home.<br /> <br /> Reluctant Warrior: Scott is not a violent person and has terrible memories of what he did to the dogs during his First Change. Scott seeks diplomatic solutions and has a different idea of glory and honor than the sort which involves conflict. While Scott is perfectly willing to fight to protect himself or those he loves, he can't bring himself to initiate violence.<br /> <br /> Language: While Scott isn't the greatest speaker, he does know both modern Mandarin and Hindi. He practices up on the languages when he has the time, with many old books given to him by Threefold Path laying around his apartment dedicated to the languages, so he can better serve as a bridge between people.<br /> <br /> <u>Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Apparent Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Sign:</u> Lu-Bat<br /> <u>Race:</u> Caucasian<br /> <u>Sex:</u> Male<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Masculine<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> Celibate<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u> Blonde<br /> <u>Fur Color:</u> White<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Blue<br /> <u>Height:</u> 5'6&quot;<br /> <u>Weight:</u> 140<br /> <u>Build:</u> Thin<br /> <u>Distinctive Features:</u> Cross tattoo on chest<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> Scott is a thin young man with blonde hair and soft features. He dresses casually, and while he has an attractive boyish look, there is little distinctive about him. Scott's Lupus form is more unusual, being a wolf with blonde fur. His fur remains the same color in his Crimos shape, though it is marked with white streaks reminiscent of lightning. <a href=\"http://i59.tinypic.com/24l52di.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Homid</a> <a href=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/289h4c2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Lupus</a><br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u><br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> Having been raised in a rather secluded environment, Scott's first few years in the world left him feeling awkward and unable to fit in. He's adopted a number of shy traits, and rarely opens up to individuals. Scott is a caring individual who wants to help others, though he is susceptible to loneliness and often lacks initiative in relationships with others.<br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u><br /> Blank<br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Experience Details</u><br /> Bonus Points<br /> -Berserker (2pts)<br /> -Calm Heart (3pts)<br /> -Reluctant Warrior (-2pts)<br /> -Persistent Parents (-2pts)<br /> -Rites 0 to 1 (1pt)<br /> -Language (mandarin) (1pt)<br /> -Language (hindi) (1pt)<br /> -Rage 4 to 6 (2pts)<br /> -Willpower 4 to 6 (2pts)<br /> -Gnosis 1 to 4 (6pts)<br /> -Resources 0 to 1 (1pt)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Character History<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Scott was born to a powerful family of Silver Fangs called the Stormlords in West Virginia. He grew up on a farm with a very large family, with many sisters, cousins, mothers, and aunts. Scott had fewer male relatives for some reason, and didn't fit in well with other boys while he was younger. Scott did not grow up meeting anyone outside of his family, and was home schooled.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fang pack his family was centered around didn't see much potential in Scott due to his lack of aggression. But he was smart and had nurturing tendencies, so they agreed to send him to school to learn some skills that could be useful for the family. Scott traveled to Pennsylvania to attend nursing school when he was just sixteen, and graduated by eighteen.<br /> <br /> City life was a large shock to Scott, and the outside world he had only seen glimpses of became very real. Even though his family prepared him before he left, the trip was a culture shock. The Stormlords did contact the local Silver Fangs to keep an eye out on Scott, but he kept out of trouble. The only problem was that Scott found himself a girlfriend, a kind and sweet girl who found his naivety endearing.<br /> <br /> The girlfriend, whose name was Lindsey, was not well received when reported back to the Stormlords by the local Silver Fangs, as Scott had already had a mate lined up for him that fit with their careful family planning. But it wasn't too much of a concern until Scott and Lindsey got engaged, and Scott called his father to let him know that he would not be coming home.<br /> <br /> Scott started work as a nurse and life seemed to be moving in a better direction. He started to make a bit of money, was in love with a girl, and had friends. It ended when Lindsey died walking home, torn apart by &quot;wild dogs&quot; on the streets of Philadelphia. Scott sank into a deep depression. Scott bankrupt himself paying for Lindsey's funeral expenses and burial as she had no family of her own, and only had his friends to lean on for support.<br /> <br /> But that changed as well, and so did Scott. While he and his friends were working at a dog boarding home for people on vacation, Scott was left with the pets while his friends went to get coffee. Their barking and the noises they made drove him into a range, and Scott experienced his First Change, proceeding to rip every last animal apart and eat what bits of them was left. Scott's friends returned to find him naked and covered in blood. Scott was sued by various pet owners, abandoned by his friends for his monstrous actions, and had charges pressed against him for multiple counts of wrongful death of animals.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, it was during this time that Threefold Path, a wise Stargazer, found Scott, having been lead back to Philadelphia after a long absence. He was lead by the stars to find his final protege, the one he would leave his connection and entrust his will to. With connections to Stargazer kin, Scott's upstanding financial charges and legal issues were resolved, and Scott went on an adventure with Threefold Path overseas, to the Appalachian Mountains, then to China and India, and finally into the spirit world itself. All the while Scott learned more of the world he was now a part of, and what would come in the future.<br /> <br /> Scott works now for a Stargazer kinfolk doctor when he has the time, and who understands his erratic schedule and helps make life easier. Bills are still hard for Scott since he can't work much at all and has dedicated most of his time to learning what it means to be Garou and Stargazer. Threefold Path is soon to leave to the deepest parts of the spirit world where he will never return, and Scott will be a member of a pack. During his trip he avoided any backlash from his family, but now that he know there are other Silver Fangs he realizes it is a possibility. He's anxious to meet his new pack, and is unsure if he will be able to live up to the great expectations that Threefold Path has for him.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> -Scott's last name was changed from &quot;Cavendish&quot; to &quot;Cadwell&quot;. Now he's not named after a banana<br /> -He is now known as &quot;Bridge-Between-the-People&quot;, which could refer to just the Garou Nation, or perhaps all of Gaia's children. Scott isn't even sure.<br /> -Character History was updated to reflect the change from Children of Gaia to &quot;Scottgazer&quot;.<br /> -Scott's physical attributes are now puny.<br /> -Scott is no longer a struggling amateur author. He's a spirit guru-hippie.<br /> -All references to the make-believe tribe &quot;Silver Claws&quot; have been changed appropriately to &quot;Silver Fangs&quot;. Oops.<br /> -Scott's Gifts are updated. Now it's one Homid, one Galliard, one Stargazer.<br /> -Scott's Academics specialty changed from literature to astrology.<br /> -Updated appearance and personality. Spots left blank I don't have anything significant to mention.<br /> -Took &quot;Reluctant Warrior&quot; as a Mental Flaw (originally it was Zodiac).<br /> -Changed Scott's Homid Gift to &quot;Master of Fire&quot;.<br /> -Scott now has an astrological sign. He's also celibate. Maybe he hasn't met the right person yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3789,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","user":"DeathmatchFM","date":". 11-17-2014, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T07:16:27-07:00","id":290482,"title":"","content":"<u>Name</u>: Val (Narasimha-Vallabha)<br /> <u>Player</u>: Josh<br /> <u>Chronicle</u>: Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <u>Breed</u>: Homid<br /> <u>Auspice</u>: Ragabash<br /> <u>Tribe</u>: Get of Fenris<br /> <u>Camp</u>: Vrikodara Jata<br /> <u>Sept</u>: Sept of Friends<br /> <u>Pack Name</u>:<br /> <u>Pack Totem</u>:<br /> <br /> <u>Nature</u>: Seeker<br /> <u>Demeanour</u>: Contrary<br /> <u>Concept</u>: The Heretic<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Manipulation: 4 (Elaborate Lies)<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 2<br /> Intelligence: 3<br /> Wits: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u><br /> <br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness: 2<br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Empathy: 3<br /> Expression: 3 (Rhetoric)<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Leadership:<br /> Primal-Urge: 2<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Melee: 1<br /> Performance:<br /> Stealth: 2<br /> Survival: 1<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics: 3 (Indian philosophy)<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas: 2<br /> Investigation: 2<br /> Law:<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 2<br /> Rituals:<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u>:<br /> Ancestors: 3<br /> Contacts: 1<br /> Mentor: 2<br /> Pure Breed: 3<br /> Totem: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Persuasion (Homid; Level 1; W20; pg 153)<br /> Blur of the Milky Eye (Ragabash; Level 1; W20; pg 161)<br /> Visage of Fenris (Get of Fenris; Level 1; W20; pg 180)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity</u>: N/A<br /> <br /> <u>Rage</u>: 2 (2)<br /> <u>Gnosis</u>: 3 (3)<br /> <u>Willpower</u>: 6 (6)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent: 1<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent: 2<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Rank</u>: 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Language x 2 (Mental; 1; W20; pg 475)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Exclusive Ancestor (Supernatural; 1; Custom)<br /> Twisted Upbringing (Social; 1; W20; pg 481)<br /> Intolerance (Mental; 1; W20; pg 477)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Background Description</u><br /> <br /> Ancestors: This should really read <i>Ancestor</i>, as despite Val\u2019s efforts, he can\u2019t contact any of his famed antecedents. The only one who offers him any attention is Vashti, who has an almost obsessive interest in his development. Val can\u2019t be sure if Vashti is simply a figment of his imagination or an <i>actual</i> ancestor. Or worse, not a werewolf at all, but rather something\u2026<i>else</i>.<br /> <br /> Contact: Karl Wavecleaver, Get of Fenris, Germantown Volunteers Sept, Theurge<br /> <br /> Mentor: Sunchaser, Children of Gaia, Sept of Friends, Rank 3 Philodox<br /> <br /> Pure Breed: Although Val\u2019s not entirely aware of it, he\u2019s descended from renowned warriors. Whether he can live up to his glorious ancestors is another matter entirely. Dehazku saw something in him that\u2019s for certain.<br /> <br /> Language: Val\u2019s interest in his heritage led him to learning the ancient language of Indian scholarship, Sanskrit. Thanks to his mother (and a steady supply of Bollywood) he\u2019s also proficient in Hindi.<br /> <br /> Exclusive Ancestor: Not long after Malakai attempted his strange ritual to welcome Val into the Wyrm\u2019s embrace, he began having\u2026dreams. At least he thinks they\u2019re dreams. In them, a battle-arrayed woman appears. She calls herself Vashti, and claims to be an ancient warrior, whose glorious deeds are recounted in the <i>Vrikasya Prasvapah Sutra</i>, a text Val has never heard of. Vashti urges Val not to trust the Fenrir, who she curses as the \u2018Great Betrayers\u2019. Furthermore, she\u2019s eager to teach him Jata philosophy, the \u2018True Path\u2019, in the hopes that he\u2019ll use his knowledge to \u2018Awaken the World-Bearer\u2019 whatever the hell <i>that</i> means. Although Val wants to believe Vashti is just the product of his disordered mind, he fears she might not only be real, but highly dangerous.<br /> <br /> Twisted Upbringing: Val\u2019s had just about enough of crackpot philosophies. First from Dehazku, then Malakai and Sunchaser, and now from some over-built Aryan bastard who smells\u2026Unusual. Anything could be true, or nothing. But Val will be damned before he blindly prostates himself before Gaia and dedicates himself to the Wyld. And who approves these spellings anyway? Just another reason not to take anything seriously.<br /> <br /> Intolerance: Val <i>really</i> hates absolutes. Everytime someone says, \u2018it is so\u2019, some primal part of him just wants to rip their sanctimonious face off. Val refuses to commit wholesale to any belief, and responds aggressively to all attempts to force a world-view on him. He regards it as a mental straitjacket, which he won\u2019t just shrug off, but tear apart.<br /> <br /> <u>Age</u>: 17<br /> <u>Apparent</u> age: 20<br /> <u>Sign</u>: Meros<br /> <u>Race</u>: Indian<br /> <u>Sex</u>: Male<br /> <u>Gender</u>: Male<br /> <u>Sexuality</u>: Homosexual<br /> <u>Hair Colour</u>: Black<br /> <u>Fur Colour</u>: Grey, but the mane is brindled with black.<br /> <u>Eye Colour</u>: Hazel<br /> <u>Height</u>: 6\u2019 2\u201d<br /> <u>Weight</u>: 150 lbs<br /> <u>Build</u>: Tall and slender<br /> <u>Distinctive Features</u>: Lips quirked in a permanent half-smile (or smirk), prefers to slouch rather than stand straight.<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u>: Val\u2019s skin is light brown. He keeps his hair cropped short and he rarely bothers to shave; his face is usually covered in a scruffy-half beard that makes him look both older and homeless, which is technically true. Val would be fairly intimidating, if he packed on another 40 pounds of muscle, his height alone allows him to stand out. He has a lean, hungry look, which puts one in mind of a feral animal caged against its will. If he bothered with personal hygiene, he\u2019d be quite handsome, and despite his best efforts, he can still turn heads. Val\u2019s eyes are always moving, absorbing his surroundings, and he\u2019ll disarm any awkward encounters with a brilliant smile and a chuckle.<br /> <br /> Val prefers to wear a knee-length kurta, both to showcase pride in his Indian heritage and because it\u2019s pretty darn comfy. With this, he dons a pair of faded, long-suffering jeans and ragged sandals. He also hangs an amulet around his neck, which he claims is a family heirloom. It never leaves his sight. When paired with his untamed facial hair, his apparel gives the impression of a guru in training, or a <i>very</i> lost sadhu.<br /> <br /> In lupus form, Val\u2019s sleek fur is the grey of storm-heavy clouds, save for his mane, which is spotted with black. His eyes are the colour of dark honey, and his wiry body is built for speed rather than raw strength.<br /> <br /> In Crinos, Val is a bit of an embarrassment by Fenrir standards. His limbs are long and graceful, tightly coiled with muscle, but far from bulging. His tail is thick and lustrous, and his fur practically luminous. His mane is shaggy, mirroring his ill-maintained facial hair in homid. Only in this form does Val stand straight, with impressive results. His taloned fingers are slender and sensitive, not ideal for rending flesh, but incredibly dextrous. As for his eyes, they seem to glow with an inner fire, like cooling embers. If there were Crinos beauty contests, Val could definitely compete. As it is though, most Fenrir are likely to regard him as a preening pretty boy; barely worthy of his fangs.<br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u>:<br /> <br /> A battered copy of the <i>Bhagavad Gita</i>.<br /> <br /> An antique amulet. Val likes to believe it\u2019s gold, but it\u2019s probably some sort of copper alloy.<br /> <br /> Some smart phone, Val keeps getting the brand confused.<br /> <br /> A tacky bead bracelet given to him by Sunchaser as \u2018a mark of friendship\u2019. The sentiment\u2019s a tad precious for Val, but he wears it anyway.<br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u>: Val has a rather complex personality. Owing to his dislike of absolutes, he\u2019s very accepting. In fact, he\u2019s so broadminded; he could probably tie his brain under his chin. His non-judgemental nature means he\u2019s easy to get along with, and he takes life in its stride. He likes making people smile, and hates all things serious. If he can laugh about it, he will, no matter how tragic his circumstances might be. However, when it comes to the higher realms of philosophy, Val can get downright vicious. He refuses to be told what to do, and instinctively rebels against authority. He\u2019ll work in a team, but won\u2019t be ordered around, and he\u2019ll listen to your thoughts, but won\u2019t buy into them. All things considered, he\u2019s a great drinking buddy, but any deeper<br /> relationship would require more work than the average person would be willing to invest.<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u>: Oh shit, what the hell have I gotten myself into? That about sums up Val\u2019s thoughts on his new existence. Drawn into a bizarre world by Dehazku, an elder Garou masquerading as a caring relative, Val\u2019s discovery of his lycanthropic heritage was most definitely <i>not</i> what he wanted. On the run from a quasi-Hindu cult of werewolves (You can\u2019t make this stuff up!) Val finds himself far from home, surrounded by strangers. And then it all goes to hell. In Delaware, he meets Malakai, who, apart from the surreal philosophy is damn good-looking.<br /> <br /> Pity he was also into that cult bullshit. Fine, whatever. Val was quite happy to let Malakai complete his ritual and \u2018Dance the Black Spiral\u2019 (He\u2019s always liked dancing) when a bunch of mangy-flea biters crashed the party.<br /> <br /> And they had to <i>debate</i> whether they should kill him! What the hell? Haven\u2019t these assholes heard of human rights? Werewolves count as humans, don\u2019t they? Displaying a modicum of intelligence, they decided not to summarily execute him. Gee, thanks guys, you shouldn\u2019t have. But maybe death would\u2019ve been preferable, because now he\u2019s stuck with a pedantic hippy for a mentor. Worst of all, she doesn\u2019t have a sense of humour! And maybe it would\u2019ve been okay, except now, oh sweet Shiva, he\u2019s got some white supremacist trying to teach him <i>more</i> pseudo-spiritual mumbo jumbo. At least the guy\u2019s fun to look at, although Val would rather lose his tongue than admit it. But Val sure as hell isn\u2019t gonna serve \u2018Great\u2019 Fenris just because some musclehead tells him to. And if Great Fenris\u2019 got a problem with that, the bastard can say it to his face.<br /> <br /> If that wasn\u2019t enough to drive the average mortal into insanity\u2019s sweet embrace, there\u2019s Vashti. Good thing his conversational Sanskrit is up to scratch, or he wouldn\u2019t have a clue what the old battle axe was saying. She needn\u2019t worry; Val isn\u2019t planning to trust the Get, or anyone for that matter. Still, it\u2019s nice to have someone who isn\u2019t a glorified eco-terrorist to talk to\u2026Even if Vashti <i>is</i> just a symptom of his stress-addled mind.<br /> <br /> At least it can\u2019t get any worse\u2026Right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u>:<br /> <br /> Family: A veritable army of relatives scattered across India and beyond, but Val barely knows most of them. He cares only for his mother, Natasha. His father died of heart complications years ago. Dehazku claims to be a relative too, although Val doubts it.<br /> <br /> Greatest aspiration: To discover some great Truth behind his new existence, even if that truth is there is no truth at all.<br /> <br /> Greatest fear: To be found by Dehazku, and dragged into his twisted machinations. Val considers such a fate no better than slavery.<br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u>:<br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Experience Details</u>:<br /> <br /> Freebies Spent:<br /> 3 on Ancestors<br /> 1 on Contacts<br /> 3 on Totem<br /> 1 on Rage<br /> 4 on Gnosis<br /> 2 on Willpower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 12-31-2014, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:19:54-07:00","id":290840,"title":"","content":"<u>Name:</u> Geoff Bolen<br /> <u>Player:</u> Evilmarmelade (Or Florian. Call me Flo.)<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> <u>Breed:</u> Homid<br /> <u>Auspice:</u> Philodox<br /> <u>Tribe:</u> Children of Gaia<br /> <u>Camp:</u><br /> <u>Sept:</u> Marshall Island Sept<br /> <u>Pack Name:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <u>Pack Totem:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <br /> <u>Nature:</u> Visionary<br /> <u>Demeanor:</u> Caregiver<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Children Educator<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: 3<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 3<br /> <br /> Charisma: 4 (Reassuring)<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 2<br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 2<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u><br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness: 1<br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Empathy: 4 (Emotional State Reading)<br /> Expression: 2<br /> Intimidation: 1<br /> Leadership: 2<br /> Primal-Urge: 1<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts: 1 (Drawing)<br /> Drive: 1<br /> Etiquette: 2<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee: 1<br /> Performance: 1 (Guitar)<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics: 3 (Education)<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law: 2<br /> Medicine:1<br /> Occult:1<br /> Rituals: 2<br /> Science: 1 (Biology)<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u><br /> <br /> Mentor 1<br /> Ressource 1<br /> Kinfolk 1<br /> Totem 2<br /> Fetish 1 : Truth Earring (Lvl1; p222; Corebook)<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Persuasion (Homid; level 1; Core W20 p 153)<br /> Fangs of Judgement (Philodox; level 1; Core W20 p 166)<br /> Mother's Touch (Children of Gaia; level 1; Core W20 p 164-177)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u> [Nope. N/A. Nothing to see here.]<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> 3 (3)<br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> 3 (3)<br /> <u>Willpower:</u> 5 (5)<br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent: 3<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Rank:</u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Supporter (Mental, 2; Corebook p 480)<br /> Calm heart (Mental 3; Corebook, p 476)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Phobia : Cleithrophobia (Mental; 2; Corebook, 477)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> <b>Mentor </b><br /> Steve Bolen, aka Growl-In-The-Wind, Geoff's favorite and loudest uncle, even if he's a Fianna. He's the one who's teaching him how to fight properly. He lives near the Marshall Island Sept.<br /> <br /> <b>Kinfolk</b><br /> The Bolen family : Mark and Allison, the parents. They're scared of what may happen to their dear geoff, so they try to help him in the best way they can, so he can keep his focus on helping people. They try to show that they still love him, but in truth, they're also a little scared of their son.<br /> There's also Aaron, the little brother. He's feeling conflicted about his big bro : at first, he was healous of him being the one with superpowers. But then, he witnessed a Garou First Change and eating a policeman. He's bitter and wary, but with the proper convincing (and maybe a little scolding from his parents), he may help his brother.<br /> <br /> <b>Ressources</b><br /> Geoff still lives on a stipend from his parents. he doesn't trust himself fully yet to hold a full-time job, and besides, how could he manage it with his Garou life? He still lives at his parents', but he sometimes crashes on his uncle's couch after a training session, when he's too tired to drive back to his parents', in Easttown. He has an old car, a blue Ford Fiesta 1993. It's old, noisy, slightly rusty, but hey, if it does the job, that's enough, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Fetish</b><br /> A few months after he was welcomed in the Children of Gaia, Sarah Moonlight gave him a Truth Earring, saying it would help in his duties as a Philodox. He slightly unhappy that he had to get his ear pierced for that (it WAS painful, dammit!), but he wears it proudly, happy to display this (small, but still) act of trust and respect.<br /> <br /> <u>Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Sign:</u> Tambiyah<br /> <u>Race:</u> Caucasian<br /> <u>Sex:</u> Male<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> Homosexual<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u> Light Brown, but he dyes it regularely (with eco-friendly products!) in auburn.<br /> <u>Fur Color: </u> A light brown coat with a cream undercoat and a tuft of red on the top of the head and behind his ears.<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Blue, in both forms.<br /> <u>Height:</u> 6'3<br /> <u>Weight:</u> 210lb<br /> <u>Build:</u> Tall, broad shoulders, but slightly overweight, with some muscles from his training.<br /> <u>Distinctive Features:</u> He wears reading glasses, and tries to always keep at least some stubble on his face. He also has long hair that goes up to his shoulderblades, but usually, he ties it into a quick ponytail.<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> The Gentle Giant. That's the most clich\u00e9 description of Geoff. He's lucky enough to have inherited some strong genes from his family, which granted it this thick frame. However, he kinda took it for granted, and didn't bother to regulate himself when he started to take some weight. It's nothing too serious, but he could stand to lose a few pounds. Nothing that a good Garou training can't fix.<br /> He has somewhat of a round face, but the glasses he wears help slimming it down. He enjoys having facial hair, but you'd be surprised at the number of parents who prefer having a shaved man taking care of their kids. So, he usually tries to keep it at a minimum, grooming his stubble.<br /> He likes to wear practical clothes. He knows nothing about fashion, he just buys what he likes. Simple T-Shirts and jeans will do the trick. If it gets colder, he just add some hoodies and gloves. But still, he has a few favorite items in its wardrobe that he only uses for special occasions, such as a leather jacket, or even a kilt offered by Steve. He only wore it once, and can't bring himself to admit that...it was comfy, dammit!<br /> <br /> In Lupus, he looks a little unkempt to say the least. His fur is a light brown coat with a cream undercoat, and on the top of his lupine head, there's a tuft of red, amusing echo to his auburn dye. His body isn't built for strength or speed, but his assured demeanor reveals one thing : this wolf will endure.<br /> <br /> And in Crinos, the Giant lets loose. He's a hulking beast of rage and muscle that crosses the 8 foot threshold and settles at around 8'2. Geoff's self-control make sure that this form is rarely used, and it shows in its physique. There's nothing left from the nice teen that used to sing songs with kids, except...for the red mane, a natural merge of the fur and the hair that contributes to the fiery look of the beast. The rest of his fur is mostly dark brown, with a creamy white spot on his belly.<br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u><br /> His Blue Ford Fiesta 1993<br /> Reading Glasses (and a small kit to clean them)<br /> In his bag, he almost always has at least some band-aids, scissors, pen and paper.<br /> He also has a basic laptop that he mainly uses to study.<br /> A Samsung Galaxy S II (Booo Apple!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> Geoff was raised to be polite, and as such he can always show a smile to a stranger. He doesn't always <i>want to</i>, but that's irrelevant. He hates conflict, and tries to always defuse it or avoid it, but sometimes he prefers to just... back off. Obviously, as a Philodox, he'll have to work on that. He's a team player, who really wants everyone to get along toward the same goal.<br /> However, he's also an incorrigible sarcastic. Sometimes, he just <i>has</i> to get this irony out of his system. And the kids don't get it, it doesn't have the same flavor!<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u><br /> <br /> The Bolen were quite happy with Geoff, as he was far from being a troublesome teen. Of course, this was before becoming a fluffy killing machine with anger issues. Mark and Allison were both Kinfolk, with both of their siblings being Garou, but they didn't really envision that one of their two sons would rage and pick up the torch. Mark works at the Fun n' Learn Daycare Center, a charity organization he funded with the help of the city council. Sometimes, he asks his sons to lend him a hand with the kids when they're short on staff. As such, Geoff spent his teenage years taking care of small kids, and while it didn't help his social life, he loved it, and wanted to become a teacher so he could help with their future. Of course, the First Change got in the way. The daycare center had recently received a stock of free toys generously offered by Avalon Plastic. And while the kids were happy at first, the Wyrm-taint in those toys was making them meaner and more capricious, and it also affected the staff, who was becoming increasingly bad-tempered.<br /> One day, when Geoff was alone with his dad at the center, cleaning up after the kids, they were attacked by a small team of Pentex employees, who was intent on abducting them so they could be corrupted by Banes, and ready to fully spread the Wyrm's influence on the center. But woe to them as Geoff experienced his First Change and fought back, killing some of them in the process. Fortunately, his dad had the presence of mind to call Steve, his Garou brother so that he could get there to forcefully calm his son before he accidentally kills him. They threw the toys away, and cut all ties from Avalon Plastic.<br /> <br /> Now a Garou, Geoff continues to work with the kids, but on a rarer basis. He has joined the Children of Gaia because he is convinced that educating the new generations, homid and garou, is essential to Gaia's survival. He has started working on a online degree in education with a minor in nature science, and he plans to do school interventions in the future, while in the meantime he sometimes visits his father's charity to teach the kids about fauna and flora. He will shows no mercy to those who harm children, but he's still traumatized by the fact that he could have easily turned into a Black Spiral Dancer.<br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u><br /> -Geoff is still terrified by the fact that he could easily have killed his father during his First Change. He sometimes has nightmares about it, but until now, he has never committed the dreaded parricide in them. And the story Aaron told them, about being in a car accident with a girl who changed into a hulking wolf and ate a policeman... He won't ever lose control like this stupid girl. Right?<br /> <br /> -Before his own First Change, Geoff had something important to admit to his parents. But, the I-can-transform-into-a-fluffy-monster-at-will came first, and the kid hasn't found the right occasion yet. And so, alas, he hasn't made his coming-out yet. A few of his friends in highschool were aware of that, but that's it. He's quite shy on this subject. Not that he's ashamed of his sexual orientation, it's just that...at 19, he has only kissed 2 boys, and nothing more. Never had a boyfriend either. And...there is a little thing inherent to his homosexuality that bothers him : he won't be able to have children, or only through adoption (or in vitro, but it's a real mess right now). And now, there's this whole thing with the Litany forbidding relationships between Garou...he understands the reason but... being someone who's &quot;outside the norm&quot; himself, he can't help but have some compassion about those poor fellas who just want some love. He hopes not, but who knows, maybe he'll be in their positions one day, when he'll finally meet someone. Thank Gaia he's part of the Children of...well...hem...Gaia.<br /> <br /> <b>Cleithrophobia</b><br /> You know how a phobia is an irrational fear of something? Well, for Geoff, the irrationality comes from the fact that he doesn't know where his cleithrophobia comes from. He doesn't recall having experienced a trauma related to being locked up. In fact, he only discovered this slight handicap when some of the kids locked him in the laundry room for fun a few years ago. He got violent after half an hour of anguish, and almost broke the door before his dad discovered him in there.<br /> <br /> -Since he became a Garou, Geoff has been questioning himself. He's always been a good kid, the one who does his homework on time, who listens to his parents, who helps them on his free time... But now, he's something more. He has all this Rage inside of him and...it makes him think about his future. Yes, he likes helping kids, and he's convinced that they need to be protected...but what about him? He has spent his teenage years helping the family &quot;business&quot;, and maybe, now's the time to finally think about what he really wants to do in his life. He wonders if he should be more...well, selfish. He has always lived for the others, and he doesn't even know what he want. He's only working on his degree in education because he has some experience in it, but he hasn't even considered another career!<br /> That's part of the reason he chose to join the Children of Gaia : he's used to work for others. He was fine with it at first, and he's especially glad to not be involved in some political war. However, with his Fianna uncle training him, he's wondering if he hasn't been too hasty in his choice of tribe. Yes, he's not an Ahroun like Steve, and he certainly doesn't feel very irish...but there is something about their passion for life that is just appealing. The tales of their Galliard, their boasting and partying... They're larger than life, and Geoff is kinda jealous of that. The Children are nice, and the moots are peaceful and welcoming... but they could be more exciting. If he could go a few months back, after his First Change... he's not sure he would make the same choice.<br /> <br /> -For all the problems he has faced since his Change, with his Rage and all, Geoff is fairly happy with his new life. Before he discovered his powers, he was quite the geeky kid, and he had read tons of fantasy books. He had that stupid childhood dream in which he finally discovered that he was actually a wizard and/or the estranged son of an ancient god. It changed frequently, according to his latest favorite book, but he had never actually imagined being a werewolf. But now, even as the elders tell him about the dangers of the spirit world, of the others creatures that lurks into the night...he can't help but geek a little at the idea of discovering more supernatural creatures (Vampire actually exists?! Faes too?!). Sometimes, he wishes he was a Theurge...<br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> Freebies Spent :<br /> -1 dot of Fetish<br /> -2 dots of Gnosis (4)<br /> -1 dot of Melee (2)<br /> -1 dot of Empathy (2)<br /> -1 dot of Ritual (2)<br /> -1 dot of Willpower (1)<br /> -Calm Heart (3)<br /> <br /> <u>Experience Details</u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-25-2014, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T23:04:00-07:00","id":291074,"title":"","content":"I'm also working on my sheet, and will edit it into this post within the next day or two.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I had a question for our ST: Would Echo be able to contact Eager Spark through the Ancestors merit? Would she be capable of being an Ancestor Ally, one that Echo wasn't aware of yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T10:17:31-07:00","id":291442,"title":"","content":"OK, let's see what we have here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Mark- </u><br /> <br /> Looking good so far. You'll want to choose specialties for Dexterity, Crafts, Performance and Academics. I'm especially interested in the specialty for Crafts, as I can't think of much from Hannah's history that would suggest that. A hobby, perhaps?<br /> <br /> This is just a suggestion, but you might want to consider Inspiration as a starting gift (it's in tribe/auspice for both Silver Fangs and Ahrouns). Razor Claws and Sense Wyrm are both excellent and versatile gifts, but given Hannah's history, Inspiration may make more sense as a starting gift; you can always pick up Sense Wyrm or Razor Claws later. Just a suggestion, though; I have no problem with the gifts you've selected.<br /> <br /> As we discussed via PM, Foe From the Past at 3 pts may be a better idea than Enemy.<br /> <br /> You mention her training as a &quot;classic gymnast.&quot; Is &quot;classic&quot; a distinct type or style of gymnastics, or did you just use that to differentiate it from some newer style or something? I'm not that familiar with the minutiae of gymnastics.<br /> <br /> A quick note on Charles Dawnstar, which I think I should make clear if she wants to have a closer relationship to him- he works at a hospital in Camden, but he doesn't live in Camden. Camden is a shit-hole. It has the highest per capita violent crime rate in the United States. Hardly anybody chooses to live there. He lives in the nearby affluent suburb of Mount Laurel, NJ.<br /> <br /> 5'2&quot;. Out of curiosity, is she done growing? As a 16 year old, she could conceivably still grow taller. No need to make a decision now, just something to think about.<br /> <br /> As for the resources, to make sure I'm clear- her money is basically a stipend from her parents, correct?<br /> <br /> I'm fine with the car, just remember that she's too young to have a license in Pennsylvania, so it would legally be in her parents' names, and if she gets pulled over, things could get interesting.<br /> <br /> Nitpicky detail- the game is beginning on January 1, 2014. The iphone 6 isn't out yet. :-P<br /> <br /> A cheerleading outfit to fight sometimes, eh? She's sounding more and more Buffy-esque. ;-)<br /> <br /> Nitpicky detail- the Grand Klaive is called &quot;Dawn's Pride,&quot; not &quot;Dawnstar's Pride.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>James-</u><br /> <br /> Hmmm... by my count, you spent 12 freebie points on your attributes; big investment, but they're all quite appropriate.<br /> <br /> Good choices on all the specialties.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hold off on further comments until things are a little more fleshed out, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Josh-</u><br /> <br /> Contrary is a perfect demeanor for Val, but I wonder about Guru as his nature. There's not much we've seen so far that suggests him sharing his wisdom with others. Or is this something you plan to come out in his actions later? Can you tell me your thinking?<br /> <br /> I'm concerned about Val's total lack of combat abilities. I know he's not a combat oriented character, but the Garou are still Gaia's Warriors. Preparation for his Rite of Passage, even with the Children of Gaia, would have included at least some basic combat training. Unless you have a good and strong objection, you should put at least one dot in firearms, melee or brawl.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed 3 is pretty high, but the purity of his blood drawing the attention of the Vrikodara Jata is part of the backstory, so I'll allow it.<br /> <br /> The Ancestor idea is interesting. I need to think on it. First, tell me what &quot;<i>Vrikaprasvapa Sutra</i>&quot; translates as, please. Also, five dots of ancestors is a big investment; are you sure you want to do that for this? I'm also not sure if the &quot;Ancestor Ally&quot; merit is appropriate. In fact, if you really do intend to only be able to contact one ancestor with the ability, that seems more like a flaw than a merit.<br /> <br /> Karl is also Rank 3, if you wanted that detail.<br /> <br /> Twisted Upbringing and Intolerance are both good flaws.<br /> <br /> Kilograms? Really? You're going to make me do MATH?!? :-P<br /> <br /> You know, I have always thought those kurtas look comfortable.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the mental image of someone with their brain tied around under their chin. I need to design a fomor that looks like that. ;-)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Marmelade-</u><br /> <br /> Thanks for checking in. Enjoy your weekend!<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Echoes-</u><br /> <br /> The Ancestors background would work to contact Eager Spark. And remember, you don't have to take the Ancestor Ally merit; that reflects a close relationship with one particular ally, but is not required to contact that particular ancestor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Everybody-</u><br /> <br /> Feel free to comment on each others' sheets. Ask each other questions, make suggestions. No reason to stop our cooperative approach just because we've moved into mechanics. :-)<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T21:54:44-07:00","id":291817,"title":"","content":"Okay, awesome.<br /> <br /> Here's her rough draft. I still need to finish the personality, appearance, and spend the last of the freebie points. Other than that, I'm a little worried that she might come off as too specialized, so I wanted to throw this up now, see if you guys think anything's off or needs changing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Name:</b> Stir of Echoes<br /> <b>Player:</b> Eve<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> <b>Breed</b>: Lupus<br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Theurge<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Red Talons<br /> <b>Camp:</b><br /> <b>Sept:</b> Sept of the Thundering Pines/Sept of the Hidden Peak<br /> <b>Pack Name:</b><br /> <b>Pack Totem:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Big Bad Wolf<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Caregiver<br /> <b>Concept:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Attributes</span><br /> <b>Strength:</b> 2<br /> <b>Dexterity:</b> 3<br /> <b>Stamina:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma:</b> 2<br /> <b>Manipulation:</b> 2<br /> <b>Appearance</b>: 2<br /> <br /> <b>Perception:</b> 4 [Uncanny Instincts]<br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> 3<br /> <b>Wits:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Abilities</span><br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Talents</span></u><br /> <b>Alertness:</b> 4 (Ambushes)<br /> <b>Athletics:</b> 2<br /> <b>Brawl:</b> 3<br /> <b>Empathy:</b> 2<br /> <b>Expression:</b><br /> <b>Intimidation:</b> 2<br /> <b>Leadership:</b><br /> <b>Primal-Urge:</b> 3<br /> <b>Streetwise:</b><br /> <b>Subterfuge:</b><br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> <b>Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance:</b><br /> <b>Stealth:</b> 2<br /> <b>Survival</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledge</u><br /> <b>Academics:<br /> Computer:</b><br /> <b>Enigmas:</b> 3<br /> <b>Investigation:</b> 1<br /> <b>Law:<br /> Medicine:</b><br /> <b>Occult:</b> 2<br /> <b>Rituals:</b> 3<br /> <b>Science:<br /> Technology:</b><br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u><br /> <b>Mentor:</b> 3<br /> <b>Pure Breed:</b> 1<br /> <b>Ancestors:</b> 1<br /> <b>Fetish:</b> 1<br /> <b>Totem:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Heightened Sense (Lupus; Level 1; W20 pg.158)<br /> Mother's Touch (Theurge; Level 1; W20 pg.164)<br /> Eye of the Hunter (Red Talon; Level 1; W20 pg.185)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u><br /> N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Rage:</b> 3 (3)<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 7 (7)<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6 (6)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Renown</span><br /> <b>Glory</b><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <b>Honor</b><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom</b><br /> Permanent: 3<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Iron Will (Mental, 3; W20 pg.476)<br /> Wolf Sight (Physical, 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> Acute Sense - Hearing (Physical; 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Sign of the Wolf (Supernatural; 2; W20 pg.484)<br /> Animal Musk (Physical; 1; W20 pg.473)<br /> Pack Mentality (Mental; 2; W20 pg.477)<br /> Camp Enmity (Social; 1; W20 pg.481)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> <b>Mentor</b><br /> Sunset Howl, Red Talon, Galliard, Sept of the Thundering Pines<br /> <br /> <b>Sign of the Wolf</b><br /> Echo bears some stereotypical 'werewolf' traits, such as yellowish eyes, hairiness, palm lines that just happen to resemble a pentagram, and a few other things that pop culture has declared as proof of a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Musk</b><br /> &quot;Stench? What stench?&quot; You know that smell when someone decides to horde 20 cats in their apartment? It's kinda like that, except 100% wolf.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Mentality</b><br /> The only time she was truly alone was after her first 'pack' was killed and kidnapped - it was traumatizing, and now, she struggles to work alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Camp Enmity</b> (Dying Cubs)<br /> She doesn't know their name, but the Garou who had planned on 'baptizing her in blood' were apart of a Camp, and those Garou were thoroughly pissed when she left to avoid their ritual. Their anger spread to the Camp, and now they're unlikely to welcome her until she undergoes the rite and accepts their ideology.<br /> <br /> <b>Age:</b> 2<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> 15<br /> <b>Sign:</b> Rorg<br /> <b>Race:</b> White<br /> <b>Sex:</b> Female<br /> <b>Gender:</b> Female<br /> <b>Sexuality:</b> Unknown<br /> <b>Hair Color:</b> Reddish<br /> <b>Fur Color:</b> Reddish<br /> <b>Eye Color: </b>Dull green, gold specks<br /> <b>Height:</b> 5'1<br /> <b>Weight:</b> 124 lbs<br /> <b>Build:</b> Wiry, lean; more muscle than fat.<br /> <b>Distinctive Features:</b> Wild, unkempt hair; &quot;Signs of the Wolf&quot;; distinctive wolf scent in all forms.<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> <b>Homid</b><br /> Echo could be the poster girl for feral children, with her dirty skin, her animalistic gait, and her wide, round eyes that always appear to be on the alert, and which, on occasion, seem more yellow than green. She's pale, very pale, and quite short as well, made more apparent by the slouch in her shoulders - it's clear she's uncomfortable in this 'skin.' Her hair doesn't fall below the ear, and looks as though it's been cut with a rusty knife or sharp rock, with strands of various different lengths. It's a sort of dark coppery blonde in color, or auburn, and always tangled, never brushed. Physically speaking, she's scrawny, but tough, with what muscles she has readily apparent, lithe and limber.<br /> <br /> She's not a fan of clothes, and, unless absolutely necessary, she doesn't wear them, preferring instead to wander nude (in breed form). If the situation calls for them, she grabs whatever's available, without regard to style or good fashion sense. Her choices tend to be very bland (or very garish, if you let go wild), very &quot;blue collar&quot;, and often a size too big. She can't stand long sleeves, or collars that reach around the neck.<br /> <br /> <b>Lupus</b><br /> Here is where she truly excels, moving with a predatory grace few outside the Talon's can match. Powerful muscles ripple under thick red fur, fur that's painted with black patterns that run down from the nape of her neck to the tip of her tail. In stark contrast, below the jaw, the stomach and the legs are white. Her eyes a bright, intense gold.<br /> <br /> <b>Crinos</b><br /> She bears the visage of the penultimate hunter, a towering mass of muscle and sinew. Each limb is of equal width, made more for the chase and a quick, brutal kill over prolonged fighting. The red-black patterns of her fur have merged to become a dark, almost maroon shade, with one exception: at her knees and elbows, the color fades into a milky white, creating 'socks'. Her eyes are a brilliant gold, and they always seem to catch light in such a way that causes her pupils to 'glow.'<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment</b><br /> Nothing of importance.<br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> To sum her up in one word? Quiet. She's a wolf lost in thought, trying to make sense of all this madness. This might make her come off as aloof or cold, but beneath all that is a passionate woman, struggling to reign in her emotions. This passion leads to strong opinions, and Echo's not one to hold her tongue when the pressure's on; if you've been acting the fool and ask for her opinion, she'll lay it out bluntly, explaining why you're a moron (and what you ought to do to fix that). This is not meant to insult (well, usually), but to help, as Echo grows attached easily, and only wants to see that her people remain safe.<br /> <br /> Part of this is born out of insecurity. Echo fears losing someone again, and she's found that, if they don't respect wisdom, they certainly do respect <i>fear.</i> There's a darker side to this - she'll deny it viciously, but deep down, she gets a morbid sense of pleasure and comfort from seeing others recoil from her presence.<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u><br /> Stir of Echoes wasn't your typical Red Talon. She was born in captivity, hand fed by humans before being tossed into pack of unrelated wolves on some wild wolf preserve in New Jersey. Life was simple, yes, but it wasn't easy. The food was often road kill that smelled of oil and burnt rubber, or treats tossed to them by gawking humans with flashing lights and squalling children. The fences that protected them was still just a fancy cage. It was frustrating, and squabbles over ranks, food, frustration, and sheer boredom were common. Still, it was her home, it was all she knew, and you could say she loved them, her pack. Even the hairless ones that dumped food at their door.<br /> <br /> So, when a pack of Red Talons decided to break in one night, slaughter her &quot;human&quot; pack, kidnap her wolf family, and whisk off her off through the fence and to some alien landscape, Stir of Echoes had a hard time dealing with it. Her entire life had been destroyed in under an hour, and her saviors expected her to be overjoyed about it! Once the change happened, she was thrown into a sort of rehab for wolves - hunting, surviving, spirits, rituals - everything that was expected of her, as both a Talon and a oracle of her people. Rest was forbidden until she had the 'domestication' thoroughly ripped from her soul. This continued for months, until, suddenly, they decided she was ready. Soon, she was expected to go on her Rite of Passage (turns out her 'saviors' had been on their own), but they had something different in mind for her. She needed to be 'baptized in blood', to 'truly throw off the shackles of humanity'.<br /> <br /> It was too much. She figured what they meant, that she was to murder humans in some sort of ritual sacrifice, but she couldn't. Everything was moving too fast. One day all she worried about was if Wolf #5A1M was going to be a prick about that leg of deer, and the next she was expected to understand a thousand alien concepts, fight a holy war and play shaman to a race of warriors. It was too much. When Sunset Howl came with the opportunity to travel, Echo jumped for it, much to the chagrin of her elders, and fled.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b><br /> [Any notes you want to jot down about your character to have readily available for easy reference. Names of family members living or dead, particular goals, aspirations or fears, etc.]<br /> <br /> <b>Renown Details</b><br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> <b>Experience</b><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Details</b><br /> [This space is for me to record the details of experience granted and spent, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> Freebie Points 21<br /> <br /> +2 for Signs of the Wolf<br /> +1 for Animal Musk<br /> +2 for Pack Mentality<br /> +1 for Camp Enmity (Dying Cubs)<br /> -4 for Intimidation 2<br /> -3 for Willpower 3<br /> -3 for Iron Will<br /> -1 for Ancestors 1<br /> -2 for Alertness 4<br /> -1 for Wolf Sight<br /> -1 for Acute Sense<br /> -1 for Fetish 1<br /> -4 for Gnosis 7<br /> -1 for Rage 3<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have much to add to everyone else's characters, they all look great to me.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b><br /> - Finished appearance/personality, fixed spelling mistakes (hopefully I didn't miss any :-o)<br /> - Switched out Danger Sense for Alertness 4, Wolf Sight &amp; Acute Sense<br /> - Chose Big Bad Wolf for nature, explained in personality<br /> - Added Fetish 1; I'll be making a post here soon to ask about &amp; see if its concept is okay<br /> - Bumped Rage to 3 and Gnosis to 7. The rage boost is from all the stress she's been through, and the gnosis... I'm still working on a good justification for that, but basically I wanted her to be highly tuned to the spirit world, along with it being a reason why they named her Stir of Echoes (I doubt the Red Talons have seen/are fans of the movie :-P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":3804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","user":"Stir of Echoes","date":". 11-11-2014, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T02:06:34-07:00","id":291882,"title":"","content":"Man, I can already foresee some...<i>interesting </i>interactions between Val and Echoes. A quiet, confused lupus who just wants to be left alone, and a thoroughly irritating Ragabash who secretly thinks he's smarter than everyone else. Good times.<br /> <br /> Right-o, here's some more info on Val:<br /> <br /> Nature: Hmm, yeah, I had the same thoughts on the Guru thing. For now, Val\u2019s search for answers is too selfish to fulfill the \u2018spiritual mentor\u2019 aspect of the nature. I wanted Val to start off with a more egocentric nature, which, eventually, morphs into a more selfless one. However, none of the natures (that I've seen) really fit my character concept. So, with your permission, I can use one I made up:<br /> <b>Seeker</b>: You believe \u2013truly, deeply- that there is some great Truth to existence, hidden just beyond the sight of ignorant humanity. Of course, it could all just be meaningless and random, but nothing will stop your search for answers. For you, the journey itself is what matters. Other Garou might scoff, let them. After all, Truth wouldn't have much value if every thick-skulled fleabag sought it.<ul><li>Regain one point of Willpower whenever you achieve an epiphany that confirms your personal philosophy. Also, gain a point of Willpower when a revelation significantly shakes your metaphysical assumptions.</li> </ul>Ancestors: I wanted to have five points in this background to suggest that Vashti is both very powerful and highly interested in Val\u2019s development. However, I don\u2019t want Val to have any contact with his other ancestors. Furthermore, Vashti isn\u2019t quite an ally, as she won\u2019t step in to help Val out of a tight situation. For now, she\u2019s simply an enigmatic mentor, more annoyance than potent spiritual aid. If you think it works better, I can knock Ancestors down to three and boost Totem to three, for the good of the pack.<br /> <br /> <i>Vrikasya Prasvapah Sutra: </i>According to my horrendous Sanskrit, <i>Vrikasya Prasvapah </i>translates as \u2018Dream of the Wolf\u2019 and in this context, sutra means religious verse. And in case you got excited, no, it\u2019s not a real text, sadly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Weight: Hey, just consider it revenge for all the times I paged through White Wolf publications, squinted at the measurements and said: \u2018Yeah, but what\u2019s that in our money?\u2019 However, seeing as the majority of the pack\u2019s using the Imperial system, I\u2019ll convert it. Anything to save you from the horrors of arithmetic.<br /> <br /> Combat: See, this is what happens when you play too much Vampire, you start forgetting there <i>is</i> a combat system. Okay, how about this: Sunchaser knows Kung Fu...er, I mean Iskakku, and while she didn\u2019t teach Val the esoteric art, he does know how to poke someone in their squishy bits with a solid length of bamboo. Fear him.<br /> <br /> And may I ask a question, Jim? Why are you so critical of high levels of Pure Breed? I'm just curious to know your reasoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops! I made a serious grammatical error. 'Dream of the Wolf' should in fact be 'Vrikasya Prasvapah'. Told you my Sanskrit was horrendous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 10-26-2014, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:41:51-07:00","id":293387,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, my internet was down for a couple of days due to a storm messing with the lines.<br /> <br /> I'll update the sheet tomorrow and make some comments, but the internet just came back on and I should go to bed, just wanted to check in.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:27:11-07:00","id":293868,"title":"","content":"<u>Eve-</u><br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry about becoming too specialized. The ability restrictions on starting Lupus characters make this a common issue. As Echoes becomes more familiar with both human and garou culture, her skillset can expand with experience.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about your choice to put two dots in Investigation. Was that just a natural extension of Echoes' sense of curiosity? I don't have a problem with it, I'm just curious.<br /> <br /> As far as Danger Sense is concerned- it can be a little problematic in a PbP format. I will secretly make the rolls for you, and I will inform you via PM if Echoes has a premonition of danger. However, since this is via PM, this could lead to some situations where the other players forge ahead before you have a chance to check the forum. So, this could invalidate the danger sense in some cases. When I can, I'll try to shoot out the PM a little in advance of whatever post I make to give you a little more lead time, but that won't always happen, and it won't always be enough. So, it's a potential complication for both of us. There's nothing wrong with the merit, and I'm willing to work with you on it, but I wanted to make this clear to you before you make a final decision about whether you want to include it on Echoes' character sheet. I leave it up to you. If you're looking for an alternative that would still leave Stir of Echoes as the best at sensing danger without the troublesome aspects that premonition abilities bring to a format when we're not all at the table at the same time, consider maybe spending two of those freebie points on a fourth dot of alertness, with a specialty in Ambushes or Traps. Then use the remaining freebie dot to purchase a sensory merit such as Acute Sense (hearing, taste or smell) or Wolf Sight. That, combined with her already high perception (with appropriate specialty), the Lupus bonus to perception (when in that form) and the heightened senses gift (when in use) already put her well above the rest of the pack in that area. It's entirely your call, though. If the danger sense is part of how you envision the character, we'll make it work.<br /> <br /> Pack mentality is an excellent choice for Stir of Echoes, considering her personality and back story, and I am glad you chose it, but I warn you that it will come into play. There will be times when Stir of Echoes will be separated from the pack. Not to give anything away, but I actually have one entire chapter planned down the line which centers on the pack being involuntarily split up, with each member separated from the other for the entire chapter until they can [hopefully] reunite.<br /> <br /> I'm OK with Sign of the Wolf, just make sure that some of the signs are notable in the appearance description of Echoes (well, her homid form, at least). Also, be sure to bring one or two of them up once in a while when writing descriptions of her in play, for flavor.<br /> <br /> Awww, you figured out they were members of the Dying Cubs up at the Sept of the Hidden Peak? I was trying to be subtle. :-P<br /> <br /> Given Echoes' relative youth as a wolf, I was a little surprised you chose 18 as the age for her homid form. Did you just want to avoid the complications of a younger looking human form? I'm fine with it, I was just wondering your reasoning.<br /> <br /> Her Crinos form has socks! That's <i>so cute</i>!! She's just adorable!!!! :-D Seriously, I don't think I've ever seen a crinos form description with socks before. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Wolf #5A1M is always hogging the deer. He's such a jerk. &gt;:-(<br /> <br /> <u>Josh-</u><br /> <br /> Hmmm... so, the Seeker nature gives willpower when a revelation confirms his philosophy, or when a revelation contradicts his philosophy? If I didn't know better, I'd say you were trying to stack up on WP by having it both ways. :-P Seriously, though, I'm OK with it. It's basically a fancy way of saying that he can regain willpower whenever he experiences a major metaphysical epiphany, whether it confirms his beliefs or forces him to reevaluate them. I kind of like it.<br /> <br /> As for Ancestors, I do think 5 is a bit of overkill. Three does seem more reasonable. As for the fact that he can only contact one ancestor... I think we'll create a custom flaw:<br /> <br /> <b>Exclusive Ancestor (Supernatural; 1; Custom)</b><br /> Whether through some quirk of genetics or spirituality, a potent curse or through the actions of the ancestor spirit itself, your character can only use his Ancestors background to contact a single ancestor. You and the Storyteller should work together to determine the personality, history and traits of this Ancestor, and your character can only use the Ancestors background to increase traits that this single ancestor was skilled in. As a small compensation, contacting this ancestor only requires the usual difficulty 8 roll; since he can only contact one ancestor, there is no need for a 2 point difficulty increase to separate that ancestor from all the others. Depending on the nature of the block, this flaw can be bought off with experience after a quest to lift the curse, make direct contact with other ancestor spirits or make some other suitable change to justify it. If this flaw is bought off, the Ancestors background will work normally. Your character must have at least one dot of the ancestors background to take this flaw. It may not be combined with ancestor ally, but it may be combined with insane ancestor for a particularly miserable experience.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?<br /> <br /> As for the text, thanks for the translation. I had already googled it attempting to find a translation for myself, and discovered that it was not real. That works for me; now I can put whatever crazy stuff I want in there.<br /> <br /> I assume that Sunchaser's training would result in a dot of Melee. Do you intend for Val to carry a weapon?<br /> <br /> As for the Pure Breed thing... very high ratings of Pure Breed are supposed to be very rare, especially since they're tribe specific. However, in many games, I see pure breed thrown around like it was confetti. I'm fine with it if it's an integral part of the background, but I hate seeing players sink a bunch of points into it for the social bonuses when it really has nothing to do with their character history.<br /> <br /> <u>Mark-</u><br /> <br /> Thanks for checking in. :-) Hope you get things up and running.<br /> <br /> <u>James-</u><br /> <br /> Let's take a look. Well, we discussed Seed of Speech from the Stargazer Tribe Book, so I'm OK with the gift. However, your starting gifts are supposed to be one each from Breed, Auspice and Tribe, not three from the tribal list. So, take a look at the Homid and Galliard level one gifts on pages 152 and 169, and choose which Stargazer gift you want to keep. Remember, you can always pick up the others later. Level one gifts are quite inexpensive (3 xp if the gift is favored), and it's almost trivially easy to get a spirit to teach a level one gift of your own auspice, breed or tribe.<br /> <br /> We already discussed the Rite of Meeting from the Stargazer Tribebook, and I'm OK with it. For everyone's info, I've also house ruled that this rite has started to spread among the Hengeyokai, so it can be used on first meeting with any member of the Beast Courts who also knows the rite and chooses to participate, not just with other Stargazers.<br /> <br /> I like the relatively high rage, combined with the merits and flaws regarding its control. They make for an interesting combination that fits well for Scott's personality and history.<br /> <br /> So, the kinfolk doctor, to clarify- when you say she has a private practice, do you mean she has her own clinic or office or whatnot, or that she has a private practice within a larger hospital?<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs, not Silver Claws. :-P<br /> <br /> Your description for Reluctant Warrior is fine, but remember also that this is a Zodiac Flaw, not a Mental Flaw. It comes, at least in part, from the influence of Nerigal the Ice Warrior and the planet Mars at the time of his conception, birth and/or first change.<br /> <br /> Chester County is fine, but bear in mind that French Creek State Park, home of the Silver Fang Caern of the New World's Glory, is also partially in Chester County. It's up to you whether that's too close for comfort for Scott. ;-)<br /> <br /> Other than that, it looks good. One clarification in the back story- Scott doesn't know who killed his girlfriend exactly, whether it was garou from his own family traveling to Pennsylvania, or the local Silver Fangs working on their behalf, is that right?<br /> <br /> <u>New House Rule</u><br /> <br /> I'm going to add a new section to the first post for house rules, which I will fill as they come up. However, I just remembered one as I was flipping through Rites that I should mention. It's not a new rule; I use this in all my games. I just forgot to include it in the character creation post. The Rite of Accomplishment does not exist. When a garou earns 10 points of temporary renown, they automatically roll over into permanent renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T01:01:40-07:00","id":294609,"title":"","content":"<br /> <u>Jim-</u><br /> Nature: I realized after a bit of thought that the Seeker nature seemed like I was trying to game (hah) the system. But as you say, I\u2019m just trying to simulate the search for enlightenment. If you have any familiarity with Kindred of the East, gaining Willpower through the nature will be similar to achieving a low-scale \u2018<i>dah</i>\u2019, the moment of insight when one becomes more self-aware. I\u2019m glad you think it\u2019s okay, in my opinion it fits a lot better than Guru\u2026for now.<br /> <br /> Ancestor: Looks good! You say I need to work with the Storyteller (namely you) to create the ancestor\u2019s personality, history, traits etc. Do you want me to post a prototype character sheet for Vashti here, or shall we work it out over PM? Oh, and I hope that reference to \u2018insane ancestor\u2019 wasn\u2019t a suggestion for me to take the flaw. I can just imagine the horrid things you\u2019ll make poor Val do. Story Teller\u2019s and their nefarious schemes\u2026<br /> <br /> Melee: Yup, Sunchaser showed him how to swing a staff. Reading my words again, they seem a bit obtuse. What I was trying to express was that Sunchaser didn\u2019t teach Val Iskakku <i>per se</i>, but she did teach him the basics of staff-play. As for carrying a weapon, I don\u2019t know. Won\u2019t it seem a bit odd for Val to wander around town wielding six foot of bamboo? Mind you, the Children of Gaia Tribebook has an Ahroun who not only staff-fights his way through Seattle, but does so in Crinos to boot. I guess people are just more oblivious/open-minded over there? <br /> <br /> Pure Breed: You don\u2019t need to worry about that in Val\u2019s case. I think his personality will mitigate any respect his ancestors might have earned him. Especially from the Fenrir, mainly because Val\u2019s Crinos form looks like it should be sparkling. As a side-note, I never understood why Pure Breed improves Social rolls with Black Spiral Dancers. Isn\u2019t their whole shtick basically: \u2018The Litany can suck it! Hail the Wyrm! This message endorsed by Pentex.\u2019 Why would they care who you\u2019re related to?<br /> <br /> <u>James-</u><br /> Scott can speak Hindi? Darn, so I guess Val can\u2019t call him a bloody <i>gora kuta</i> behind his back\u2026As for the rest of the pack, hehehe\u2026<br /> <br /> And being named after a banana isn\u2019t so bad. At least he\u2019s not actually <i>named</i> banana, like the unfortunate ex-president of Zimbabwe, Canaan Banana. He even passed a law forbidding people to make fun of his name.<br /> <br /> Also, Silver Claws works better than Silver Fangs. Considering Garou aversion to silver, having a mouth full of the stuff must make chewing awkward. No wonder the whole tribe\u2019s nuts. Except Hannah of course, I\u2019m sure she\u2019s lovely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T16:45:29-07:00","id":295373,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll get to stuff point by point.<br /> <br /> NutiketAiel<br /> <br /> 1. I hadn't realized it was one breed, one tribe, and one auspice. I had thought it was just three level 1 Gifts. I will take a look and correct what I've got.<br /> <br /> 2. Lots of private practice doctors have clinics where they see patients for general stuff, where 90% of what they do is just see people who are sick. That's what Scott does. It's mostly about checking insurance information, weighing people, blood pressure, and maybe take some blood for a test. As his stats can tell you, Scott doesn't know a whole lot about medicine. Now, doctors who work at private practices like this also usually work with a hospital that their patience go to for bigger important stuff, but Scott personally doesn't have the training to help with any sort of surgery or anything.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, Silver FANGS. I'll edit my post up and try to remember that.<br /> <br /> 4. This is one thing I want to ask you on. This is my first time with Werewolf the Apocalypse and I actually the first time I've played Old World of Darkness outside of a few brief sessions many years ago. So it's a lot of new stuff for me to swallow. While Reluctant Warrior is, as you say, supposed to be a Zodiac Flaw and not a Mental Flaw, would you mind if I just had it as a Mental Flaw instead? That did exactly the same thing. With Scott I'm trying to grasp some of the more personal aspects of a person dealing with rage and being a werewolf, and introducing astrology into my character concept early on makes things a bit more difficult.<br /> <br /> 5. It doesn't have to be Chester County. I'm not too familiar with the area. I would make me feel best if you picked a place for Scott to live, and then I could just read up on that, instead of trying to familiarize myself with all of the Delaware Valley. I do have to finish the Stargazers Tribebook first, and I'd like to be able to sort of focus on that more than on where I situate my character.<br /> <br /> 6. Actually Scott doesn't even know if it was werewolves who killed his girlfriend. Most people aren't torn apart by &quot;wild dogs&quot; on the streets of Philadelphia, and it probably was werewolves, but that's a connection point that Scott admits probably exists but hasn't pointed fingers. Scott does know his family is crazy and relentless, but he doesn't suspect them or the Silver Fangs. It's fresh enough in his mind that it's still a tragic accident.<br /> <br /> Al-Haleem<br /> <br /> 1. Val wouldn't know that Scott can speak Hindi, so he can call him whatever he wants! I doubt Scott will ever really speak Hindi in game, and rarely speak Chinese. While I haven't decided what Scott looks like, it won't be anything at all &quot;ethnic&quot; or give any indication that he's anything but some back-woods country bumpkin.<br /> <br /> 2. I'll switch back to Cavendish if people think that's a better last name than Cadwell. I just kept thinking about bananas whenever I thought of Scott and wanted to try to go with something more seriously &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:38:58-07:00","id":295444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, let's see what we have here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Mark- </u><br /> <br /> Looking good so far. You'll want to choose specialties for Dexterity, Crafts, Performance and Academics. I'm especially interested in the specialty for Crafts, as I can't think of much from Hannah's history that would suggest that. A hobby, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I updated all the specialties, and changed Crafts to Professional Skill: Cooking. I can see Hannah enjoying making her own food, especially so she can feed herself while training in the months leading up to her Rite of Passage (gotta carbo load right?), a practicality that became a bit of a passion she's just delving into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just a suggestion, but you might want to consider Inspiration as a starting gift (it's in tribe/auspice for both Silver Fangs and Ahrouns). Razor Claws and Sense Wyrm are both excellent and versatile gifts, but given Hannah's history, Inspiration may make more sense as a starting gift; you can always pick up Sense Wyrm or Razor Claws later. Just a suggestion, though; I have no problem with the gifts you've selected.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I changed Razor Claws to Inspiration, which was something I also debated about a lot. I want to keep Sense Wyrm though just to make sure someone has it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As we discussed via PM, Foe From the Past at 3 pts may be a better idea than Enemy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I changed my flaws a bit, adding in Dark Secret, which I already had in the back ground I had written for Hannah, and also added Compulsion from Players Guide to Garou. Between Overconfident, and Compulsion I basically gave myself the Silver Fang tribe flaw (Derangement: Delusions of Grandeur), which I like because of the very high pure breed. To be clear the Compulsion is to brag and be superior over those who appear weaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mention her training as a &quot;classic gymnast.&quot; Is &quot;classic&quot; a distinct type or style of gymnastics, or did you just use that to differentiate it from some newer style or something? I'm not that familiar with the minutiae of gymnastics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I updated the wording a bit to make it more clear, but I didn't mean a particular style, other than she trained in gymnastics and dance as separate things. She didn't just do one or the other, they were complimentary to being a good cheerleader, but she's formally trained in being an actual gymnast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A quick note on Charles Dawnstar, which I think I should make clear if she wants to have a closer relationship to him- he works at a hospital in Camden, but he doesn't live in Camden. Camden is a shit-hole. It has the highest per capita violent crime rate in the United States. Hardly anybody chooses to live there. He lives in the nearby affluent suburb of Mount Laurel, NJ.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted, also I wouldn't mind having that relationship be closer. Like saying she crashed at his place regularly during her months of training just to get way from the family when she was feeling down about eating people and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5'2&quot;. Out of curiosity, is she done growing? As a 16 year old, she could conceivably still grow taller. No need to make a decision now, just something to think about.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I figured she still would grow a bit more, probably leveling out around 5'5'' or so, I can make her taller now, but I figure she'll never get really that tall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the resources, to make sure I'm clear- her money is basically a stipend from her parents, correct?<br /> <br /> I'm fine with the car, just remember that she's too young to have a license in Pennsylvania, so it would legally be in her parents' names, and if she gets pulled over, things could get interesting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's her allowance so to speak, and it is a lot. I did lower it a dot to keep it more controlled, and to move a point around. However, as the game progresses, it should be noted that Hannah may take over a more leadership role in her family, which would allow her access to even more money. In my head her family is pretty damn Rich, that happens when you invest for House Wyrmfoe at large, which is what her mom and dad do, control Silver Fang money.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, she does have a learners permit at this point, but the car isn't hers, but it was her 16th birthday gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitpicky detail- the game is beginning on January 1, 2014. The iphone 6 isn't out yet. :-P<br /> <br /> Nitpicky detail- the Grand Klaive is called &quot;Dawn's Pride,&quot; not &quot;Dawnstar's Pride.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Updated them both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=291442#post291442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A cheerleading outfit to fight sometimes, eh? She's sounding more and more Buffy-esque. ;-)<br /> <br /> <br /> -Jim</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the family feud with Vampires, and the fact the character was a Cheerleader from the very inception of the concept, can you really blame me =p<br /> <br /> Jim with your approval, I'd like to have the Rite of Boasting (level 1 Renoun; pg 216 W20); as Hannah might have just picked it up by watching, and being like &quot;I would so do that,&quot; and she has Rituals one, as a knowledge. And if you're feeling super generous, Greet the Sun (minor Rite, pg 220, W20), which I think Hannah would have been taught as she showed interest in the Sun Lodge. Let me know if either of those are cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now for everyone else!<br /> <br /> Echoes- Keep in mind that as your sheet stands you have no Rituals, considering you're a lupus and this is like pre rite of passage, that might be fine, but as the theurge, don't forget to pick them up sooner or later =p<br /> <br /> Everyone else looks good for their concept, except for the general lack of Athletics, which is the skill you use to dodge in W20. I'm happily awaiting seeing everyone else's sheets.<br /> <br /> As it stands it looks like we have all the bases covered for basic stuff. Someone has sense Wyrm, someone has mother's touch, and everyone else can generally fight.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is jumping the gun a bit, and Jim already has plans in mind, but maybe we should talk about a mission statement for the pack a bit ahead of time, and possibly even look at a totem that represents that. If it's too early for that, I understand Jim, but having an idea of where the pack as a whole is headed could help people decide where to put any extra points, or how to shape things if they're unclear.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 10-28-2014, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T05:57:06-07:00","id":295759,"title":"","content":"<u>Mark</u><br /> <br /> Hey, Val doesn't <i>do </i>athletics. He hides behind the Ahroun and says stuff like, 'Yeah, you show 'em!' And if the battle goes badly, he turns and runs. With dignity. I didn't put any real points into a combat-oriented skills because I didn't think it fit Val's character. He spent most of his time indoors reading, and definitely skipped out of gym class when he could. But if you think he's gonna get mangled in the first fight, maybe I should rethink that.. <br /> <br /> And don't you think it'll be more fun to work out the pack's mission statement in character? Think of all the potential arguments! The drama! I'm sure Jim has something planned...<br /> <br /> Oh man, you chose Dark Secret. Hehe. Val now has a mission. I foresee him and Hannah getting on like two cats in a sinking sack.<br /> <br /> <u>James</u><br /> <br /> If this is your first Werewolf game, I hope you find it enjoyable. I haven't played much Werewolf myself, being far more familiar with Vampire. Don't be afraid to ask our Storyteller lots of difficult, complex questions!<br /> <br /> And Cavendish makes me think of Henry Cavendish, an 18th century British natural philosopher. I had no idea Cavendish was a brand of bananas...The things you learn.<br /> <br /> (And please, call me Josh. Al-Haleem is a perfectly legitimate name...if you come from 9th century Baghdad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T23:42:45-07:00","id":296664,"title":"","content":"<u>Josh</u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Man, I can already foresee some...<i>interesting </i>interactions between Val and Echoes. A quiet, confused lupus who just wants to be left alone, and a thoroughly irritating Ragabash who secretly thinks he's smarter than everyone else. Good times. </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Now that I've finished writing her up, I can see that they're nearly opposites, and I'll be surprised if there isn't a clash of personalities at some point. Maybe they'll balance each other out. :-P He can teach her how to chill out, and she can teach him how to murder things.<br /> <br /> <u>Jim</u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm curious about your choice to put two dots in Investigation. Was that just a natural extension of Echoes' sense of curiosity? I don't have a problem with it, I'm just curious. </div> </div> </div>This was a case of my Forsaken background/bias bleeding into Apocalypse, as in that game Investigation is pretty important for characters who needed to solve riddles and the like. After glancing at W20 again, I think it might be more appropriate for her if a dot was tossed into Enigmas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as Danger Sense is concerned, ... </div> </div> </div>I decided to swap it out for Wolf Sight &amp; Acute Sense. I hadn't thought how the pbp format could effect powers like those, and I think things will run smoother this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pack mentality is an excellent choice for Stir of Echoes, considering her personality and back story, and I am glad you chose it, but I warn you that it will come into play. </div> </div> </div>That's fine by me. ;D I know it'll be harder for her, but it makes for good character development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Awww, you figured out they were members of the Dying Cubs up at the Sept of the Hidden Peak? I was trying to be subtle. :-P </div> </div> </div>A lucky guess! From their description I thought there had to be at least a small group of Dying Cubs or Predator Kings in there, and that they'd have something to say about her upbringing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given Echoes' relative youth as a wolf, I was a little surprised you chose 18 as the age for her homid form. Did you just want to avoid the complications of a younger looking human form? I'm fine with it, I was just wondering your reasoning. </div> </div> </div>I originally had her as 15, but then I realized that it might come off as weird or creepy with the whole walking around nude in Homid form thing. If that's alright, I'd like to put her back to her original age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her Crinos form has socks! That's <i>so cute</i>!! She's just adorable!!!! :-D Seriously, I don't think I've ever seen a crinos form description with socks before. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Wolf #5A1M is always hogging the deer. He's such a jerk. &gt;:-( </div> </div> </div>^^<br /> <br /> I think she's pretty much ready to go now, but there was one more thing I was interested in - a fetish. Specifically, a fetish that'd allow her to speak Garou and/or human languages (English in her case) fluently in lupus/hispo form. I imagine it might be important for some Talons to interrogate humans/etc. they come across before offing them, and a fetish to allow them to speak might speed up the process over shapeshifting. Being able to communicate with other tribes in your favored form is always a bonus, too.<br /> <br /> If that sounds good, I imagine it being some sort of fur-braided thread with teeth and feathers, wrapped around the body so that it doesn't easily slip off. Basically, something like these:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://werewolfcalendar.com/wp/wp-content/galleries/2015-images-1/tatchit_2015.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://werewolfcalendar.com/wp/wp-content/gallery/2011-gallery/11december.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <s>totally not echoes</s><br /> <img src=\"http://werewolfcalendar.com/wp/wp-content/gallery/2012-images/blackpassion7772012.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://werewolfcalendar.com/wp/wp-content/gallery/2008-gallery/july.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...okay, maybe not as flamboyant as that last image, I don't think the pack would appreciate her strolling around dressed like some sort of wolf pimp.<br /> <br /> <u>Mark</u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Echoes- Keep in mind that as your sheet stands you have no Rituals, considering you're a lupus and this is like pre rite of passage, that might be fine, but as the theurge, don't forget to pick them up sooner or later =p </div> </div> </div>Will keep this in mind. ;D I plan on rites becoming her thing later on in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T04:15:47-07:00","id":296909,"title":"","content":"Oh my gosh, Eve! Scrap your whole character sheet and make Echoes a wolf pimp! Val can be her ho, and we'll defeat the Wyrm through the power of awesome. Also, I just noticed, the Black Fury in W20 also has 'socks'. There's just something about terrifying forces of nature and looking adorable.<br /> <br /> But seriously, have you seen that Black Fury? I wouldn't want to meet her in a dark alley is all I'm saying.<br /> <br /> And interesting choice for nature/demeanor. So if I've got this right, Echoes wants to protect and nurture her pack, yet at the same time, harbors a dark desire to cause terror. But if her 'demeanor' is a caregiver, does that mean it's just a front? Does she secretly want to be the teeth in the night that haunts the dreams of man? Because that's pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 10-30-2014, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T09:05:59-07:00","id":297169,"title":"","content":"<u>Josh-</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nature: I realized after a bit of thought that the Seeker nature seemed like I was trying to game (hah) the system. But as you say, I\u2019m just trying to simulate the search for enlightenment. If you have any familiarity with Kindred of the East, gaining Willpower through the nature will be similar to achieving a low-scale \u2018<i>dah</i>\u2019, the moment of insight when one becomes more self-aware. I\u2019m glad you think it\u2019s okay, in my opinion it fits a lot better than Guru\u2026for now. </div> </div> </div>Just for clarification (since the rules in previous editions tended to be kind of sketchy on this), both your nature and demeanor can change over time, with suitable in character justification and my approval.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ancestor: Looks good! You say I need to work with the Storyteller (namely you) to create the ancestor\u2019s personality, history, traits etc. Do you want me to post a prototype character sheet for Vashti here, or shall we work it out over PM? Oh, and I hope that reference to \u2018insane ancestor\u2019 wasn\u2019t a suggestion for me to take the flaw. I can just imagine the horrid things you\u2019ll make poor Val do. Story Teller\u2019s and their nefarious schemes\u2026 </div> </div> </div>LOL, no, it was not a suggestion. I actually have some plans in mind for who Vashti is (or, perhaps more accurately, was). However, these are things Val will need to discover on his own as the game goes on and he interacts with her. Since he doesn't really know who she was, he won't know for certain if she was good at a particular skill unless he tries to channel it, or if it comes up while he's communicating with her (assuming she doesn't lie). If there is anything specific you have in mind for Vashti, tell me now before I get any further in my secret plans for her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Melee: Yup, Sunchaser showed him how to swing a staff. Reading my words again, they seem a bit obtuse. What I was trying to express was that Sunchaser didn\u2019t teach Val Iskakku <i>per se</i>, but she did teach him the basics of staff-play. As for carrying a weapon, I don\u2019t know. Won\u2019t it seem a bit odd for Val to wander around town wielding six foot of bamboo? Mind you, the Children of Gaia Tribebook has an Ahroun who not only staff-fights his way through Seattle, but does so in Crinos to boot. I guess people are just more oblivious/open-minded over there? </div> </div> </div>Ugh. The Revised Children of Gaia Tribebook is pure garbage. Some of the mechanical stuff is OK (for example, it includes Black Unicorn, one of my personal favorite totems), but the story info and the history of the tribe as described therein are terrible, and the stuff about the protests in Seattle made me want to throw up. Don't take it too seriously. As for walking around with a staff, yes it would be a little unusual, but people do sometimes walk around with walking sticks. Remember also that, while Sunchaser's training may have focused on the staff, the melee skill can be applied to practically any hand to hand weapon. A <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baton_%28law_enforcement%29#Expandable_baton\" target=\"_blank\">collapsible baton</a> would be just as non-lethal (for those of us with Children of Gaia-ish sensibilities) and far more concealable. Of course, I wouldn't recommend trying to use it in Crinos unless you want to look pretty damn silly...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pure Breed: You don\u2019t need to worry about that in Val\u2019s case. I think his personality will mitigate any respect his ancestors might have earned him. Especially from the Fenrir, mainly because Val\u2019s Crinos form looks like it should be sparkling. As a side-note, I never understood why Pure Breed improves Social rolls with Black Spiral Dancers. Isn\u2019t their whole shtick basically: \u2018The Litany can suck it! Hail the Wyrm! This message endorsed by Pentex.\u2019 Why would they care who you\u2019re related to? </div> </div> </div>Oh, they predate Pentex by centuries, but that's neither here nor there. I always understood it as a kind of instinct thing. BSDs may serve the Wyrm instead of Gaia, but they're still werewolves. It works on them for the same reason that it works on Glass Walkers or Bone Gnawers, who don't care about such things on an intellectual level. It's ingrained.<br /> <br /> <u>James-</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. I hadn't realized it was one breed, one tribe, and one auspice. I had thought it was just three level 1 Gifts. I will take a look and correct what I've got. </div> </div> </div>Good choices, but bear in mind that Apecraft's Blessing requires a Wits+Crafts roll, and Scott doesn't have any dots in Crafts at the moment, so it'll be a bit difficult to use. Side-note: I love abilities like Perfect Recall when used in an online setting; if it's something that happened during play, all we need to do is copy-paste. ;-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Lots of private practice doctors have clinics where they see patients for general stuff, where 90% of what they do is just see people who are sick. That's what Scott does. It's mostly about checking insurance information, weighing people, blood pressure, and maybe take some blood for a test. As his stats can tell you, Scott doesn't know a whole lot about medicine. Now, doctors who work at private practices like this also usually work with a hospital that their patience go to for bigger important stuff, but Scott personally doesn't have the training to help with any sort of surgery or anything. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. This is one thing I want to ask you on. This is my first time with Werewolf the Apocalypse and I actually the first time I've played Old World of Darkness outside of a few brief sessions many years ago. So it's a lot of new stuff for me to swallow. While Reluctant Warrior is, as you say, supposed to be a Zodiac Flaw and not a Mental Flaw, would you mind if I just had it as a Mental Flaw instead? That did exactly the same thing. With Scott I'm trying to grasp some of the more personal aspects of a person dealing with rage and being a werewolf, and introducing astrology into my character concept early on makes things a bit more difficult. </div> </div> </div>The Stargazer is worried about introducing astrology? :-P Nah, it's fine, you can change it to a mental flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. It doesn't have to be Chester County. I'm not too familiar with the area. I would make me feel best if you picked a place for Scott to live, and then I could just read up on that, instead of trying to familiarize myself with all of the Delaware Valley. I do have to finish the Stargazers Tribebook first, and I'd like to be able to sort of focus on that more than on where I situate my character. </div> </div> </div>No prob, I'll give it a little thought and get back to you. And, again, there's nothing wrong with him living in Chester County, I just wanted to make sure you were aware of the proximity to the Silver Fang caern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Actually Scott doesn't even know if it was werewolves who killed his girlfriend. Most people aren't torn apart by &quot;wild dogs&quot; on the streets of Philadelphia, and it probably was werewolves, but that's a connection point that Scott admits probably exists but hasn't pointed fingers. Scott does know his family is crazy and relentless, but he doesn't suspect them or the Silver Fangs. It's fresh enough in his mind that it's still a tragic accident. </div> </div> </div>Really? He comes from a family of werewolf kin who hated the fact that he was dating a non-kin woman, and he bought the wild dog story? Interesting. BTW, please let Scott know that I have a bridge to sell him. ;-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I'll switch back to Cavendish if people think that's a better last name than Cadwell. I just kept thinking about bananas whenever I thought of Scott and wanted to try to go with something more seriously &gt;_&gt; </div> </div> </div>Again, you can go with whatever name you like, banana boy. :-P<br /> <br /> <u>Mark-</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I updated all the specialties, and changed Crafts to Professional Skill: Cooking. I can see Hannah enjoying making her own food, especially so she can feed herself while training in the months leading up to her Rite of Passage (gotta carbo load right?), a practicality that became a bit of a passion she's just delving into. </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with all those specialties, and Professional Skill Cooking is a good choice. Did she take that in case she decides to eat more cops? It's OK, you can tell me. ;-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I changed Razor Claws to Inspiration, which was something I also debated about a lot. I want to keep Sense Wyrm though just to make sure someone has it. </div> </div> </div>Looks good. Remember, she can always get Razor Claws back later with experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I changed my flaws a bit, adding in Dark Secret, which I already had in the back ground I had written for Hannah, and also added Compulsion from Players Guide to Garou. Between Overconfident, and Compulsion I basically gave myself the Silver Fang tribe flaw (Derangement: Delusions of Grandeur), which I like because of the very high pure breed. To be clear the Compulsion is to brag and be superior over those who appear weaker. </div> </div> </div>These are fine, but Compulsion was actually included in W20. It's on page 476.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Noted, also I wouldn't mind having that relationship be closer. Like saying she crashed at his place regularly during her months of training just to get way from the family when she was feeling down about eating people and all. </div> </div> </div>That's cool. Does he know her Dark Secret?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it's her allowance so to speak, and it is a lot. I did lower it a dot to keep it more controlled, and to move a point around. However, as the game progresses, it should be noted that Hannah may take over a more leadership role in her family, which would allow her access to even more money. In my head her family is pretty damn Rich, that happens when you invest for House Wyrmfoe at large, which is what her mom and dad do, control Silver Fang money. </div> </div> </div>I was fine with three dots, actually. I wasn't concerned that it was too high; I just wanted to clarify the source. Three dots seemed appropriate for such a spoiled little rich girl from the Main Line. The Dawnstar family is pretty damn rich, but as you note, that wealth comes almost entirely from their kinfolk, so that's something to bear in mind. Raising her resources background in play is possible, but it would require some roleplay, particularly with those kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jim with your approval, I'd like to have the Rite of Boasting (level 1 Renoun; pg 216 W20); as Hannah might have just picked it up by watching, and being like &quot;I would so do that,&quot; and she has Rituals one, as a knowledge. And if you're feeling super generous, Greet the Sun (minor Rite, pg 220, W20), which I think Hannah would have been taught as she showed interest in the Sun Lodge. Let me know if either of those are cool. </div> </div> </div>Well, as I noted, every character that starts with the Rituals knowledge would be starting with one or more appropriate rites of my choice, over and above those they choose with the Rites background. However, I intend to announce those as the last part of character creation, so as not to discourage players from making their own choices. I will tell you, however, that the Rite of Boasting is not the one I picked for Hannah. If you want her to start with it, you'll need to spend a point on the rites background. Of course, she can always learn it after her rite of passage, during play or downtime. Finding a teacher would not be difficult.<br /> <br /> <u>Eve-</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This was a case of my Forsaken background/bias bleeding into Apocalypse, as in that game Investigation is pretty important for characters who needed to solve riddles and the like. After glancing at W20 again, I think it might be more appropriate for her if a dot was tossed into Enigmas. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. Yes, if you were looking for skill with riddles, Enigmas is the way to go, though Investigation is still a good ability to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I decided to swap it out for Wolf Sight &amp; Acute Sense. I hadn't thought how the pbp format could effect powers like those, and I think things will run smoother this way. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I think this was a good choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's fine by me. ;D I know it'll be harder for her, but it makes for good character development. </div> </div> </div>Just remember, with appropriate roleplaying, most flaws can be bought off with experience later. Perhaps Echoes will one day move beyond this limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I originally had her as 15, but then I realized that it might come off as weird or creepy with the whole walking around nude in Homid form thing. If that's alright, I'd like to put her back to her original age. </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's fine. We're all adults here, and this is an adult game. Adult situations and adult themes will be a part of the game. I think we can handle nudity. Just no pictures, obviously. Go ahead and put her back to apparent age 15 if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think she's pretty much ready to go now, but there was one more thing I was interested in - a fetish. Specifically, a fetish that'd allow her to speak Garou and/or human languages (English in her case) fluently in lupus/hispo form. I imagine it might be important for some Talons to interrogate humans/etc. they come across before offing them, and a fetish to allow them to speak might speed up the process over shapeshifting. Being able to communicate with other tribes in your favored form is always a bonus, too. </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmmm... well, remember that Garou in Lupus and Hispo form can make themselves understood to other Garou, though it is difficult. That being said, I'm OK with this as a level one fetish. Where did she get it from, though? Who made it for her/gave it to her, and why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will keep this in mind. ;D I plan on rites becoming her thing later on in the game. </div> </div> </div>Remember that every character starting with dots in the Rituals knowledge will start with one or more appropriate rites chosen by me. So, she will be starting with a few.<br /> <br /> <u>Everyone-</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe this is jumping the gun a bit, and Jim already has plans in mind, but maybe we should talk about a mission statement for the pack a bit ahead of time, and possibly even look at a totem that represents that. If it's too early for that, I understand Jim, but having an idea of where the pack as a whole is headed could help people decide where to put any extra points, or how to shape things if they're unclear. </div> </div> </div>A mission statement for the pack is really something that should be discussed IC. As for a totem, sure, you guys can start talking about it now. I had intended to start this discussion amongst you OOC while we were roleplaying your rite of passage, but if you want to start discussing it now, by all means do so. A final decision will have to wait for the time being, though. Remember, you're not limited to those that appear in the W20 core book. There are many excellent sources of totems. The revised edition Players Guide to the Garou has an excellent selection of totems, and there are some good ones in the tribebooks as well (don't feel limited to the tribes in the pack, either; just because those totems favor certain tribes doesn't mean they don't adopt packs without members of that tribe). Rage Across the Heavens is also an excellent source; the Planetary Incarnae make potent and influential, albeit expensive, totems. Of course, the stats of totems from the revised edition may warrant some updating. Custom totems are also an option, with my approval. One caveat- this game will involve a lot of traveling, sometimes on short notice, so a totem with a ban that forces the characters to stay in a particular geographic area would not be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 10-30-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T11:26:45-07:00","id":297276,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Sunchaser will probably insist Val take a staff to the Rite of Passage. He needs to impress his Fenrir brothers with his lack of prowess after all. So he\u2019ll begin the story with a staff, but he probably won\u2019t drag it around everywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, after some reading I\u2019ve (tentatively) chosen a star sign for Val.<br /> <br /> And poor Children of Gaia revised. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s <i>quite</i> so awful. It\u2019s just a shame that one of the few books featuring a gay Garou couple had to be so lacklustre. Sigh. C\u2019est la vie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T11:52:47-07:00","id":297291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=297276#post297276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so Sunchaser will probably insist Val take a staff to the Rite of Passage. He needs to impress his Fenrir brothers with his lack of prowess after all. So he\u2019ll begin the story with a staff, but he probably won\u2019t drag it around everywhere.<br /> <br /> Also, after some reading I\u2019ve (tentatively) chosen a star sign for Val.<br /> <br /> And poor Children of Gaia revised. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s <i>quite</i> so awful. It\u2019s just a shame that one of the few books featuring a gay Garou couple had to be so lacklustre. Sigh. C\u2019est la vie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meros, eh? Interesting. What made you decide that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T12:12:00-07:00","id":297330,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of the wandering planet; no home, no rest, just an endless journey, always searching for something. It's a lonely life, but someone's gotta live it. Plus, Pluto's not technically a planet anymore, and the idea of Val being born under a 'dwarf planet' just fits with his characterization. Because OF COURSE its gonna be the lamest planet, nothing cool like Jupiter, please. Ever the underwolf, that's Val.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:37:09-07:00","id":297555,"title":"","content":"Alright, I finally posted my character sheet on the first page. I need some help, especially with flaws, as I can't seem to find some that would fit Geoff. Having his history and his personality more defined would help, of course, but I'm still quite sick, and I just want to lay down and sleep, as my fever is running high. But first, does it look good, stats-wise? I've neved done a Werewolf character before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T19:12:02-07:00","id":297704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=297555#post297555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I finally posted my character sheet on the first page. I need some help, especially with flaws, as I can't seem to find some that would fit Geoff. Having his history and his personality more defined would help, of course, but I'm still quite sick, and I just want to lay down and sleep, as my fever is running high. But first, does it look good, stats-wise? I've neved done a Werewolf character before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Ward could work for your character's Brother.<br /> <br /> Also maybe Soft Heart, Geoff always seemed super nice to me. But maybe not that nice =p<br /> <br /> Maybe Naive, again cause of the generally nice guy optimism thing.<br /> <br /> Maybe none of those work, just throwing ideas out. I wish I could give you page numbers, but I don't have my book with me.<br /> <br /> Sheet looks good so far, I will offer that Gifts are super expensive with freebies, but pretty cheep with XP, but they're your points.<br /> <br /> Jim-<br /> <br /> Of course I intend to eat more cops....*shifty eyes*<br /> <br /> I'm fine with whatever rituals.<br /> <br /> I'd also assume Charles knows I ate people, it probably took a lot of cajoling to get it out of Hannah, but she probably broke down and told him eventually. I assume he's supportive, but weary.<br /> <br /> I think the rest of the sheet is locked in at this point though, I wish I could have squeezed a few more points, but I spent a ton on Merits, and I don't want to give any of them up =p<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 10-30-2014, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T00:43:32-07:00","id":297917,"title":"","content":"Awesome, the pack's all together! I'm glad you're here Flo, although I'm sorry you're sick. I hope it's nothing too serious.<br /> <br /> Now an abrupt change of topic! For flaws, I don't think Na\u00efve will work, because it'll mitigate the point of high empathy. Ward might be interesting. Aaron would probably resent having his brother constantly checking up on him. Soft-Hearted could also work. Although I don't know why the flaw insists you must AVOID a situation where someone's in pain. Wouldn't it be more dramatic if you felt compelled to aid someone in pain...no matter what? I'll probably have a better idea for things when you post more of Geoff's personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:32:20-07:00","id":298026,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tip on the gifts Mark, I admit that I didn't thought about looking at the xp chart while creating my character. I'll keep the gift for later then.<br /> <br /> Naive won't work . He might have worked with kids for years, but that doesn't mean that he's seeing the world with rose-tinted glasses. Soft-Hearted could be better, but as Josh said, the flaw as it is written is kinda stupid. And I don't think I'll take it, anyway. Yes, he's used to take care of children, especially since they tend to get hurt all the time with them touching everything, But sometimes, well, they fight, they do stupid things, and they need to have some sort of sanction. And he can't go soft on that, or further sanctions won't mean anything.<br /> <br /> I think I'll take Ward. I didn't think about the brother angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 10-31-2014, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T12:30:50-07:00","id":299183,"title":"","content":"So you're going with Ward and Claustrophobia? That means Aaron is doomed to be kidnapped, or otherwise end up in a sticky situation. And for sure Geoff will have to crawl through dark, tight tunnels. Maybe his life will depend on it. You've also still got loads of freebies left. Are you saving them for something? I like Geoff so far though. I was afraid the Philodox would be a bitchy hard-ass...I guess we've got Hannah for that. I joke...Please don't eat me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T19:25:40-07:00","id":299539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299183#post299183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're going with Ward and Claustrophobia? That means Aaron is doomed to be kidnapped, or otherwise end up in a sticky situation. And for sure Geoff will have to crawl through dark, tight tunnels. Maybe his life will depend on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Val, you silly Ragabash. Never change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299183#post299183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've also still got loads of freebies left. Are you saving them for something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! My sheet wasn't over yet, that's all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299183#post299183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Geoff so far though. I was afraid the Philodox would be a bitchy hard-ass...I guess we've got Hannah for that. I joke...Please don't eat me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassionate justice for the win! (..I should have taken Naive).)<br /> <br /> (And by the way..)<br /> <br /> (She is totally a bitchy hard-ass.)<br /> <br /> Ahem! My character sheet should be almost complete now, <i>except</i> for my character history. I know, I know. But in addition to me being still sick (man, Rubella is FUN to have when you're 23!), my computer suddenly decided to stop working. I've got one for the weekend, but I hope I'll manage to repair my old machine (but I doubt it. Yay for unplanned expenses!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T01:13:58-07:00","id":299812,"title":"","content":"Tsk, tsk Flo. Not completing your character sheet because of a bit of Rubella. What a shameful lack of dedication! Seriously though, Rubella looks <i>nasty</i>. I hope you're getting better. I'd give you a virtual hug, but I wouldn't want to catch anything :-p<br /> <br /> Well Geoff is looking pretty good. Although seriously, his students looked him in a laundry room? Those rats! He shouldv'e eaten them! Never trust children. Grrr. And nice choice of phone. Maybe Val should carry a Blackberry just to balance things out.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks for pointing out all the iffy stuff regarding Garou and homosexuality. I decided to ignore it, Val's got more pressing things to worry about, but it was definitely on my mind. Are you going to make it a major part of Geoff's character? I always thought the conflict between the Litany and love was something worth exploring. Especially if both Garou are the same sex. You don't have to worry about Metis then. At least, I think so.<br /> <br /> Oh boy, Geoff likes sarcasm. Val likes sarcasm. Look how much in common they have! I'm expecting them to try and murder each other after the third conversation.<br /> <br /> And only kissing two boys by the age of 19 isn't so bad...for a loser!<br /> <br /> (I also love how Hannah's already got a...<i>reputation </i>and we haven't even started playing.)<br /> <br /> (I'm also a fan of the creamy spot on Geoff's belly in Crinos form. Between you and Echoes, our pack with be the cutest on Gaia's green earth.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:35:36-08:00","id":299875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299812#post299812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tsk, tsk Flo. Not completing your character sheet because of a bit of Rubella. What a shameful lack of dedication! Seriously though, Rubella looks <i>nasty</i>. I hope you're getting better. I'd give you a virtual hug, but I wouldn't want to catch anything :-p</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's more like a benign form of rubella. Nothing major or too serious. It's a just a pain in the ass, because it keeps me tired and cranky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299812#post299812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, thanks for pointing out all the iffy stuff regarding Garou and homosexuality. I decided to ignore it, Val's got more pressing things to worry about, but it was definitely on my mind. Are you going to make it a major part of Geoff's character? I always thought the conflict between the Litany and love was something worth exploring. Especially if both Garou are the same sex. You don't have to worry about Metis then. At least, I think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't plan on making it a major part, because I don't want geoff to be defined by his sexuality. It's just one of his components. If it comes into play, great. If not, well, that's okay. It's the Apocalypse after all, there's a lot more stuff going on out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=299812#post299812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm also a fan of the creamy spot on Geoff's belly in Crinos form. Between you and Echoes, our pack with be the cutest on Gaia's green earth.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We're gonna fight through the Apocalypse with cuteness and fluffyness \u00e8_\u00e9","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T07:41:51-08:00","id":299990,"title":"","content":"Hey Flo,<br /> <br /> Looks like you've still got 6 freebies unless my count is off, I did just wake up. Defining the background is probably going to get you a clearer picture of where to put them though. I do hope you feel better and get your machine working soon.<br /> <br /> Guys,<br /> <br /> I don't mind Hannah having a reputation out the gate. We're talking mostly high school kids here, and she does have a reputation in those circles. Just remember, Geoff only kind of knows Hannah's Dark Secret, and that's that his brother <i>thinks</i> she ate those people, he might believe it flat out, but my guess is he's never actually asked Hannah or got her side of the story. So unless he just outs Hannah as soon as the game starts, no one<i> really</i> knows.<br /> <br /> Also, if you can't stop primordial evil with adorableness then what's the point in even fighting the apocalypse?<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:28:40-08:00","id":300068,"title":"","content":"<u>Flo</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I need some help, especially with flaws, as I can't seem to find some that would fit Geoff. </div> </div> </div>Oh, dear. This is what I worry about when it comes to allowing flaws. If you can't find any that fit Geoff, then don't take any. You don't need the extra freebie points. Flaws are there to enhance the character, and provide more opportunities for roleplaying. Trying to find flaws that fit just to gain extra freebie points is... not the way to go.<br /> <br /> Damn. I wish I could have posted before this exchange got so far ahead of me. Double-shifts suck. :-(<br /> <br /> OK. Let me start by going over the sheet itself:<br /> <br /> The Pedagogue demeanor? I wasn't expecting that. It's an interesting choice; is Geoff the preachy sort?<br /> <br /> You'll need to pick specialties for Craft and Performance.<br /> <br /> Education is a good choice as an Academics specialty.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm... Natural Science isn't really appropriate as an Expert Knowledge. It falls under the purview of the Science ability. In fact, it kind of combines four of the listed specialties of Science (Biology, Chemistry, Physics and Astronomy), among other things. So, go ahead and drop that; you can put the point in Science instead, or just not spend those freebies.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify: Growl-in-the-Wind is a Rank 3 Garou, which would normally make him a 2-dot Mentor. You can spend only one dot if you want, but in that case he'll be a little less available than he normally would be. I'm fine either way, I just wanted to make sure you were clear on the choice.<br /> <br /> Good choices on the gifts.<br /> <br /> Yes, I will choose certain rites for the character, since he has the Rituals knowledge. However, if you want to choose a few for yourself, you may do so with the Rites background.<br /> <br /> Wow. The Supporter merit is WAY underpriced for what it's supposed to do. -2 difficulty to <i>all</i> social rolls, and +1 total dice pool to any group effort, for only 2 freebie points? How did I not catch that when I was formulating house rules? I <i>really</i> don't like changing rules to the player's detriment once character creation has already started... but that merit is way too powerful for the price. I need to think about this.<br /> <br /> And now we get to the flaws. We'll start with Phobia. I see you've decided to leave it to me to come up with an explanation for his claustrophobia. Well and good, I like open ended mysteries that I can fill in. Why did you choose that particular fear, though? Also, do you understand how debilitating this fear could end up being? There are a lot of foes of the Garou who have a fondness for making their lairs underground, which will usually mean tight spaces. It's not as debilitating as Cynophobia or Nyctophobia would be, but it's pretty close. And remember, if you buy it as a flaw, it's not just a discomfort in small places that can be expressed through role-play or overcome without too much difficulty in an emergency. If you still want Geoff to be claustrophobic, that could be expressed with a flaw like Compulsion (Avoid Enclosed Spaces) or Intolerance (Being In Enclosed Spaces). The Compulsion flaw can be overcome by spending a WP, and the Intolerance flaw adds a difficulty penalty, but will not in and of itself force the character to flee. However, if you fail the willpower roll associated with the Phobia flaw (and remember, you have to get <i>three </i>successes on the roll, not just one), Geoff <i>must</i> flee unless flight is physically impossible or someone has a gift or something that can help him overcome his fear. I won't make you give it up, but I <i>strongly</i> urge you to change it to one of the more manageable alternative flaws I have described above, or choose a different phobia that is easier to manage Maybe Acrophobia (fear of heights), and it was revealed when the kids locked him on the roof? Cleithrophobia, which is the fear of being <i>locked or trapped</i> in an enclosed space could also work, as it is less restrictive form of claustrophobia and would most likely trigger if Geoff was about to be taken prisoner and some such.<br /> <br /> You know, I once played in a Vampire game in which the ST allowed one of my fellow players to take Eosophobia (fear of dawn) as a flaw. I wanted to smack him. :-P<br /> <br /> Ward. I can see a lot of discussion went into this one. The problem with the Ward flaw is that it has a tendency to define the relationship. Any family member or friend of a character (especially teenagers) has the possibility of getting into trouble and needing rescue, but the Ward flaw guarantees it, and guarantees that it'll happen more than once. It also limits the character growth of the NPC in question- unless you choose to buy off the flaw with experience later (or transfer it to another suitable NPC, if one arises in the story), the Ward NPC will always be needing rescue, and I can't develop them into a character that is capable of caring for themselves. So, I urge you to give this some serious thought.<br /> <br /> Remember, you don't HAVE to have flaws. You don't really need the extra freebie points (I think you haven't spent them all yet, and I just pointed out above that you can get two of them back from the Natural Science ability). It's better, generally, to just not have those extra points rather than to force changes to your character to accommodate flaws that don't really fit. However, if you insist, then based on the way you wrote his personality, Shy (W20 pg 477) could be an option, though I'd suggest buying it off later with experience as he grows more confident.<br /> <br /> Anyway, moving on, I'm OK with the Truth Earring fetish and the explanation for it.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the character history. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, thanks for pointing out all the iffy stuff regarding Garou and homosexuality. I decided to ignore it, Val's got more pressing things to worry about, but it was definitely on my mind. Are you going to make it a major part of Geoff's character? I always thought the conflict between the Litany and love was something worth exploring. Especially if both Garou are the same sex. You don't have to worry about Metis then. At least, I think so. </div> </div> </div>It's true that you don't have to worry about Metis, though many garou (especially more conservative ones) would see it as a technical violation of the litany anyway. However, even if it isn't spelled out in the Litany, Garou are also considered to have a social responsibility to take a mate and procreate to perpetuate the species. Deliberately and openly refusing to do so while engaging in acts that cannot possibly result in children could result in a loss of honor renown for both participants, depending on circumstances. These characters are all young yet, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't plan on making it a major part, because I don't want geoff to be defined by his sexuality. It's just one of his components. If it comes into play, great. If not, well, that's okay. It's the Apocalypse after all, there's a lot more stuff going on out there. </div> </div> </div>I don't plan to have any character defined by his or her sexuality, but romance is often an important part of drama, so it certainly has the potential to come up. This is an adult game, after all, and I don't shy away from such things. If Geoff finds himself attracted to and/or in a relationship with an NPC (or another PC, for that matter), these things could come up. Similarly if he finds himself having to reject the advances of a female kinfolk who is attracted to him, but whose feelings he does not (or can not) return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:09:58-08:00","id":300257,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you're going to treat the characters' sexuality as something relevant. I hope this isn't TMI, but a society which regards gay people as threats to social stability and selfish pariahs 'not doing their duty' is a very familiar cutural context for me. So I think it'll be fascinating to roleplay someone thrown into such an environment...and resist it. That's always been the main appeal of White Wolf games for me; exploring different facets of the human experience, seeing existence from a slightly different angle. Ummm...and murdering stuff I guess. <br /> <br /> Yeah, and sorry Flo, I really should have just told you not to pick any flaws if you didn't think they added to your character. But that's why I'm not running this thing. I never even considered how making Aaron a ward would limit his character. Although I DID warn you picking claustrophobia would force Geoff to crawl through icky tunnels. Always trust the Ragabash, it's in the Litany. Honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T13:41:22-08:00","id":300404,"title":"","content":"On the freebies points : I think you all miscounted, but it's my fault guys, I haven't written my points recap in the clearest way. It's fixed now.<br /> <u>Jim</u><br /> There's now specialties for Craft and Performance.<br /> <br /> I changed my Nature and my Demeanor, as I wasn't satisfied with Pedagogue in the first place. Visionary fits better, I think.<br /> <br /> The point of Natural Science was not bought with the freebie, but he went anyway into more Academics. Education is what he's studying right now, and he has a lot of practical experience to back up the theory.<br /> <br /> Okay, on the Merits and Flaws ! First up, I just want to clarify one thing : I don't want to take flaws to have freebie points. In fact, you might haven't noticed, but I took flaws and merits that balance each other, cost-wise. I only took Claustrophobia and Ward to buy Calm Heart and Supporter, because I feel that those two are an important part of Geoff's character. I've looked at all of the other merits, and while most of them are nice, they're not essential to him. And I don't mean gameplay-wise : I don't mind if you houserule Supporter, as long as it still carries the same meaning : that Geoff is a team-player. And I took Calm heart because I don't want him to snap easily : he's a Children of Gaia and a children educator, if he wants to be successful in his mission, he needs to control himself. I really want those two core aspects of his character to be reflected on his sheet, and that's why I'm so bummed about not finding flaws that are suitable to buy those two merits. I really don't care about the freebie points.<br /> For the Claustrophobia, actually, I wasn't really asking you to come up with an explication. I mean, phobias can be unexplained, and I speak from experience : I'm afraid of fire, even though I've never had a trauma related to it. It baffles everyone who hears about it, though. But do as you please! I'm certainly not opposed to more backstory! And you're right : I didn't realize how crippling this flaw can be. I'll settle on Cleithrophobia, I really like the dramatic aspect of it.<br /> And Ward...yeah. I don't like that much. You're right that it locks Aaron into a certain relationship, and I created the jealousy in him because I wanted him to have options to go in many different directions : I can see him becoming a traitor, a trusted ally, a Kinfolk that just want to get a piece of the action, a traumatized teen, even a Skin Dancer... And ward is also an option, albeit one that is kinda boring. But right now, I don't have any other idea for a 3-points flaw. And as I really want Calm heart and Supporter, well...<br /> No, Shy won't work. If you want to work with the kids, you can't be shy, and it's not what I want Geoff to be. So...<br /> <br /> I haven't look into the zodiac merits and flaws yet. I don't have Rage Against the Heavens, so, does anyone have a list of merits and flaws? It could help. :x<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=300068#post300068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's true that you don't have to worry about Metis, though many garou (especially more conservative ones) would see it as a technical violation of the litany anyway. However, even if it isn't spelled out in the Litany, Garou are also considered to have a social responsibility to take a mate and procreate to perpetuate the species. Deliberately and openly refusing to do so while engaging in acts that cannot possibly result in children could result in a loss of honor renown for both participants, depending on circumstances. These characters are all young yet, though.<br /> <br /> I don't plan to have any character defined by his or her sexuality, but romance is often an important part of drama, so it certainly has the potential to come up. This is an adult game, after all, and I don't shy away from such things. If Geoff finds himself attracted to and/or in a relationship with an NPC (or another PC, for that matter), these things could come up. Similarly if he finds himself having to reject the advances of a female kinfolk who is attracted to him, but whose feelings he does not (or can not) return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's exactly what I was thinking. His &quot;inability&quot; to procreate will be a problem in the future, and I'm looking forward to playing it.<br /> <br /> <u>Mark</u><br /> Aaron told his immediate family (his parents and his brother), but Geoff, while horrified, has trouble believing that the queen bee from his former high school is also a Garou, and one that eat people. Both of the brothers haven't told anyone else yet ; Aaron is terrified, and Geoff just don't see the point of spreading what could be a false rumor. Besides, he doesn't even know the girl, outside from her reputation in high school. He has never met her! And as for outing her right away... I can assure you that it won't be the case. It wouldn't be interesting for any of us. But using this information to blackmail her, however...Huh...I'll think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-03-2014, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:52:51-08:00","id":301026,"title":"","content":"Well the flaw for Tambiyah is...um. Yeah. It's called 'Incorrigible Flirt' (two points) and it works as follows: You feel compelled to flirt with anyone you find attractive. You must spend a Willpower point to resist this desire. Furthermore, your Willpower is considered one point lower when 'potential mates' attempt to use supernatural powers to bend you to their will. <br /> <br /> None of the Zodiac flaws really fit Geoff. There's one where you feel compelled to stuff your face with food when faced with a stressful situation. And 'food' includes human flesh. Another flaw is basically lethargy, you find it very difficult to motivate yourself. Yet another one marks you as inherently suspicious. No matter what you do, people will assume you're up to something and treat you accordingly. <br /> <br /> Nothing else really jumps out at me, but I'm trying to match things with Geoff's personality. <br /> <br /> I'm personally a fan of the flaw which makes your character suspect everyone's in some sort of conspiracy, and assume they've all got ulterior motives. Not sure it fits for Geoff though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:02:39-08:00","id":301177,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, sorry for the wait, I've been recovering from Halloween. <u><br /> <br /> Josh</u><br /> That's the idea. ;D Her demeanor's not a 'front', per se, but more of a remnant of what she once was. Her desire to terrify things is new, and uncertain. Depending on how things go, her nature might flip back into being a caregiver, or even change into something entirely different.<br /> <br /> <u>Jim</u><br /> Hm, maybe she could've gotten it from Quiet Storm, perhaps as a gift or reward for helping her with rituals? Not that they're close friends or anything - I imagine Echoes would mostly have been sent off on menial tasks, like collecting herbs needed for the rites and so on. This could also explain why Echoes became so adept at performing rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:12:54-08:00","id":301183,"title":"","content":"I'm on the road right now, so I'll write a proper reply later, but I wanted to shoot out this quickie to you, Flo, as you seem to be laboring under a misapprehension. You do not need to balance merits and flaws. Merits can be paid for with regular freebie points, whether you take flaws or not. So, you can have the merits that fit Geoff without having to force-fit flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:05:49-08:00","id":301634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=300257#post300257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this isn't TMI, but a society which regards gay people as threats to social stability and selfish pariahs 'not doing their duty' is a very familiar cutural context for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what Scott thinks is a threat to social stability? Werewolf on werewolf nookie! If you're going to be gay, go find a mortal or kin to do it but keep it out of the Pack!<br /> <br /> (Note that I'm not sure that homosexuality amongst Garou is actually a bad thing in this setting. I know in Werewolf the Forsaken one of the laws of the Uratha was that you couldn't get it on with your pack mates or other werewolves, as it was some sort of spiritual incest. I don't know if Apocalypse has that though, or to the same extent.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:45:21-08:00","id":301891,"title":"","content":"You think so, banana boy? Well if Scott's got a problem, maybe Val should socially destabilize his HEAD! <br /> <br /> (And I don't know about the spiritual incest angle. But there'e plenty of <i>Werewolf </i>books I haven't read, so who knows? The issue mainly seemed to be the creation of metis...and there are a surprising number of them around, so clearly someone isn't paying attention to the Litany. I personally think the writers didn't quite know how to deal with homosexuality in this context. It's most extensively discussed in the novel <i>Breathe Deeply, </i>which concludes 'eh, whatever floats your boat.' This may have more to do with the author than anything else though. Strangely, one of the characters in the <i>Book of Auspices</i> believes that the most 'honorable' relationship between high-rage garou is a same-sex one. And then there's Children of Gaia revised, which I won't go into because everyone hates it. Honestly, I'm just surprised the issue was brought up at all. So good job White Wolf! Man, with a few more sources, I could write a dissertation on this stuff.)<br /> <br /> PS: When you gonna finish your character sheet, yo? I'm still not sure what Scott looks like!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T06:59:51-08:00","id":302106,"title":"","content":"This is my first time playing Werewolf the Apocalypse and I haven't read a whole lot, but I did read and play some Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, sex between werewolves was the equivalent of incest. Lets thing on incest. Huge social stigma surrounding it, rooted in the negative reproductive impact. But is it okay if you just have oral sex? What if one of you are infertile? What if it's a homosexual relationship? Odds are that in our culture, no one is going to see it as alright to bang your sister just because she used birth control, or to get with your brother because &quot;gay makes it okay&quot;. In Forsaken it was pretty much like that. Getting it on at all with another werewolf was like &quot;spiritual incest&quot;, and even if you didn't produce a spirit child (there were not metis), it still didn't make it okay in the eyes of everyone else. <br /> <br /> That's just &quot;can two werewolves do it if they're gay&quot; though. Then there is the whole reproductive aspect of whether or not a werewolf should even be gay because it seriously cuts in their ability to produce offspring. This issue sort of exists in Exalted, where the Dragon-Blooded get their power through heritage sort of like werewolves. In the setting, producing at least a couple offspring was seen as your duty if you're a Dragon-Blooded, and a lot of Dragon-Blooded culture is influenced by eastern mindset. I think both Apocalypse and Forsaken have that &quot;duty to reproduce&quot; thing too. <br /> <br /> In American culture, we see sex as a real personal decision. It's like coffee, you get it how you want it and to hell with people who try and make you drink stuff you don't like. But in some cultures, duty and responsibility can mean more than individual desires and there is honor in placing the needs of your family above yourself. As much as they probably wouldn't like it to be thrown in their face, the Garou Nation is just as diverse and widespread as humanity is, and with different breeds, perhaps even more so than human culture would ever be. So it would make sense for me for there to be a lot of different views on sex, duty, and reproductive responsibility just like they have different views on *everything*.<br /> <br /> Personally, it doesn't surprise me that the writers of Werewolf the Apocalypse (or any game) would address homosexuality. It's not the '60s anymore, and I think part of it being a mature game is putting issues on the table, even if an individual game might not have any reason to address it. As far as what Scott would think, I'm not actually sure. I only assumed that the &quot;no werewolf nookie even if you're gay&quot; thing from Forsaken also applied to Apocalypse, but maybe they don't have as much of the &quot;spiritual incest&quot; factor that Forsaken did. The Tribes in Forsaken are much, much closer in mindset than the very diverse tribes in Apocalypse. I'd have to read more of the Stargazers tribebook to see if there are any clues as to what sort of mindset his mentor would have instilled in him. I know his upbringing would be uh...as &quot;against&quot; such things.<br /> <br /> (As for what Scott looks like, I didn't write it up yet because I have two ideas floating around in my head and I haven't decided yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:33:05-08:00","id":302219,"title":"","content":"Unless it's in some random book, which it very well may be, the subject of homosexuality and W:tA isn't something nearly as stressed as it is in W:tF. W:tF puts it right in the core book up front, and makes sure it's a theme in the slapts, W:tA not so much. I know there's a few gay Garou couples scattered in some of the fluff (most notable Tribe Book CoG), but I don't even remember how that's handled, I just know it's there. That being said, I think it's left pretty openly vague for the ST to fill in, and it's probably one of those things that's meant to vary based on who you ask. I say that because it's not technically a violation of the litany; let's break it down.<br /> <br /> Garou shall not mate with Garou<br /> <br /> Mate is in this case a verb, the thing that is being done. Let's use some dictionary powers.<br /> <br /> <i>verb</i> verb: <b>mate</b>; 3rd person present: <b>mates</b>; past tense: <b>mated</b>; past participle: <b>mated</b>; gerund or present participle: <b>mating</b><ul><li> <b>1</b>.<br /> (of animals or birds) come together for breeding; copulate.<br /> &quot;successful males may <b>mate with</b> many females&quot;<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_vk_tbl text_table_vk_gy\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_vk_tbl_tr text_table_vk_gy_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_lr_dct_nyms_ttl text_table_vk_tbl_td text_table_vk_gy_td\">synonyms:</td> <td class=\"text_table_vk_tbl_td text_table_vk_gy_td\"><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?biw=1920&amp;bih=969&amp;q=define+breed&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=0_tYVN60E4e2yQS56ILABA&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=0CDcQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">breed</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?biw=1920&amp;bih=969&amp;q=define+couple&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=0_tYVN60E4e2yQS56ILABA&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=0CDgQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">couple</a>, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?biw=1920&amp;bih=969&amp;q=define+copulate&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=0_tYVN60E4e2yQS56ILABA&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=0CDkQ_SowAA\" target=\"_blank\">copulate</a> &quot;pandas rarely mate in captivity&quot;<br /> <br /> </td> </tr> </table></div> <ul><li> bring (animals or birds) together for breeding.</li> <li> join in marriage or sexual partnership.<br /> &quot;people tend to <b>mate with</b> others in their own social class&quot;</li> </ul></li> <li> <b>2</b>.<br /> connect or be connected mechanically.<br /> &quot;a four-cylinder engine <b>mated to</b> a five-speed gearbox&quot;</li> </ul><br /> The emphasis is mainly on the breeding part. Sure, it's kind of evolved into a way to say married or be partnered with, but that's kind of an afterthought when it comes to the words etiology. It's a derivative of what it means to mate, rather than the meaning itself. Especially when we consider just how damn old the Litany is.<br /> <br /> Not compelling enough, let's look at the justification for why Garou shall not mate with Garou: <b>The Law:</b> Werewolves should mate only with humans or wolves. Because metis offspring are deformed, twisted or even insane, Garou are forbidden to mate with their own kind. Of course, this law is enforced largely because of age-old prejudices against metis. This stricture forms the basis for some of the greatest tragedies of Garou culture. Galliards have been known to move listeners to tears by telling ballads of two werewolves who fall in love and can never express their passion\u2026 or who do so at the cost of their lives.<br /> <b>The Reality</b>: The number of metis in Garou culture is increasing steadily, showing that this law is not as inviolate as it once was. A handful of tribes claim to actually be kinder to their metis than others. Unfortunately, these claims are often little more than tactics used to recruit and exploit metis for tasks lupus and homids would just as soon avoid.<br /> <br /> The problem here is squarely about the Metis. It's the only thing outright mentioned as a justification of a violation of the Litany.<br /> <br /> So, I can pretty plainly see what the Litany is trying to say is this.<br /> <br /> Garou shall not produce offspring with other Garou.<br /> <br /> So where does that leave us. If two Garou get it on, is it a violation of the Litany if there can be no offspring? Well only if you decide that Garou also have a duty to produce healthy offspring, which can only be done with kinfolk really. Such a thing might be seen as a waste of time and effort to the extreme, just as much as mating with a infertile kinfolk. But if that's the argument it's not about homosexuality anymore, and it's still skirting the spirit of the law when it comes to the Litany.<br /> <br /> So the only way it's a violation is by the letter of the law, which is probably a stance each Garou has to have individually, as each tribe, breed, auspice, and individual interprets it slightly differently anyway.<br /> So the answer is, there are as many answers as there are Garou, and that all Garou regardless of being gay should do two things, not make Metis, and bare the burden of breeding healthy offspring.<br /> <br /> -Mark<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:56:52-08:00","id":302253,"title":"","content":"That's why I compared it to incest. Incest is a big taboo in most human cultures, which does have a practical component. But to say that incest is all about offspring it could produce would really be a poor explanation, because the stigma would apply even to say, an incestuous homosexual couple that couldn't produce offspring (or a heterosexual couple likewise unable to produce them). This was much clearer in Werewolf the Forsaken, where the <i>purpose </i>of the law is to prevent heterosexual werewolf couples from producing spirit children (which are deranged, evil, and murderous), and the <i>tradition </i>of the law which stigmatizes it regardless of whether offspring could be produced from the specific union in question. So even if a homosexual werewolf couple in Forsaken couldn't create a spirit child (and thus threaten the lives of all packs in the area), it was still as forbidden as if the couple were heterosexual on a basis of it being a taboo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:09:45-08:00","id":302277,"title":"","content":"The problem with that is that incest itself is already seen as taboo in W:tA, it's basically the stigma that plagues the Silver Fangs, accusations of inbreeding run rampant. Incest is already looked down upon. Garou mating is a separate things; incest and garou mating are not a co-joined concept. They are in W:tF because there is a direct result from it regardless of gender. Cause and effect so to speak. However in W:tA, the direct result of Werewolf pairing is Metis, which is not a problem in homosexual relationships.<br /> <br /> The litany doesn't say anything about it being linked to incest, the taboo is that metis could be bred. The only other argument is that some garou find it icky. Probably due to the long standing cultural norm that garou mating ends with metis. Not because all garou are spiritual brothers and sisters, and therefore all garou mating is spiritual incest.<br /> <br /> In the context of what we're talking about, imagine that W:tF didn't exist. Without the idea of W:tF in the picture, you're only left to argue the litany itself, and as I pointed out, the litany is pretty clear on why Garou shouldn't mate; and it has nothing to even say on homosexuality.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:49:12-08:00","id":302379,"title":"","content":"Hare Rama, look what I've started. As I mentioned above, in <i>Breathe Deeply</i>, there'e two (lengthy) diatribes about why homophobia is BAD! Incidentally, one of the major characters is a gay Stargazer* (just sayin'!) This character (Thunder Tiger) mentions that homosexuality has always existed among the tribes, it just hasn't been discussed much because the writers...Uh, I mean because Gaia hasn't willed it. Apparently Shadow Lords do it in secret rituals. You are free to speculate. And weirdly, the book suggests the Get of Fenris are really into man-love, just don't say it, or they'll eat your face. This sentiment is echoed in the <i>Book of Auspices</i>, the Children of Gaia Tribebook, and sorta fits with their whole Nordic theme. Sort of. And homosexual behavior among wolves is well documented, even if it makes some zoologists uncomfortable. So what I'm trying to say is...I'm not really sure, I'm just fascinated by this stuff. <br /> <br /> I personally think garou dislike (exclusive) homosexuality not because they think it's ikcy, but because it impedes breeding and the propagation of the nation. To be gay is to be selfish. At least according to the garou enforcing the laws. <br /> <br /> This is still a big thing in India. Marriage is seen as something you do not for yourself, but your whole extended family. The creation of children is considered the duty of all human beings,** and the celebration of fertility is prominent in many religious texts***. Because if there's one thing India needs, it's more people. There are still cases of both same-sex and opposite-sex couples committing joint suicide to avoid being forced into arranged marriages. They argue it''s better to be united in death, than separated in life.<br /> <br /> But then there'e Brahmanic, Jain and Buddhist texts which treat homo/bisexuality as just something that happens. Jain texts even distinguish between gender and sex as early as the 5th Century AD! Not that this is really relevant to werewolves, I just think it's interesting. <br /> <br /> <br /> Who cares about the Wyrm when you can spend all night discussing sexuality? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Or would that be StarGAYzer? Sorry, couldn't resist. <br /> <br /> ** Well, according to SOME schools of Hinduism. It's a complicated religion. <br /> <br /> *** Including the ones where two women make a baby without male intervention<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Why did Mark's post only appear after I posted? Hayaraba! I hate technology -_-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 11-04-2014, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:12:40-08:00","id":302420,"title":"","content":"I think you might be reading a bit past my point, Mark. In W:tF I don't believe homosexual couples could produce spirit children, but it was still a social stigma because that was just how the culture worked. So even if in W:tA homosexual werewolf couples can't produce metis, that doesn't necessarily mean that there isn't a social stigma attached to it either. I *know* that in W:tF the Uratha were &quot;spiritual brothers and sisters&quot; which was more important to most than the practical reasons (ie producing spirit children). I *don't know* if in W:tA there is a similar restriction on inter-werewolf relations. It sounds like you're telling me that they're more practical and don't have any social implications of such a relationship as long as no metis are produced. So if that is the case, then it's good for me to know. I mentioned earlier that Scott would want werewolf nookie to be &quot;out of the pack&quot;, but if no one in W:tA cares about werewolf nookie then he wouldn't either.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about isn't really incest or homosexuality: it's <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRdfX7ut8gw\" target=\"_blank\">tradition</a>. Most traditions start for some practical or pseudo-practical purpose, but just because a tradition isn't practical anymore doesn't mean that people (like Scott) won't keep the tradition anyways! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: I saw your reply too Josh. That's what I was saying about how different cultures have different views on duty of marriage, procreation, and what sex means in a person's life. I'm also interested in the cultural diversity, and I think that it's an interesting thing in W:tA where the tribes are so different from each other. In W:tF, the tribes were all like I said, very similar in outlook but different in methods. I think trying to be a &quot;Bridge Between People&quot; for so many unique groups will be a fun part of playing this game for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3789,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","user":"DeathmatchFM","date":". 11-04-2014, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:21:27-08:00","id":302465,"title":"","content":"My point was always more along the line of that homosexuality isn't actually a violation of the Litany. Nor in any of the Renoun charts is it discussed being gay is bad and will lose you renoun. However, that there is a clear stigma around it, and it is from a tradition, but the root of that tradition is that pairings of Garou could result in metis. So by the year 2014, it's probably a issue that's still being worked out by the Garou Nation as a whole. There's no rule that flat out say, &quot;hey, gay is wrong,&quot; there's a rule that implies that Garou shouldn't bring metis into the world. That rule thus implies that Garou should have strong healthy offspring, and all Garou should be duty bound to do so.<br /> <br /> But that's all a formed tradition that started with a rule about not producing metis. I'm not saying you won't be judged for being gay, or that Werewolf society has no stance on it, just that the stance can probably universally be seen as up to interpretation with little argument by those Garou with a more liberal mindset. There are probably plenty of conservative Garou who will see the letter of the law, and agrue that. The point is that it's down to interpretation, there's no one hardline stance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:38:36-08:00","id":302477,"title":"","content":"That's a little disappointing. Sticking to the letter of the law instead of the spirit removes a lot of the potential conflict, especially when the appropriate response is &quot;lol that's not RAW&quot; when discussing a controversial topic. That's something that I really liked about W:tF. There was a clear stance on how most things were and where the community as a whole stood, but individuals still questioned the practicality of ancient traditions and it built storytelling conflict around whether or not the Uratha were entering a new age or if keeping traditions had more value than meets the eye. So with that in mind, Scott's view will probably just be &quot;well if it's not explicitly prohibited it must be allowed&quot; for most things. I also have faith that our ST will still make things engaging through various NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:57:30-08:00","id":302505,"title":"","content":"But every tribe, and every sept and every camp has their own view on things. So Scott might think something's allowed, but based on what? Inevitably, someone will disagree with you. I actually don't think Werewolf: the Apocalypse is diverse enough when it comes to conflicting philosophies. So Forsaken would probably seem staid to me. See, we've just disagreed on that. Trust me, there'll be plenty of conflict, stemming from individuals who all want to do things their way. And I'm not quite sure what you find dissappointing, the fact that the garou don't have a universal stance on things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T15:20:10-08:00","id":302714,"title":"","content":"I'm disappointed that they *don't* have diverse enough opinions. In W:tF, there was a commonly accepted way any tradition was interpreted but there was always room to argue it. The way that it sounds, there is a single &quot;RAW&quot; interpretation of Garou traditions and if &quot;it's not explicitly denied it's accepted&quot;, which actually leaves very little room to debate what is appropriate for the Garou Nation. For example, in W:tF werewolf couples were disallowed, even if they couldn't produce spirit children. This was the rule, and this was the tradition, but people challenged it on the basis of whether or not you should uphold a tradition that wasn't practical. It sounds like in W:tA, if a tradition is not practical it's not implemented. Maybe I'm reading into what was said the wrong way. If every tribe, sept, and camp has their own view, then that would make me feel better.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the entire W20 book though so doing that could probably clear up some confusion I have. I've neglected to do it though because there is a lot of information there that I think I'd enjoy experiencing in character rather than having checked up on the setting earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T00:12:29-08:00","id":303038,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, if you're new to all this, than maybe this was a bit of information overload. Forget the Litany, the most important thing is that garou must protect Gaia, and by extension, fight the Wyrm. So, let's ask each of the tribes the question, 'How do we fight the Wyrm?' We'll start with the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers</b>: The Wyrm isn't the true enemy, the Weaver is. She traps us in a web of delusion, and only by understanding this can we liberate ourselves from her illusions. Garou must spread this message to all people, this is Gaia's will.<br /> <br /> <b>Get of Fenris</b>: What a load of shit! The Wyrm is the real problem. But we've gotta prepare ourselves for Ragnarok, the Final Battle, otherwise, the Wyrm will win, and everything will end. So stop all the meditating and pseudo-mystical bullcrap, pick up a weapon and <i>fight</i>!<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers</b>: No, no, the Stargazer\u2019s are onto something. The Weaver is always getting ignored, but maybe she\u2019s our key to success! Forget the wilderness, if we work inside cities, we can change civilization from within! And it\u2019s the Weaver who\u2019ll show us the way, not the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons</b>: Miserable little <i>charach</i>! How dare you suggest we abandon the wild places? You betray Gaia! So long as green places exist, the Wyrm cannot win. When the world is smothered in the stinking corruption of mankind, then you will rue your mistake!<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers</b>: Aw, what\u2019s wrong wolfey, fleas biting? Ha! You dogs are all stupid, \u2018specially you Get-boy. There\u2019s no grand design to fightin\u2019 the Wyrm. You just gotta do what you can when you can. The cities are the best place, \u2018cause that\u2019s where all the real rotten stuff is. But forget the Weaver, do it for Gaia. It\u2019s all we can do.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies</b>: What a pathetic, defeatist attitude. Have you forgotten you\u2019re a wolf and not a mangy cur scrounging for scraps? We must protect the wild places, Gaia entrusted us with this sacred task. If we tend Her groves, then Her spirit endures. The Red Talons understand this. But, there is a second duty. So long as womankind remains oppressed from east to west, the Wyrm will win. It feeds on woman\u2019s suffering, and if we lessen it, we will strike a great blow against the Destroyer!<br /> <br /> <b>Uktena</b>: Ah yes, <i>womankind</i>, because apparently men can\u2019t be oppressed. Bah, what do you know about suffering anyway, white woman? If only you saw as we did, then you\u2019d weep and never cease. But enough of this. The Wyrm can be stopped, if we make sacrifices, if we truly <i>give </i>of ourselves, as our Middle Brother did. There is something, some secret, that will allow us to save Gaia, but why bother enlisting your aid in searching for it? No one ever understands.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia</b>: But we <i>must</i> work together! It is the only thing that will save us from the coming darkness! Unity is our strength. If we put aside our old grievances and unite as one, nothing will stand before us. Don\u2019t serve the Weaver or the Wyld, serve only Gaia, spread her love to all sentient beings, and the Wyrm will simply shrivel up and fade away. But we can only do this <i>together</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b>: Quite correct, we must unite. Thankfully, Gaia has already marked those who will bear the burden of leadership: Us. No, please, don\u2019t bow\u2026Alright, maybe just once. Gather under the banner of the Silver Fangs fellow Garou, and we will lead you to victory.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Lords</b>: <i>Yeees</i>\u2026Of course we shall unite with you brothers, of course. I wonder though, are you so certain Gaia appointed you as our kings? For we have heard a different story, and in fact, you might be surprised to learn who is <i>truly</i> destined to lead the Nation\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Wendigo</b>: Typical whitey squabbling. Leave us out of it. We shall serve Gaia as we always have, before you so kindly gave us your\u2026<i>civilization</i>. Pray our efforts are enough. Likely we will fail. So be it. Let it all end, and may the Wyrm choke on us!<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders</b>: Geez, what did I miss? Sorry, I was\u2026<i>elsewhere</i>. You wanna know how to fight the Wyrm? Umm\u2026I\u2019ll get back to you, I\u2019ve gotta visit someone. In Myanmar. Before I go though, I\u2019ve gotta tell you guys, you\u2019re almost there, but maybe stop looking inwards, and look outside for once. Where did I hear it? Oh, a friend. Just a friend.<br /> <br /> <b>Fianna</b>: Sigh. It\u2019s a funny old world, and there\u2019s not enough to drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now if that's not diverse, I don't know what is. And that's only the tribes, not camps or even individual opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 11-05-2014, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T15:28:41-08:00","id":303780,"title":"","content":"Just a quick addendum to Josh's post, I know this is obvious but I'm going to say it anyway.<br /> <br /> That's a very fun and clever way of showing the diversity, but those are very broad generalizations. The only real correction I would add though is that the Stazgazers as a whole do not think the Weaver is a problem, that's a large camp in the tribe mostly made up of Lupus. =p<br /> <br /> Sorry to be nitpicky,<br /> Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 11-05-2014, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T23:17:29-08:00","id":304221,"title":"","content":"Really? I based everything on The Player's Guide to Garou, and it suggested the Stargazer's wanted to escape from the Weaver's web to embrace 'the True Gaia Realm' (whatever the hell that is) I guess that must have been revised at a later date. How annoying. I thought it was a really cool philosophy. Anyway, I just wanted to reassure Jame's that there's plenty of diversity in the Garou Nation, werewolves aren't all drones mindlessly adhering to the Litany. Just some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:28:29-08:00","id":304622,"title":"","content":"See? This is why I didn't want Geoff's homosexuality to be a big deal! It has given birth to a big page of debate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=301183#post301183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm on the road right now, so I'll write a proper reply later, but I wanted to shoot out this quickie to you, Flo, as you seem to be laboring under a misapprehension. You do not need to balance merits and flaws. Merits can be paid for with regular freebie points, whether you take flaws or not. So, you can have the merits that fit Geoff without having to force-fit flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh. Ooooooooooooh.<br /> Ahem. I'll go...hem. finish up my character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:00:52-08:00","id":304652,"title":"","content":"Josh,<br /> <br /> I was basing what I said about the Stargazers on their rev Tribe Book. There's a lot of talk that many Gazers have a theory about the Weaver, and they even have some bits from that perspective thrown in there, but it's far from the main focus of the tribe. What they do focus on is achieving the middle way, balancing their inner wolf-ness and man-ness, their rage and gnosis. One of the best ways to do this is to become ascetic and contemplative. Which is definitely anti-weaver, and a lot of them don't like it, but that's just a byproduct of the middle way. The fun contradiction though is that if they ever actually achieve enlightenment, it removes them from the wheel of ages though, so no Stargazer actually wants to become enlightened, it would be like taking the easy way out of the fight for Gaia and thus giving up your duty selfishly.<br /> <br /> And Flo,<br /> <br /> I didn't take it as a big deal, just a chance to wax philosophical about the Litany. A spirted debate on what the Litany actually says and means on any given subject is par for the theme of Apoc and should warrant a big page of debate. =p<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 11-06-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:20:02-08:00","id":304669,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay, thank you for the clarification. I don't have the Stargazers' Tribebook alas. It sounds like typical White Wolf contradiction. Like how the Black Spiral Dancers are actually presented as misunderstood ascetics who want to extinguish their 'Urge' and reunite with the 'Soul of All' and thus escape a world of pain and separation...And yet at the same time BSD's are slavering maniacs who do all manner of iffy things to further the ends of corruption and decay. It's weird. But I like it. Any view could be correct. Or none of them. <br /> <br /> And Flo, all the best White Wolf games devolve into philosophical diatribes about the real-world impact of fictional beings. Join us next week as we discuss the Litany injunction to 'Not suffer the People to tend thy sickness.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:19:53-08:00","id":304696,"title":"","content":"Alright. I've finished my character sheet, and it's a bit anti-climatic, as I mostly copied and pasted what I've already written in the recruitment post. I don't think I've forgotten any details on Geoff's life...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:00:13-08:00","id":304736,"title":"","content":"Wooo, that means we've all done our character sheets...Except for someone who shall remain nameless (Gaia knows who you are). Regrading Geoff, I have questions about his back-story. Did the Pentex First Team arrive at the Daycare center to abduct Geoff? How could he have become a Dancer? And what exactly happened between Geoff and his dad? Did he attack him? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:26:15-08:00","id":304758,"title":"","content":"Not the First Team, necessarily. They weren't expecting to face a Garou, they thought they would only meet one or two poor humans. They didn't say they wanted to make Geoff a Dancer, but he's sure that if he had been kidnapped and they found out they had a Garou in their hands, they would have made him dance the Spiral. He doesn't actually know how those things work, but that's enough for him.<br /> When Geoff experienced his First Change, he slaughtered the men that tried to abduct them. In his rage, he attacked everything, and broke a few doors and walls. He actually mistook his dad for one of his foes, and tried to attack him, only to be distracted by bullets coming from one of the Pentex goons. Mark took this chance to run and hide in a locked closet, where he called his bro' for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:11:27-08:00","id":304863,"title":"","content":"Cool. It makes sense for Geoff to have some knowledge of the BSD as both his parents are kinfolk. Although I do wonder how much knowledge the average Garou has about the Wyrm, the Labyrinth, the Urge, the Center of All Mysteries etc. etc. If Geoff experienced his First Change confronting the Wyrm's minions, he'll have very different opinions on the Dancers than Val, who has a distorted (and sympathetic) conception of them. <br /> <br /> (Also, a general question. Can you <i>make </i>someone dance the Spiral? I thought it had to be a conscious choice or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:33:10-08:00","id":304904,"title":"","content":"Geoff didn't have his knowledge of the BSD from his parents, but rather from his uncle. His parents tried to keep him and his brother in the dark, but, well...it didn't work. So, when Steve picked him up after his First Change, he explained to him what he had just escaped.<br /> <br /> And I think that given time, Pentex or the BSD have the means to make anybody dance the Spiral, by breaking their spirits or something. At least, Geoff thinks so. He's aware that he's not some sort of saint, boddhisvata or whatever, and that he <i>would</i> have danced, sooner or later.<br /> <br /> And yes, he'll be sympathetic to Val, who seems kinda lost, but his sympathy to the BSD? No way. This is <i>not</i> something he'll joke about. It's too soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:10:59-08:00","id":304933,"title":"","content":"Wow. Looks like I missed a big discussion again. Let me start at the beginning.<br /> <br /> <u>Flo</u><br /> <br /> The Craft and Performance specialties look good.<br /> <br /> The character sheet looks good for the most part, but I count one too many dots in Knowledges. Should be 10 (nine, plus the one dot of rituals bought with freebies), and I count 11. Also, you spent a freebie on Fetish that you didn't need to; you only have five dots of backgrounds.<br /> <br /> <u>Eve</u><br /> <br /> I'm OK with the fetish being a gift from Quiet Storm. However, are you certain that you want to spend the point on it? It is possible to communicate while in Lupus. Speech in the Garou tongue is possible, and speech in human languages can be accomplished by partially shapeshifting the larynx. Difficult (difficulty 9 on a Dex or Sta + Primal Urge roll, if memory serves), but doable.<br /> <br /> <u>Josh</u><br /> <br /> Yes, a person can be forced to dance the Spiral. It usually drives you nuts (just like it does the people who dance it voluntarily).<br /> <br /> <u>Everybody</u><br /> <br /> OK, looks like I missed a hell of a discussion on the nature of the Garou Nation's view on homosexuality. My opinion is...<br /> <br /> ...something I'm not going to tell you! :-P The fact is, your characters are all cubs just being initiated into the Nation. The subject of homosexuality is, quite frankly, something that is unlikely to have come up during your training, unless your character specifically brought it up. You'll have a chance to see how the various groups and individuals within the Garou Nation that you encounter handle the issue as it comes up during the course of play. Just know that I do have my own ideas on the subject. Some people take a pragmatic view, as Mark has suggested. Others take a traditionalist view, as James suggested. I won't make generalizations here, though.<br /> <br /> Now, let me take a look at the character sheets and see what still needs to be done.<br /> <br /> <b>Mark/Hannah-</b> We still need to pick a garou astrological sign. Do you have access to Rage Across the Heavens? If not, I can work with you on it. I have a suggestion that I think fits Hannah very well, but if you have your own idea I don't want to push it.<br /> <br /> <b>James/Scott-</b> Looks like we're still mostly waiting on the backstory/appearance details. Everything else looks good, unless you still planned to change Reluctant Warrior from a Zodiac flaw to a Mental flaw. Remember that this isn't really necessary; the influence of the planet could be seen in the light of your explanation.<br /> <br /> <b>Josh/Val-</b> The character sheet looks ready to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Flo/Geoff-</b> Besides the notes I mentioned above, I think we're ready.<br /> <br /> <b>Eve/Stir of Echoes-</b> Looks good except for the astrological sign. Do you have access to Rage Across the Heavens? If not, I can work with you on it.<br /> <br /> Now, one more thing to discuss. I received a PM from someone who wants to join our group. I am willing to have a sixth player, but since we are so close to being ready to begin, I didn't want to delay us to incorporate another PC unless that was what you guys wanted as well. So, I put the decision to the five of you- should I allow this individual to join us, or should I consider the game closed to new members for now?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 11-06-2014, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:14:04-08:00","id":304937,"title":"","content":"As the one in question who PMed, I was that guy. I had fired of a response saying it was no longer necessary, as I finally assembled a group in Helsinki, and will be playing live. However, I am the &quot;always an ST, never a PC&quot; type. Everyone would rather I run games. So I wouldn't <i>mind</i> joining an external group, but at the same time, feel free to just fire off a &quot;we have too many, and it just be awkward&quot; note. Thanks for the opportunity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:44:58-08:00","id":304963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=304933#post304933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Flo</u><br /> <br /> The Craft and Performance specialties look good.<br /> <br /> The character sheet looks good for the most part, but I count one too many dots in Knowledges. Should be 10 (nine, plus the one dot of rituals bought with freebies), and I count 11. Also, you spent a freebie on Fetish that you didn't need to; you only have five dots of backgrounds.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Woops, you're right on Knowledges. I removed the point in computer. I let the freebie point on Fetish, but I've decided to switch my fifth dot of background to Totem, and that makes two.<br /> <br /> And hi Rall!<br /> Honestly, I'm down with whatever you all decide. The more the merrier! And we have a full circle with all aspects already taken, so you can choose whatever you want. Do you already have a character concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:27:23-08:00","id":304987,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is gonna make me sound like a total pedant, but I'm thoroughly confused about the Black Spiral thing. In 'The Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth,' it's implied that to contact the Wyrm one must perform an actual dance. Furthermore, they must seek to confront their Urge, otherwise the ritual will fail. Now I can understand a garou being told &quot;Perform this rite or die!&quot; But how could they confront their Urge if they secretly didn't want to? And if a garou is adamant that they will not take part in the ritual, how could they be forced to dance?<br /> <br /> And hi Rall! This will make me sound like jerk, but I'm going to be honest. We seem to be close to starting our game, and if you can get a first draft of your character sheet done within a few days, cool. Otherwise it's unfair to make the rest of the players wait while you flesh out your character. But I guess I <i>am</i> the Contrary, so I'll wait to see what everyone else says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:36:43-08:00","id":305016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=304987#post304987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this is gonna make me sound like a total pedant, but I'm thoroughly confused about the Black Spiral thing. In 'The Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth,' it's implied that to contact the Wyrm one must perform an actual dance. Furthermore, they must seek to confront their Urge, otherwise the ritual will fail. Now I can understand a garou being told &quot;Perform this rite or die!&quot; But how could they confront their Urge if they secretly didn't want to? And if a garou is adamant that they will not take part in the ritual, how could they be forced to dance?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's lots of contradictory material. I prefer the version put forth in the Book of the Wyrm Second Edition, which describes (among other things) hurling captive Garou into the Black Spiral, at which point they have no choice but to experience it, which in turn shatters their sanity.<br /> <br /> The moral of the story- don't let them take you alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:32:55-08:00","id":305127,"title":"","content":"<u>Astrology/Fetish</u><br /> I'll keep the fetish. Who knows, it might come in handy in the future when she doesn't have the time to shapeshift. As for her sign, I admit, I was leaning towards Rorg, but it doesn't look like that's available to new characters? In the meantime, I picked Hakahe. I think that fits her well.<br /> <br /> <u>Rall</u><br /> Hey there! I'm all for adding another character, but I'd also like to start the game soon. D;<br /> <br /> Maybe we can do a compromise? They could join in shortly after the game begins, if the character isn't ready by then? Our group could stumble across his character during the Rite, or an Elder/etc. could stroll up just before they head off to say &quot;Oh, by the way, this guy's joining y'all.&quot; Or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:13:21-08:00","id":305147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305127#post305127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Astrology/Fetish</u><br /> I'll keep the fetish. Who knows, it might come in handy in the future when she doesn't have the time to shapeshift. As for her sign, I admit, I was leaning towards Rorg, but it doesn't look like that's available to new characters? In the meantime, I picked Hakahe. I think that fits her well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;available to new characters.&quot; It represents either the sign your character was born or experienced first chane under. It's meant primarily for RP purposes and has almost no mechanical impact. So, go with Hakahe or Rorg, as you like, whichever you would prefer. I was looking at those two for Stir of Echoes myself, to be honest. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Rall</u><br /> Hey there! I'm all for adding another character, but I'd also like to start the game soon. D;<br /> <br /> Maybe we can do a compromise? They could join in shortly after the game begins, if the character isn't ready by then? Our group could stumble across his character during the Rite, or an Elder/etc. could stroll up just before they head off to say &quot;Oh, by the way, this guy's joining y'all.&quot; Or something. </div> </div> </div>If someone is going to join us at this stage, I'd prefer the character come along for the rite of passage with everyone else. It's one thing for a character to join later, as a replacement for a PC that dies or a player that leaves, but having someone join as we're starting but not take part in the Rite of Passage, missing the first adventure... I'd rather not go that route.<br /> <br /> So, I'm afraid it's an all or nothing kind of deal, guys.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:44:22-08:00","id":305178,"title":"","content":"I don't have, nor have I ever read Rage Across the Heavens. So feel free to suggest away Jim.<br /> <br /> I'm also with Josh, I wouldn't mind having another person, but I also want the game to start, so if you can get things rolling quickly Rall, then I don't mind.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 11-06-2014, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:02:57-08:00","id":305184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305178#post305178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have, nor have I ever read Rage Across the Heavens. So feel free to suggest away Jim.<br /> <br /> I'm also with Josh, I wouldn't mind having another person, but I also want the game to start, so if you can get things rolling quickly Rall, then I don't mind.<br /> <br /> -Mark</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting read; I recommend it if you get the chance.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, <a href=\"http://boilinghell.wikidot.com/system:page-tags/tag/incarnae#pages\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a> has links to a fairly faithful reproduction of the key information on the Planetary Incarnae (except Hakahe, for some reason, though he would be a poor choice for Hannah anyway). At the bottom of each of the pages is the details about that Incarna's role in garou astrology and their influences as an astrological sign.<br /> <br /> Given Hannah's personality, I think that <a href=\"http://boilinghell.wikidot.com/hyperion\" target=\"_blank\">Hyperion/Katanka-Sonnak</a>, Planetary Incarna of Helios, the Celestine of the Sun, would be a perfect fit. Take a look at that one and some of the others and tell me what you think; Zarok would also be a good, if obvious, choice, though I maintain that Hyperion fits her personality better.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:36:16-08:00","id":305200,"title":"","content":"I've read through a few of them that caught my eye, but Hyperion definitely works for Hannah's personality best, so I'm going with that. I'm sure I'll eventually read Rage Across the Heavens, I just need to pick it up off drive thru one of these days.<br /> <br /> I'll update my sheet,<br /> -Mark<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T22:04:20-08:00","id":305301,"title":"","content":"Well, now I feel a lot of pressure! I can text vomit some stuff on the screen, and perfect the sheet shortly thereafter. I do need background ideas. I also hope the concept I came up with is fine, lacking in snowflakiness, and just enough of an annoyance to annoy the characters and not the players. I've had <i>those</i> players that want to make a character complete antagonists (the one trying to play a necromancer when the party has a paladin).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u>Placehholder</u><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-07-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T22:53:29-08:00","id":305324,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... the concept does seem pretty on the nose as an &quot;anti-Hannah,&quot; but that's not necessarily a bad thing. Obviously we'd need more detail on the history. But, as a concept, what do you guys all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:03:40-08:00","id":305328,"title":"","content":"Nah, I'll come up with something else. I did come up with the concept first, but you're right. Forget what I said. I'll edit my post and come up with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:12:49-08:00","id":305335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305328#post305328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I'll come up with something else. I did come up with the concept first, but you're right. Forget what I said. I'll edit my post and come up with something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't accusing you of having done it on purpose. I actually like the concept, it's just probably not best for this group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:15:08-08:00","id":305337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305335#post305335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't accusing you of having done it on purpose. I actually like the concept, it's just probably not best for this group.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I'm trying to avoid the &quot;Necromancer in the party with the paladin&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:47:59-08:00","id":305369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305016#post305016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's lots of contradictory material. I prefer the version put forth in the Book of the Wyrm Second Edition, which describes (among other things) hurling captive Garou into the Black Spiral, at which point they have no choice but to experience it, which in turn shatters their sanity.<br /> <br /> The moral of the story- don't let them take you alive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you serious? That's basically the complete opposite of what's presented in the <i>Chronicle</i>! Bloody White Wolf! In the Book of the Wyrm is the philosophy still the same? That is, do the BDS want to confront and transcend their Urge and thus extinguish their ego and reunite with the Soul of All? Or did they just ditch that in favour of 'Rahh, we're <i>eeevil</i>! And do <i>eeevil </i>things?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And now for Rall. I think pressure is good, it drives you onwards. If you look at when most of us posted our character sheets, it was over two weeks ago. And we created our character concepts before that. So I really don't wanna be an ass, but I don't want to wait another two weeks. But see, look how much you've done already! Some pressure's good for you.<br /> <br /> So about Cody:<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice</b>: Okay, I hope I express this properly. Basically, the guy playing our other Galliard, James, is very new to <i>The Apocalypse.</i> I'm guessing you're much more familiar with it seeing as you run games. You've obviously got much more of an idea as to how to play this Auspice, whereas James probably doesn't. I'd hoped James would be able to play his character in a vacuum, that is, express his character without the need to compare and contrast with another player, so everything he does can only be measured against himself. But if you also play a Galliard it'll mean he might get overshadowed by you. I'm not saying you shouldn't pick this Auspice, just be aware of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b>: You're right, the Shadowlords are presented as the twisted reflection of the Silver Fangs. Both Tribes believe they're destined to rule, both believe might makes right, both believe they know how things should <i>really </i>be done. I think it's a cool Tribe, but you're not bound to follow the stereotype slavishly. Look at Val, he's an Indian Fenrir who think his Tribe's a joke and doesn't give a damn about 'Great' Fenris. Just because you're playing a Shadowlord doesn't mean you have to play them like a Shadowlord (yeah, that doesn't make sense. Consider it a Zen koan.)<br /> <br /> However...Cody is a tad similar to Hannah, I don't know if the pack can handle two overconfident, arrogant garou who think they should be in charge. The Shadowlords never came across as desiring the spotlight or open adulation. They seemed more like the 'power behind the throne' always watching, always waiting, always planning. In fact, it's Tribes like the Get of Fenris which exult fame and renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b>: I have only limited understanding of American culture, but would a male cheerleader really be so popular? I like the idea, but I didn't know male cheerleaders occupied the apex of cool in American highschools.<br /> <br /> And I'm assuming Cody went berserk in the classroom and gutted some students...Again, I'm a terrible pedant, but how likely is that? Yes, I know, werewolves aren't very likely either, but if a bunch of kids turned up in the morgue with their entrails hanging out, there would be investigations. Especially in a developed country like America. In India, in a <i>very </i>rural state (Like Jharkhand), it's just possible for such a thing to occur. Maybe. I'm only saying this to inspire you. When the easy explanations are removed, you're forced to come up with something more intricate. Don't be afraid to try something different. High school student turns into a werewolf? Yeah, okay. Secret Metis child of a prominent Shadow Lord is sent to America to investigate why the original Shadow Lords of the Delaware Valley turned to the Wyrm...or die trying? Don't you think that's got more bite to it? Or at least, more story possibilities. Not that you have to play a Metis...<br /> <br /> I personally don't find Cody that interesting now, he definitely needs some spicing up. I'm more than happy to work with you on ideas, but be warned, they tend towards the...<i>elaborate </i>(and our poor Story Teller has enough plot threads to untangle.)<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I'd prefer not having another High School student in the pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Hayaraba! He Ram! By all the Asuras and Devas! What the hell happened? Everything I said is now meaningless! Um...You can still consider playing that secret Metis...ahem...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 11-07-2014, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:01:08-08:00","id":305376,"title":"","content":"For the record, I'm OK with more High School students. That is the age group I assumed most of the pack would be, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:17:49-08:00","id":305387,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, Al-Haleem. I actually went ahead and nuked the concept. I'm fine-tuning a new one with help from NutiketAiel. It's still a Shadow Lord Galliard. I've taken your suggestions in account for writing up the new character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:32:41-08:00","id":305400,"title":"","content":"Sigh. Guess I was late to the party. I'm glad you picked a Shadow Lord though. <br /> <br /> And call me Josh :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T03:41:07-08:00","id":305484,"title":"","content":"But but but but! I didn't even get the chance to criticize the old character! D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T04:25:00-08:00","id":305523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305484#post305484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But but but but! I didn't even get the chance to criticize the old character! D:</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry. Plenty of time to criticize the new character! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Making a Shadow Lord is difficult. I have to admit that I've only ever played Bone Gnawers and Ratkin. In fact, I've played more of the latter than the former. I've read the Bone Gnawers books backwards and forwards. So... I'm sure you'll get plenty of laughs from my poor attempt at writing. Should have it done in an hour or so. Hopefully you'll get to start a new game very, very soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:40:50-08:00","id":305625,"title":"","content":"Don't worry, I'll never laught at you...I will ask lots of awkward questions though. And Shadow Lords are awesome, they're like furry Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T09:19:36-08:00","id":305812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305625#post305625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, I'll never laught at you...I will ask lots of awkward questions though. And Shadow Lords are awesome, they're like furry Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>They even have the accents. :-)<br /> <br /> In seriousness, though, remember Bashir that this is intended to be a very long term game. Just as important as making sure that the character is playable within the context of the group is making sure that the character is one that you are happy playing and developing over a long period of time. If you're not happy with the Shadow Lord concept, don't force it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 11-07-2014, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:09:02-08:00","id":305871,"title":"","content":"On the contrary, I am quite wedded to the idea. Yes, I may know every dirty secret and personality of the children of Mother Rat, there comes a time when one should break out of the comfort zone.<br /> <br /> I've submitted a revised history to Nutket, hopefully it's more &quot;formed&quot;. I want to get this right, despite a paranoia of having characters die after putting so much work into their background. It is a curse I have.<br /> <br /> Buuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuut, if you <i>neeeeeeeeeed</i> a Gnawer...<br /> <br /> I'm still reading through all the posts in the recruitment thread and seeing how to work in the character's relationship with the others.<br /> <br /> I'm Bashir. Funny that my family pronounces it &quot;Basher&quot;, like I'm going to give someone a beat down.<br /> <br /> Also, I love taking a starting character and building it up. I have in my email box a letter from 8 years ago where a Werewolf player was incensed that she had to play a Cliath. She ranted on about how she didn't want to be &quot;blind, deaf, and dumb&quot;, and that she was an <i>expert</i> roleplayer. She also tried to get the caern totem of cuckoo replaced with wolverine, as she does in every damn game. Oh, and she has to snowflake it harder than everyone else. The metis child of Albrecht and Cabra who has grown up to be the Keeper of Elysium in Atlanta? Sure. I'm the asshole for not letting her play it. I rather lack confidence in the fact that I don't want any snowflakiness... well, except if I can play a Ratkin, but... Nevermind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-07-2014, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:46:17-08:00","id":305930,"title":"","content":"You don't like snowflakes? Say hello to Val. I invented an Indian branch of the Get of Fenris just for him*. As far as I'm concerned, the more unique the better. Um...and this is going to sound weird but is your name related to the Arabic \u0628\u0634\u064a\u0631? Just curious.<br /> <br /> * Although Jim's doing all the actual work. Undoubtably he'll get his revenge. I'm waiting for him to ask me to translate my character sheet into Sanskrit or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:01:05-08:00","id":305945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=305930#post305930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't like snowflakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in Finland. I despise snowflakes now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say hello to Val. I invented an Indian branch of the Get of Fenris just for him*. </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with this. You're not asking to be the daughter or son of somebody in one of the Tribebooks? Just about every Vampire clan had a bloodline from a different area. Like the Tlacique, Duncir, and Wu Zao. I wouldn't blink at Indian Get. Followers of Hanuman, with his warrior spirit and honor. Granted, yeah, he's a monkey-headed god, but still. I'm just giving an example. Judging by your avatar, you're going for Narashima.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um...and this is going to sound weird but is your name related to the Arabic \u0628\u0634\u064a\u0631? Just curious. </div> </div> </div>Other than the odd pronunciation, that's how I spell it, yes. I had posted in the W:tA forum on help with a Rage Across Riyadh campaign and had some good input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-07-2014, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T12:24:35-08:00","id":306042,"title":"","content":"I'm impressed you recognised whom my display picture was of! Indeed, Val is named after Narasimha &quot;Narasimha-Vallabha&quot; means &quot;Beloved of Narasimha&quot; although the Vrikodara is inspired by Bhima. Although there are plenty of war-related Devas to choose from, so the Fenrir would probably be quite at home in India. If you're from Finland you must find the whole Get of Fenris bemusing though.<br /> <br /> And forgive me, but is Bashir a name you've adopted? I had thought you might be of Arab origin (I live in the Middle East myself) so I was just curious...although this sounds like an interrogation =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T20:22:14-08:00","id":306364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm impressed you recognised whom my display picture was of! Indeed, Val is named after Narasimha &quot;Narasimha-Vallabha&quot; means &quot;Beloved of Narasimha&quot; although the Vrikodara is inspired by Bhima. Although there are plenty of war-related Devas to choose from, so the Fenrir would probably be quite at home in India. If you're from Finland you must find the whole Get of Fenris bemusing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Get could frenzy here, and an old Finnish woman would tell, &quot;Calm down. You're making us look bad.&quot; If he got angry, she'd beat him down with a purse, even if it endangered her. The Silver Fangs wouldn't get much love here, either. At least their &quot;Russian&quot; counterparts. If they were part of the Swedish nobility, then they'd get an &quot;eh, whatever&quot;. My experience has been that the Finns laugh at &quot;royalty&quot;. Finns reading are welcome to correct me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And forgive me, but is Bashir a name you've adopted? I had thought you might be of Arab origin (I live in the Middle East myself) so I was just curious...although this sounds like an interrogation =p </div> </div> </div>You can run a game set in Helsinki and a player wouldn't have to give a reason why their choice of tribe &quot;is there&quot;. Stargazers? Influx of Nepalese workers and students. You can go to Kamppi and Hakaniemi and eat at a Nepalese restaurant or buy Nepalese goods. Silent Striders? Pshaw! Helsinki has a significant population of Egyptians, Syrians, Somalis, Indians... the list goes on. I would be remiss if I didn't mention the Roma. The University of Helsinki is trying to hire on researchers of the Roma language and culture so as to improve education for their minority population. Granted, the Roma do face extreme prejudice here.<br /> <br /> Wendigo and Uktena may be trickier, though there are the Saami in the far north. They'd have Bear or Reindeer as a totem, though.<br /> <br /> I'm not Middle Eastern, true. In my language, though, we spell my name \u0628\u0634\u06cc\u0631 which is Urdu for \u0628\u0634\u06cc\u0631 and... oh... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Feel free to interrogate me more. Developing a rapport with other players is good for interactions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-07-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T23:26:51-08:00","id":306437,"title":"","content":"Wait, is your familiy originally from Pakistan? I'm half Indian! In fact, my mother's side of the family is from Peshawar, but they left just before the Partition. And I had no idea Finland was so diverse, but how do you stand the temperature? Isn't it freezing? I start shivering when it gets below 18C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T02:24:58-08:00","id":306482,"title":"","content":"From Islamabad to America. And now I'm in Finland. I handle the cold easily. I just stay inside. Or l wear several layers of clothing. It's 2C right now. I think every major European city is very diverse. Paris, Madrid, Barcelona, Stockholm, Amsterdam, Helsinki, all have very mixed populations. So no one has to make an excuse to play any tribe of Garou. Barcelona is probably more mixed than Helsinki, but I don't think anyone has to worry about Helsinki, either.<br /> <br /> The concept is a professional liar, debater, and salesman. Years of convincing people to buy obviously defective products have worn on his soul. As with last time, I haven't done backgrounds or freebies, as I'm trying to hammer in what &quot;Jon&quot; (maybe I'll go back to Cody. And maybe change him to a woman).<br /> <br /> Edit 3<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <u>Name:</u> Jon Blaszczyk<br /> <br /> <u>Player:</u> Bashir<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> <u>Breed:</u> Homid<br /> <u>Auspice:</u> Galliard<br /> <u>Tribe:</u> Shadow Lords<br /> <u>Camp:</u><br /> <u>Sept:</u> Thundering Pines<br /> <u>Pack Name:</u><br /> <u>Pack Totem:</u><br /> <br /> <u>Nature:</u> Fatalist<br /> <u>Demeanor:</u> Competitor<br /> <u>Concept:</u> Dead-Inside Salesman<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Manipulation (Forked Tongue): 4<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 2<br /> Intelligence: 3<br /> Wits: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u><br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness:<br /> Athletics: 2<br /> Brawl: 1<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression (Inspiring Speeches): 3<br /> Intimidation: 1<br /> Leadership: 1<br /> Primal-Urge:<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge (The Long Con): 4<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive: 2<br /> Etiquette: 3<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance (Dance): 1<br /> Stealth: 2<br /> Survival: 2<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics (Ethics): 2<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law (Litany): 1<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult:<br /> Rituals: 2<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds (5)</u><br /> Kinfolk 1<br /> Rites 1<br /> Spirit Heritage (Banes) 1<br /> Totem: 2<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Persuasion (Homid; Level 1; W20, p. 153)<br /> Mindspeak (Galliard; Level 1; W20, p. 169)<br /> Aura of Confidence (Shadow Lords; Level 1; W20, p. 188)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> Rite of Boasting<br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u> N/A<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> 4 (4)<br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> 4 (4)<br /> <u>Willpower:</u> 8 (8)<br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent: 2<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent: 1<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Rank:</u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Mitanu's Tongue (2)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Dark Secret (1)<br /> Intolerance [Deadbeat Dads] (1)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> Kinfolk: Crazy ex-girlfriend named Gaye McAdams who lets him crash on her couch. Schoolgirl crush, but is too shy to make any moves. Maybe he takes after dad, too, in that he keeps his distance beyond staying the night now and then, and convincing her the food he bought for her is organic and free from government sterilizing pesticides.<br /> <br /> Rites: As a Galliard, he's tasked with knowing some of the lore and rituals of his tribe and sept. He's got a little bit of aptitude and he knows more than one.<br /> <br /> Spirit Heritage: (Considering mom...)<br /> <br /> Dark Secret: Being the product of an unholy union, it's best if people don't know of his mother's parentage. He has two strikes against him for most everyone else. First, he's a Shadow Lord, and they have a bad reputation already. Secondly, he's the son of a Black Spiral Dancer kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Intolerance (Deadbeat Dads): Learning of his father's infidelity and his penchant for being very, very disrespectful of his bastard, Jon's taken that to heart and sees all cheating spouses like his father. There are children who go through worse in this horrible world, but for some reason, anything that resembles his father's behavior is despised.<br /> <br /> <u>Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Apparent Age:</u> 19<br /> <u>Sign:</u> <i><b>Ruatma</b></i><br /> <u>Race:</u> Caucasian<br /> <u>Sex:</u> Male<br /> <u>Gender:</u> Male<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> Straight. Bi-curious.<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u> Black<br /> <u>Fur Color:</u> Slightly darker black<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u> Brown<br /> <u>Height:</u> 6' 0\u201d<br /> <u>Weight:</u> 160 lbs<br /> <u>Build:</u> The track team has given him a runner's build, but since his parting ways with dad, he's started eating more junk food and putting on weight.<br /> <u>Distinctive Features:</u> His widow's peak is a bit pronounced, but it doesn't take away from his above-average looks.<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> Homid: White male with a straight, almost regal posture despite his traditionally slovenly appearance. He looks like the world is weathering him away. He's gaining weight and his eyes often look black from an all-nighter., tends to wear geeky shirts, like those black t-shirts with the dragon that wraps around it. Maybe the one with three wolves howling. In fact, t-shirts and jeans are about all he wears. At least he dresses better than a Bone Gnawer!<br /> <br /> Crinos: Blacker than night. He cannot camouflage even during a full moon, he's just that black. He wears dedicated mementos from his time in high school, including his cheap white metal class ring. His fur is rather plush and bears no scarring. Yet.<br /> <br /> Lupus: As with his Crinos, he seems unnaturally black. No white whiskers exist on his form. His brown eyes blend with his fur so as to be practically invisible, except when the light hits him just right and makes his eyes glow.<br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u><br /> '87 Dodge Diplomat<br /> Clothes in a suitcase in the back<br /> Cheap Nokia cellphone from about 8 years ago<br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> Fatigued and pessimistic on the inside, yet Jon can switch on a bubbly personality if the situation demands. Although he seems to hate lying, he does derive some pleasure conning people he considers stupid. He's always trying to fight back a passive-aggressive remark, especially in the presence of Gaye.<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u><br /> \u201cGet a fucking job,\u201d he said. \u201cYou want that? Work for it!\u201d he said. \u201cYou don't deserve anything,\u201d he said.<br /> Yeah, life with mom was good, but dad just sucked. Whenever he deigned to grace Jon and Ms. Blaszczyk, it was always a cold encounter. Most kids who have divorced parents, or two that seem like they're a divorced couple, usually look forward to visits from the estranged parent. Not Jon.<br /> <br /> It didn't matter if Jon was captain of the debate team. It didn't matter if he ran track and cross country and got trophies. It didn't matter that he was an Eagle Scout. It didn't matter if Jon was on the honor roll. Dad always took the time to mention his many, many more achievements than Jon had.<br /> <br /> Jon was quite isolated, as his pursuits of perfection left him little time to cultivate friendships. Even with his extracurricular resume, Jon had a difficult time finding a job in this tiny town. The only place that teenagers could expect to get a job was at the local mall. Sadly, all the stores weren't hiring. But finally fate smiled upon Jon in the form of a company that was infamous for their cheap \u201cAs Viewed on Television\u201d products. All Jon had to do was use his inborn speaking skills to peddle the shit. It slices, it dices, it cuts through aluminum cans and dehydrates a turkey. Jon knew how to present these crap goods and get people to buy them, even knowing full well that those products would break after getting home, or would gather dust in a closet. It was grating on the spirit. After a year, fleecing people for an obviously corrupt company, it began wearing on Jon's soul. Keeping with the debate team, keeping with the track team, keeping up the grades, and now being a lowly huckster built up the rage until one day, after a former customer came back to the mall and started throwing the fragmented pieces of the Juicertron with included Shammytastic cloth at Jon just about lost it. When he got home that night, dad was there, likely to toss some hush-money to Jon and his mom. He wasn't in the mood to see dad or take his money, and after tossing it right back at the old man, heated words were exchanged.<br /> <br /> The next thing Jon remembers is dad having claw marks on his chest and a bite wound on his shoulder. Mom was incommunicado. Life was upended in an instant.<br /> <br /> A few years later and Jon found himself learning the ways of the Garou, in the role of a Lorekeeper and Ritemaster. Thank Gaia for those good study habits he forced himself into learning. These Shadow Lords of the Thundering Pines are tough bastards with higher standards than dad, but at least they are <i>there</i>. One day Jon will be worthy of a name and Grandfather Thunder.<br /> <br /> Daddy Issues:<br /> Dad didn't want Jon. Even after hearing of the child's existence, dad kept Jon at a distance, rarely visiting his mother, and maybe renewing a Netflix membership in hopes of shutting the kid up. Dad was a thoughtless, careless philanderer. Dad supposedly had a happy marriage, so why would he have women on the side? There were complaints of having to cover up Jon's fucking mess, how he almost ruined everything. Why was dad even angrier than usual? The story goes that his father had an affair with what he thought was Shadow Lord kin was in fact Black Spiral Kin. Somehow someone, somewhere found out. What fantastic blackmail material.<br /> But father felt obligated to tutor his son in the ways of the Lords. He was determined to not allow his kid fall to the Spiral. The Garou nation could not afford to lose another, despite the cub's unfortunate history. Dad taught as much as he felt his son needed. How to cut someone, how to petition spirits, how to use one's gifts. He taught Cliff's Notes version of Garou hierarchy, rites, and history. Once the bare minimums were passed on, dad handed over the keys to an ancient '87 Dodge Diplomat and sent him to finish off whatever he needed with Shadow Lords of the Thundering Pines sept.<br /> <br /> Jon doesn't understand too much about the concept of Kinfolk, it was obvious his mother was one. Dad didn't know her true lineage, and thus, neither does Jon. Since she was an outsider and working at one of the local chemical plants, it's rumored that she was Black Spiral Kin. After the night of his First Change, mom had disappeared, adding to his father's suspicion. Dad, of course, took the opportunity to belittle his son and tell him of the suspicion. Jon cared deeply for the mother who worked hard and often stayed late to make sure he had a good life. He deeply hopes that she is alive, and when he has more time, he will find her and learn the truth. Even if he learns that she was Spiral Kin, he may find himself torn on protecting her, arguing that she's a good person and needs to be cleansed. He will do anything to clear her name, even if it means telling one of the biggest lies in his life.<br /> <br /> While Jon struggles to ingratiate himself with the new pack, he considers a woman named Gaye McAdams to be as close to a friend as possible. She's his crazy ex-girlfriend from high school. She moved away halfway through senior year, as she proved herself highly intelligent and got to enter college early for a electrical and computer engineering degree at Rowan University. But she's always had a crush on Jon. The problem is, is she's too much of UFO nutter. Aliens are real and the government is covering it up. She spends an inordinate amount of time toying with a HAM radio and a 1960s oscilloscope, when she's not trying to do a pathetic job of flirting. Her computer is almost always on and running SETI algorithms. One week, Gaye had said she was going to visit her mother and asked if Jon would apartment-sit. Naturally, he agreed. One gibbous moon and Jon decided to test his shapeshifting abilities, when Gaye came home early because she forgot a gift she meant to bring her parent. Her response was a dropped jaw, followed by \u201cthat... is so fucking awesome!\u201d The platinum-haired nightmare is kinfolk, so he's told by the sept,and that's the limit of his understanding on the matter, and apparently she's unaware of the connection, too. Shit. And you're never supposed to stick your dick in crazy. Well, like the government conspiracies she's trying to uncover, she loves having her own conspiracy to be a part of.<br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <u>Experience Details</u><br /> Gnosis +3 (6 points)<br /> Willpower +5 (5 points)<br /> Etiquette +1 (2 points)<br /> Subterfuge +1 (2 points)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yet another edit. Added reasons for Gaye. Fixed backgrounds. Did balance sheet so that I can remember how to do math.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Edit 4</u></b><br /> <br /> Added the two missing points for talents for Skills. Boosted Etiquette to give (Tribal), reflecting his indoctrination with the Shadow Lords, though if the ST prefers, I can switch to Big Business to reflect his increased knowledge in how businesses, well, do business.<br /> Added a point in Survival to reflect his overachiever attitude in the Boy Scouts.<br /> <br /> *Possible changes: Increasing Dance to 2 to reflect his Prom King achievement.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Edit 5</b></u><br /> Added the merit that I swear was there, but like so many things, was, in fact, not there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-13-2014, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:19:12-08:00","id":306540,"title":"","content":"He doesn't quite look like a highschooler. How old is he?<br /> (A little older is fine : my character Geoff is 19, and works on an online degree. But Jim wants us to be young and fresh!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:21:51-08:00","id":306543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306540#post306540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't quite look like a highschooler. How old is he?<br /> (A little older is fine : my character Geoff is 19, and works on an online degree. But Jim wants us to be young and fresh!)</div> </div> </div> </div>On my character sheet, he's 20. Skirting the maximum age for a cliath. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:35:20-08:00","id":306549,"title":"","content":"Shoot, I was hoping to keep the &quot;older and wiser&quot; role! Although...well, looks like I might still get to have the wiser part. x)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:37:47-08:00","id":306550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306549#post306549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shoot, I was hoping to keep the &quot;older and wiser&quot; role! Although...well, looks like I might still get to have the wiser part. x)</div> </div> </div> </div>My ring finger is hovering over the backspace key. Nothing is set in stone. Well, except Homid Galliard Shadow Lords. I need to research how old malls usually employ those super saccharine kiosk salespeople.<br /> <br /> Edited: It's a miserable weekend in Helsinki. I'm probably going to be F5-ing the forums every ten minutes or so. People can expect quick responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:50:27-08:00","id":306578,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying this to influence you, but I'm surprised that with six players, we only have one Lupus and no Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T05:19:08-08:00","id":306580,"title":"","content":"I have some questions:<br /> <br /> 1: If a Black Spiral Kinswoman brought Jon to term, why would she give her child up to a Shadow Lord? (What's the dad's name btw?) Did she just turn up on his doorstep and say : Hey bitch! Here's a free baby. Later sucker! (Unless of course dad's story was a complete lie...)<br /> <br /> 2: So Jon worked at a kiosk in a mall? If a former customer turned up, bitched at him, and triggered his First Change...Wouldn't there have been a lot of witnesses? Unless it was in an isolated place, <i>someone </i>would notice a slavering werewolf. And malls tend to have lots of security surveillance, so even if everyone succumbed to the Delirium, there'd still be evidence.<br /> <br /> 3: This is more a nitpick, but only metis in the Thrall of the Wyrm seek to sexually violate their targets. A homid would try to devour them. Again, unless this is just a malicious invective, but invective needs some basis in fact to be effective.<br /> <br /> I do like the dad's portrayal through, he's not the typical 'Lord of the land beyond the forest, who doesn't drink...<i>vine</i>'<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless...Dad is in fact a Black Spiral! <i>Dun dun duuun</i>!<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And Flo, you're totally saying that to influence him =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T09:03:03-08:00","id":306693,"title":"","content":"1. The Black Spiral kin was a suggestion given to me. I tried to add it in, and from your confusion, I didn't do it very well. The idea was that &quot;Dad&quot; (who will remain nameless) is a Shadow Lord that was leading a double life, having affairs and stuff. Keep in mind, this guy is from Trenton. How many Wyrm-tainted factories and chemical plants are around that region. It kinda makes sense that something would rock the system.<br /> <br /> 2. I thought I changed it, but I didn't. As with many Garou stories, a murder here and there gets covered up. Small town, or suburb, one guy found in a darkened dumpster looking mangled by a large animal. While certainly out of the ordinary, cases can go cold with the right contacts. Right? Sure, it's made of elemental handwavium, but I can't think of anything better right now.<br /> <br /> 3. If Dad is a Black Spiral, he sure has a foot in the door with the Shadow Lords of the region. I'll leave that up to the ST, but as far as I know both in- and out-of-character, he's just a shamed Shadow Lord with a young adult sword of Damocles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T11:04:40-08:00","id":306807,"title":"","content":"I'm tottaly cool with 'Dad' being a no-good dog. I just don't know why a Black Spiral would give up their child. Either dad took his son back by force (which raises other questions) or this kinswoman had a very close relationship with Dad...which raises questions about dad's loyalties. And instead of Jon murdering a disgruntled customer in a crowded mall (talk about straining the Veil) what happened if Jon finnaly got sick of dad's shit and underwent the First Change. Nearly killing your own father...talk about daddy issues. Also, don't Black Spirals employ kin-fetch (?) Spirits? That means someone's (or something's) looking for Jon. Drama! One more thing. I'm assuming dad is a disgraced Shadow Lord, what doed he get out of sending his son to the Thundering Pines Sept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T11:24:14-08:00","id":306813,"title":"","content":"Changed to &quot;back alley, nighttime, single victim&quot;. Whether or not it was Jon or a big-ass wild dog, it's the story he's been told. Add a guilt complex to fuel his need to be a <i>better</i> Shadow Lord than his dad. Sure, Jon's become a fatalist (hah, nature). Perhaps climbing the seemingly impossible ladder the tribe has...<br /> <br /> I do like the &quot;nearly killing daddy&quot; idea. Maybe one aspect is that the dad knows he's giving in to the Wyrm, and being an asshole and exiling his bastard son might be the last vestige of caring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T23:32:18-08:00","id":307210,"title":"","content":"Well that makes more logical sense (as far as werewolves are logical). Don't forget to edit your post so we can see the changes. Also, there's still the problem of the mother. I was thinking about it, and I came up with something like this: <br /> <br /> Dad has an affair with a woman he thinks is Shadow Lord kin, but is actually a Dancer. Because he's a responsibility-shirking philanderer, dad leaves his son to mom, who raises him. However, to subvert the stereotype, mom is actually pretty nice, and Jon has a happy childhood. However, dad eventually discovers his mistake, and fears what will happen if his son turns to the Wyrm. He turns up at mom's place and demands she hand Jon over . Naturally, she refuses. Jon is distraught at seeing his mom threatened by a man who's little more than a stranger, and it triggers his First Change....<br /> <br /> He can't quite remember what happened next, but now he's in dad's car and mom's gone. Did dad kill her? He won't say, only that Jon will never see her again. Dad doesn't want to introduce Jon to garou society just yet, as he fears his son may have been tainted. Jon lives an isolated life, winning no respect from his dad despite his achievements. He gets a crappy job selling equally crappy products in a mall. And all this time he's dealing with his slow-boiling Rage. Eventually, he snaps and frenzies, killing someone in a quiet back-alley. Dad realizes he made a mistake in not dealing with his son's new...condition, and sends him to the Thundering Pines Sept before he makes more of a mess.<br /> <br /> And mom? Who knows. The Black Spirals haven't shown up yet...but maybe that's because they think Jon is serving the Wyrm already... <br /> <br /> <br /> That way, you answer the question about the mom, and you can work in the nearly killing dad thing (he underwent the First Change to defend his mother from dad). But you can also keep all the latter stuff about living with dad and working in the mall. And it makes a nice contrast between his blissful life with mom, and his horrid life with dad. Dad forbade his son from contacting his mother, and made certain he obeyed him. But now that Jon's free of his father's control, maybe he wants to reconnect with his mom? <br /> <br /> Feel free to ignore all of that. So far, Jon is a major improvement on Cody, but he's an interesting character, which is why I gave so much thought to this. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T07:15:43-08:00","id":307389,"title":"","content":"Okay, editing now. I'm pretty much going &quot;yoink&quot; with your version.<br /> <br /> Now, question: What backgrounds with you suggest for Jon? I figure Resources 2 to represent his car being in good working condition, but with the knowledge that if he doesn't keep up the &quot;act&quot;, he could run out of cash soon. Let's see... Pure Breed is out. Contacts is out. The book suggests that Shadow Lords go without Allies. Ancestors? Doesn't seem like he's too in contact. Rites? Sure, but which ones?<br /> <br /> I guess beyond investing in the pack totem and maybe a fetish, Jon isn't going to have much.<br /> <br /> I always felt that Dark Secret was a cop out flaw that every one of my players in Vampire and Mage games took. But here? I think it's quite obvious. I don't think it's more than one. Sure, he's got some baggage, but <i>that</i> much?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T19:02:44-08:00","id":307734,"title":"","content":"<u>Bashir</u><br /> If you want to push his connection to the Wyrm even further, you could throw a dot or two into the background &quot;Spirit Heritage - Banes&quot;.<br /> <br /> <u>Jim</u><br /> Ah, the wording in Rage Across the Heavens confused me, specifically this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Although the Hunter does not &quot;rule&quot; over any given lunar month, some Garou seen to gravitate toward Rorg as their patron, regardless of the actual sign of their birth. Because of this, <b>Garou who claim Rorg as their celestial ruler do so out of choice</b> rather than accident.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The choice bit threw me off. I wouldn't expect Echo to know much about Garou astrology at this point, much less for her to go off choosing a new sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:11:05-08:00","id":307905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying this to influence you, but I'm surprised that with six players, we only have one Lupus and no Metis. </div> </div> </div>I'm not. Metis and Lupus are significantly more difficult to play. There's a reason the majority of players choose to be Homid. Had we ended up with an entirely homid pack, I would not have been surprised. I believe I noted this possibility in the original character creation post, in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: This is more a nitpick, but only metis in the Thrall of the Wyrm seek to sexually violate their targets. A homid would try to devour them. Again, unless this is just a malicious invective, but invective needs some basis in fact to be effective. </div> </div> </div>I don't like the Thrall of the Wyrm to be that predictable. In my games, the activities of an individual while frenzying under the Thrall of the Wyrm are not determined by breed. They're determined by... other factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, don't Black Spirals employ kin-fetch (?) Spirits? That means someone's (or something's) looking for Jon. </div> </div> </div>Even among Gaian Garou, not every child is tagged with a kin-fetch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, question: What backgrounds with you suggest for Jon? I figure Resources 2 to represent his car being in good working condition, but with the knowledge that if he doesn't keep up the &quot;act&quot;, he could run out of cash soon. Let's see... Pure Breed is out. Contacts is out. The book suggests that Shadow Lords go without Allies. Ancestors? Doesn't seem like he's too in contact. Rites? Sure, but which ones?<br /> <br /> I guess beyond investing in the pack totem and maybe a fetish, Jon isn't going to have much. </div> </div> </div>A Fetish would be very difficult to justify. It has to have come from somewhere, and there are few places in his backstory that would be an appropriate source for fetishes (unless it was something left from his Mom, I suppose, but you SO do not want to go there). Ancestors... considering his lineage, that could be potentially disastrous. Could be interesting, but it is another complication that you may not want to add. Rites is not a bad choice, since he could have learned them from the Shadow Lords at the Sept of the Thundering Pines.<br /> <br /> Don't buy resources just to justify the fact that his car works. He can have the car either way as a part of his backstory; the resources background is for a continuing source of income. You'd need to justify where it's coming from, and somehow I doubt he still works in the mall.<br /> <br /> Screw the book's recommendations on backgrounds; most of them are garbage, which is why I have my own house rules on backgrounds in the character creation post. The tribal pigeonholing of which social backgrounds can be chosen is and always has been absurd.<br /> <br /> Honestly, at this point I need to see a new version of the backstory, with whatever modifications you've decided on based on the discussion here, before I can make more coherent suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to push his connection to the Wyrm even further, you could throw a dot or two into the background &quot;Spirit Heritage - Banes&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That's not at all a bad idea, though again, it would create complications down the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The choice bit threw me off. I wouldn't expect Echo to know much about Garou astrology at this point, much less for her to go off choosing a new sign. </div> </div> </div>Right, I forgot about that little detail, sorry. I never liked the idea of simply tying the signs to a particular lunar month; too simplistic. In my game, an individual's sign is chosen by complex astrological calculations involving the location of various features in the Aetherial Realm and the penumbral sky at the time of birth and first change. Translation- choose whatever you want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T23:36:06-08:00","id":307929,"title":"","content":"I would have replied sooner, but the forum was down : (<br /> <br /> I'm glad you liked my suggestions Bashir. I always enjoyed creating back-stories for characters. It used to be my favourite part of Vampire...As sad as it sounds.<br /> <br /> The Flaw Dark Secret works well. Jon has a Black Spiral kin for a mother, who he cares about, and he resents his garou father...and then there's the whole murder thing. Also, depending on how well dad is known, the flaw Notoriety might also work. The Merit Mitanu's Tongue fits Jon's profile as the consumate liar as well.<br /> <br /> Another thing I was thinking about. Val has a bit of a thing for a Black Spiral named Malakai. What happens if Malakai was the brother of Jon's mother? It would be an interesting connection between Val and Jon. Maybe Malakai was the one who gave Jon a fetish*...<br /> <br /> * Hey! Stop the sniggering in the back!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=307905#post307905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game, an individual's sign is chosen by complex astrological calculations involving the location of various features in the Aetherial Realm and the penumbral sky at the time of birth and first change. Translation- choose whatever you want.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this made me chuckle, because I'm sure that's the exact same thing pandits say when picking an auspicious day for a Hindu wedding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 11-10-2014, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:20:29-08:00","id":307945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing I was thinking about. Val has a bit of a thing for a Black Spiral named Malakai. What happens if Malakai was the brother of Jon's mother? It would be an interesting connection between Val and Jon. Maybe Malakai was the one who gave Jon a fetish*...<br /> <br /> * Hey! Stop the sniggering in the back! </div> </div> </div>No. I have other plans for Malakai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:46:59-08:00","id":307960,"title":"","content":"This is all rather ominous...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:49:28-08:00","id":307963,"title":"","content":"Muah ha ha ha!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:52:46-08:00","id":307968,"title":"","content":"Why are all the best Storytellers so terrifying? I fear for Val. I fear for us all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:02:10-08:00","id":307991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=307929#post307929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have replied sooner, but the forum was down : (<br /> <br /> I'm glad you liked my suggestions Bashir. I always enjoyed creating back-stories for characters. It used to be my favourite part of Vampire...As sad as it sounds.<br /> <br /> The Flaw Dark Secret works well. Jon has a Black Spiral kin for a mother, who he cares about, and he resents his garou father...and then there's the whole murder thing. Also, depending on how well dad is known, the flaw Notoriety might also work. The Merit Mitanu's Tongue fits Jon's profile as the consumate liar as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I decided not to take any ranks in Fetish. Instead, Jon just has Rites 2 (he's learning his place as a Galliard), Kinfolk (just one, see in bio), Spirit Heritage (Banes) 1, and invested 1 in the pack Totem. How many points is Mitanu's Tongue, what book is it in, and what is the system? I've only &quot;invested&quot; one point in Dark Secret, but it could be higher.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-10-2014, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:19:44-08:00","id":307998,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306482#post306482\">Edited.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:07:06-08:00","id":308148,"title":"","content":"<b>Mitanu's Tongue</b> (Zodiac Merit, 2 points): You have the ability to talk your way out of most things when dealing with reasoning beings, including most spirits. You gain two extra dice on rolls involving Subterfuge (Or related Secondary Abilities) when attempting to evade the issue, avoid the blame or otherwise escape an awkward situation. (Rage Across the Heavens, pp: 127) <br /> <br /> Also, what happened to mom? If Jon was happy with her, does he want to find her, or re-establish contact? Also, I'm assuming dad turned up at mom's to take back his son, not to toss some money at her. Maybe you should make that clear. Furthermore, Jon's just got one side of the story. All he knows is he was living with his mom, some ass turns up, demands he come with him, and the next thing, Jon turns into a werewolf. His dad says it was for his own good, but how can Jon be sure? The Wyrm, the Black Spiral, what makes them so bad? Mom seemed fine. Why would Jon consider himself tainted? Others would, but a guy who has such high Willpower wouldn't give into others opinions so easily. So what does Jon think about his heritage? <br /> <br /> And I think 1 point is enough. Hannah's also got a Dark Secret, and it's a pretty big one, but it's only worth one point. <br /> <br /> (Really, Robert's Rules of Order? Was Jon running a lot of Town Hall assemblies or something? Unless American High School debate teams employ the rules...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:19:36-08:00","id":308152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308148#post308148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mitanu's Tongue</b> (Zodiac Merit, 2 points): You have the ability to talk your way out of most things when dealing with reasoning beings, including most spirits. You gain two extra dice on rolls involving Subterfuge (Or related Secondary Abilities) when attempting to evade the issue, avoid the blame or otherwise escape an awkward situation. (Rage Across the Heavens, pp: 127)</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, especially when involving his friend-zoned kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what happened to mom? If Jon was happy with her, does he want to find her, or re-establish contact? Also, I'm assuming dad turned up at mom's to take back his son, not to toss some money at her. Maybe you should make that clear. Furthermore, Jon's just got one side of the story. All he knows is he was living with his mom, some ass turns up, demands he come with him, and the next thing, Jon turns into a werewolf. His dad says it was for his own good, but how can Jon be sure? The Wyrm, the Black Spiral, what makes them so bad? Mom seemed fine. Why would Jon consider himself tainted? Others would, but a guy who has such high Willpower wouldn't give into others opinions so easily. So what does Jon think about his heritage? </div> </div> </div>I did the editing in the middle of a physiology lecture. Guh. You're right in that I have very little flow in my paragraphs. I need to write better outline.<br /> <br /> You're going to make me work really hard at this. So much for &quot;Generic Bone Gnawer, third from the left&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think 1 point is enough. Hannah's also got a Dark Secret, and it's a pretty big one, but it's only worth one point. </div> </div> </div>I need another 1 point to get the above-mentioned Merit. Hmm...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Really, Robert's Rules of Order? Was Jon running a lot of Town Hall assemblies or something? Unless American High School debate teams employ the rules...) </div> </div> </div>Debate clubs and some of the national organizations, like Future Farmers of America, Future Business Leaders of America, and others require parliamentary procedure, as dictated in Robert's Rules of Order. This is especially true if the clubs have conventions or competitions. I figure Jon would care for <i>some</i> organization. Edit: As an instructor who had to lead one of those teams, I'm fairly familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-10-2014, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:42:58-08:00","id":308166,"title":"","content":"I much prefer the Indian method of debate: whoever shouts the longest and loudest wins. (Note: I hate this method) And working during a lecture, shameful! (I've been there many a time) It might help to break all the important aspects of Jon's backstory into bullet points, and flesh them out from there. As I said, I love creating characters. I'm a bit of a tyrant when it comes to details, but it's worth the time investment. Trust me, playing a character like Jon will be far more rewarding than playing 'Generic Bone Gnawer, third from the left' (at least I bloody well hope so!) Love the crazy kinfolk, she's a nice touch. Definitely the kind of girl who'd say: Hey, can I meet your pack? They sound sooo cool! Also, you don't need to balance out merits and flaws, you could buy Mitanu's Tongue with freebie points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T07:54:35-08:00","id":308213,"title":"","content":"Real quick. Would &quot;cheating men&quot; or &quot;irresponsible fathers&quot; be alright for a 1 point Intolerance flaw? Or is that too general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:35:38-08:00","id":308233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308213#post308213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real quick. Would &quot;cheating men&quot; or &quot;irresponsible fathers&quot; be alright for a 1 point Intolerance flaw? Or is that too general?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be good, I guess.<br /> <br /> Reading all your characters left me unsatisfied with how I wrote Geoff. I don't think I'll change him, but I may rewrite his background when I'll have the time and motivation. No big changes, I just want a better written background. <br /> <br /> However, I need your opinions here. I can't help but feel that Geoff is a little...bland, as a character. Do you think he's maybe too one-dimensional? I want to add something, but...I don't know what. Any ideas, or am I just overthinking it and my Philodox is actually perfectly fine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T09:53:54-08:00","id":308309,"title":"","content":"An intolerance of cheating men/irresponsible fathers is fine. Val's got an intolerance for 'absolutes'. The important thing is you make it part of your character and are ready to role-play it!<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh gosh, don't encourage me, or Geoff will end up being an avatar for the Wyrm or something. Just because everyone else is dysfunctional, doesn't mean that Geoff is boring. In fact, it might be good for the pack to have a more grounded member, you did want Geoff to be an 'older, wiser brother' for everyone else. As he's written now, I don't think I can make any suggestions without changing his personality.<br /> <br /> I do think Geoff could benefit from a clear driving goal or motivation. Or, alternatively, to use Werewolf speak, an Urge*. An Urge is a negative emotional attachment that a character needs to work through. For Hannah, it's coming to terms with falling to the thrall of the Wyrm. For Echoes its confronting and acknowledging the part of herself that revels in others fear. For Jon it's his hatred and resentment of his father. If you don't want an Urge, a personal goal or motivation is also good. Val's goal is to discover Truth in his new existence (and not give into Fenrir ideals). Jame's motivation is to embody his mentor's teachings and become a 'bridge between the people'...at the cost of his own desires. So what's Geoff's personal goal? Does he have an Urge? What's the deal with his mysterious cleithrophobia? Are there any spiritual entities interested in his development?<br /> <br /> Perhaps ask Geoff these questions:<br /> <br /> 1: What does he want?<br /> <br /> 2: How does he achieve it?<br /> <br /> 3: What's stopping him from achieving it?<br /> <br /> 4: And what happens when he gets what he wants?<br /> <br /> <br /> As he is though, I'm a fan of Geoff. The pack sorely needs someone to play the role of peacekeeper. But sharpening up Geoff's motivations might be a good place to start if you want to develop his character more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Uh...I know nothing of the Black Spiral...Nothing at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 11-10-2014, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:59:07-08:00","id":308372,"title":"","content":"Well, other than cleaning up the bio, the character sheet is done, I think. The Dark Secret and Intolerance was used for the Tongue merit. There... Okay, so I'm thinking of moving that one point of Larceny that I bought with freebies to something else...<br /> <br /> Edited: I've probably put more time in this character's bio than I did my last two papers on jasmonic acid pathways in <i>Mimosa</i> <i>spp. </i>And now my curse where I die when I put a detailed background in a character will take effect...<br /> <br /> Edit 2:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308233#post308233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading all your characters left me unsatisfied with how I wrote Geoff. I don't think I'll change him, but I may rewrite his background when I'll have the time and motivation. No big changes, I just want a better written background.<br /> <br /> However, I need your opinions here. I can't help but feel that Geoff is a little...bland, as a character. Do you think he's maybe too one-dimensional? I want to add something, but...I don't know what. Any ideas, or am I just overthinking it and my Philodox is actually perfectly fine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's fine! As stated above, the only thing I'd say is clear motivation. If you're talking about <i>my</i> characters, then I would say I only have the benefit of reading a lot of Thomas Pynchon and William S. Burroughs novels. I tend to write very on the fly. It's why I wasted no time in cranking out a character when everyone wanted to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-10-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:22:19-08:00","id":308386,"title":"","content":"<u>Bashir</u><br /> <br /> All right, let me take a read through of your character sheet with the modifications.<br /> <br /> Fatalist and Competitor are a good nature/demeanor combination for this character.<br /> <br /> You should really pick specialties for your attributes over 4 (technically it's optional, but if you don't choose one, you won't get the associated bonus). Manipulation is great; however, I worry about the distribution of mental abilities. Given Jon's skill at debating and fast-talking, it seems like you've skimped on Wits. The ability to think and react quickly is essential for those abilities, after all. It would be better if you took a point out of Intelligence and put it into Wits (unless you wanted to respend some other things to free up freebie points; either way works).<br /> <br /> You should consider putting a point into Streetwise. Given Jon's background, especially his job, a very low level of Streetwise would certainly be justified and could prove useful. Just a suggestion, though.<br /> <br /> You'll need to choose specialties for Academics and Expression. These aren't optional. Remember that custom specialties are fine, pending my approval.<br /> <br /> Robert's Rules of Order (and yes, Josh, many debate teams employ parliamentary procedure, though I'm more familiar with it from my time in Student Government) is not really an appropriate specialty for Law. Not only is it far too narrow, but I wouldn't even classify parliamentary procedure under Law; I'd consider it a function of the Etiquette skill (and I would consider Parliamentary Procedure to be an appropriate Etiquette specialty). Also, given Jon's background, two dots in Law is pretty high. It suggests a level of formal training that isn't implied by his background. Unless it was your intention for his focus to be on Garou law, with his training having been received at the Sept of the Thundering Pines?<br /> <br /> You spent six points on Backgrounds; I'm assuming this is where the freebie point from Dark Secret went?<br /> <br /> Good choices on the gifts; they're exactly the choices I would have made for Jon. <br /> <br /> The Rite of Cleansing is not a bad choice; a very useful rite that many Garou choose to learn, though not usually a focus for Galliards. The Rite of Heritage is a little more... problematic. Remember, rites have to have been learned from another Garou at some point. One would think that a demonstration would be a part of that, and then... bam, there goes his dark secret. You might want to rethink that one. A suggestion- maybe drop both of those and take the Rite of Praise, which is both useful and very appropriate for a Galliard? There are also two level 2 rites from the Shadow Lord revised Tribebook that would be both useful and appropriate for Jon to have been taught- the Murmur Rite (which protects the participants from all forms of supernatural eavesdropping) and Communion with the Storm (which, if enacted during a thunderstorm, allows the ritemaster to commune with Grandfather Thunder). I won't require you to change your choices, but know that if you stick with the Rite of Heritage, whichever Garou (probably Quiet Storm, the Alpha and Ritemaster of the Sept of the Thundering Pines) taught him the rite will be, at the very least, suspicious of Jon's heritage.<br /> <br /> Although, I can see why Jon would want to know the Rite of Heritage. After what happened with his Dad, the desire to be able to verify the... pedigree... of any potential mating partners would certainly be important to him.<br /> <br /> I'm cool with Gaye but, if she knew Jon when they were in school together, we need a reason for her to be in South Jersey now (as opposed to up near Trenton, where Jon grew up). I suggest that she be a Computer Science major at a university down here, like Rowan or Rutgers Camden.<br /> <br /> We'll need to pick a garou astrological sign for Jon. I see that you do not have access to Rage Across the Heavens. Check out <a href=\"http://boilinghell.wikidot.com/system:page-tags/tag/incarnae#pages\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> for details on most of them (unfortunately, it doesn't include Hakahe; I'll have to get you some information on him when I can). The information on each of the Planetary Incarnae from an astrological perspective is on the bottom of each page. Take a look and see if any jump out at you. I suggest special attention to Ruatma and Mitanu.<br /> <br /> I need clarification on something, since the backstory is a little unclear on the issue- is Jon aware of his mother's heritage? If so, was it his Dad who told him? If it wasn;t his Dad, how did he find out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An intolerance of cheating men/irresponsible fathers is fine. </div> </div> </div>Good thing we have you here to approve these things for me, Josh. I appreciate your help, and I'm glad that we're all working together, but please remember that I need to make the final decisions on questions like this.<br /> <br /> And yes, Bashir, either of those would be fine for the Intolerance flaw. Just make sure you are prepared to roleplay it (as Josh said). I'm also OK with Mitanu's Tongue.<br /> <br /> <u>Flo</u><br /> <br /> I think Geoff is great as he is. He has an interesting backstory, a playable personality and sufficient connections for me to thread interesting things from his life into the story.<br /> <br /> As for Josh's suggestion of an &quot;urge&quot; or driving motivation, I'm inclined to disagree. It's fine for some characters to have such a clearly defined motivation at the start of play, but it's hardly essential. Most people go through life without such a particular and singular focus. You have the character down, and there's nothing in his history that necessarily defines a major focus of his activities like that. Such a thing should not be forced. It is, however, something that he can come to have during the course of play. If you want the character to have an &quot;urge,&quot; rather than forcing it, why not let it happen naturally during the course of play, once we start?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:25:48-08:00","id":308388,"title":"","content":"Thanks Josh. I don't think that I'll take all the questions you suggested (I'm especially having trouble coming up with an Urge for Geoff, as you say), but I'm gonna add some different character aspects to him, expand on his motivation, his choice of tribe... Again Jim, don't panic, I'm not making any drastic changes.<br /> <br /> Although, I think I'll rewrite his background with a first person point of view. It's how I do them usually, and I think it adds a lot of character. I'm doing this tonight guys (It's 8 p.m here and I'll be up late), so expect a lot of edits to the character sheet and fast answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-10-2014, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:28:09-08:00","id":308391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308388#post308388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Josh. I don't think that I'll take all the questions you suggested (I'm especially having trouble coming up with an Urge for Geoff, as you say), but I'm gonna add some different character aspects to him. Again Jim, don't panic, I'm not changing anything drastic.<br /> <br /> Although, I think I'll rewrite his background with a first person point of view. It's how I do them usually, and I think it adds a lot of character. I'm doing this tonight guys (It's 8 p.m here and I'll be up late), so expect a lot of edits to the character sheet and fast answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, I'm not worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:54:08-08:00","id":308414,"title":"","content":"You're quite welcome Flo. The urge was just another character facet to work with, something to give Geoff direction. It's not his sole reason for existence, rather another layer of his personality. Geoff's motivations don't need to be overly dramatic, but having a clear idea of why a character exists in a story can help you refine them.<br /> <br /> And writing Geoff's character history in first person is a great idea! It'll definitely help you see events from his perspective.<br /> <br /> And Jim, I'm merely trying to keep the creative process going. If I say something's fine, I mean it makes sense in the context of the character. It's not meant to imply that it's approved for play. I apologize if I come across as overbearing, but I wasn't trying to take over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:58:21-08:00","id":308418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308414#post308414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Jim, I'm merely trying to keep the creative process going. If I say something's fine, I mean it makes sense in the context of the character. It's not meant to imply that it's approved for play. I apologize if I come across as overbearing, but I wasn't trying to take over.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's OK, Josh. I know that my work schedule makes waiting for me to reply a little frustrating sometimes. Like I said, I appreciate character creation being a cooperative process. I just worry about people getting too far ahead with certain assumptions of what's OK before I have a chance to weigh in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:21:33-08:00","id":308445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308386#post308386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Bashir</u><br /> <br /> Various excellent suggestions...</div> </div> </div> </div>I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306482#post306482\">edits</a>, complete with notes, and bolded and italicized changes to bio and added Rautama.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T20:04:21-08:00","id":308787,"title":"","content":"Aaand, I added three paragraphs in Geoff's notes. I hope that it doesn't feel forced. <br /> (I also switched the point in Enigma to Occult.)<br /> <br /> I wanted to have a productive night but my roomate showed up with pizzas and movies, and...well... who am I to say no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T21:34:24-08:00","id":308826,"title":"","content":"I dunno if it's forced. I mean, I have no room to speak. I've been taking a belt sander to the square peg for the past two days. If I were to make a suggestion, I'd say go ahead and incorporate those notes into the story. &quot;Geoff felt the need to come out of the closet... twice.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do wonder what would happen if Jon sarcastically called Geoff &quot;girlfriend&quot;, provided that Geoff is out of the closet with the pack. I imagine Jon would have a nice aggravated bite wound for his remark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:02:32-08:00","id":308926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=308826#post308826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if it's forced. I mean, I have no room to speak. I've been taking a belt sander to the square peg for the past two days. If I were to make a suggestion, I'd say go ahead and incorporate those notes into the story. &quot;Geoff felt the need to come out of the closet... twice.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do wonder what would happen if Jon sarcastically called Geoff &quot;girlfriend&quot;, provided that Geoff is out of the closet with the pack. I imagine Jon would have a nice aggravated bite wound for his remark.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean, twice? Because of his First Change? It happened in front of his father, so they found out alongside him x)<br /> <br /> It all depends on how tired he is at the moment. Best case scenario, you get a passive-agressive retort. Otherwise, well...yeah, the bite wound. <br /> <br /> And with Jon in the pack, we now have two people that are partial to the Black Spiral! Oooh, Geoff is gonna have so much fun hating you guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T05:49:16-08:00","id":308974,"title":"","content":"<u>Bashir</u><br /> <br /> You still haven't chosen a specialty for Manipulation. You don't have to choose one, of course, but there is no benefit to not having a specialty in an attribute or ability rated 4 dots, unless you intend to choose one later during the course of play. You definitely need to choose one for Performance, though; that's required.<br /> <br /> The Skills aren't adding up. I only count 7 dots.<br /> <br /> The Rite of Boasting is a level 1 rite, if memory serves. So, you only need to spend one point on the Rites background to choose it.<br /> <br /> I thought that you had decided on the Intolerance flaw and the Mitanu's Tongue merit; did you change your mind? Wait, I see Intolerance under Background Descriptions, but not under flaws. Is this an error?<br /> <br /> Ah, it's &quot;Ruatma,&quot; though a spelling error isn't a big deal, of course.<br /> <br /> About Gaye, a few questions. You say that Jon was told that she's kinfolk; told by whom? Does she know that she's kinfolk, or what that means? Also, under what circumstances did Jon change in front of her? Remember, it doesn't just happen on its own. Unless Jon was frenzying at the time, he had to choose to change. Did she walk in on him unexpectedly? Or did he purposely show her his Garou nature? If it was the result of a frenzy, what sparked it, and how did she survive?<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of Gaye, I've been doing some thinking about my plans for her. If you have no objection, I'd like her to be an Electrical and Computer Engineering major at Rowan University. It fits a little better for what I have in mind for her (muah ha ha ha).<br /> <br /> <u>Flo</u><br /> <br /> The new notes are interesting; they add a little nuance to the character. If you like them, go ahead and keep them. I have no objection, and it's certainly something I can work with. Especially the one about his choice of tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T06:44:16-08:00","id":309045,"title":"","content":"Oh, I intend to keep them alright. I'm all for nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T14:30:10-08:00","id":309461,"title":"","content":"<u>Jim</u><br /> Oh, okay, cool. ^-^ I'll put her as Rorg, then.<br /> <br /> Also, since we seem to be pretty close to starting now, can I ask how we're going to roll dice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T05:12:34-08:00","id":310044,"title":"","content":"I had to break out the spread sheet to balance the books, so to speak. I scaled down the spreadsheet I used to make characters for A Time of War: Battletech RPG. I was a playtester, and kept writing how shit the creation process was. It takes me a half hour to make a character, but said character can be shot and die almost instantly.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the balance sheet I used. I will edit my post sometime later. As for the typographical error, it might have been influenced by the fact I've had to take the bus to <i><b><u>Raut</u>etientori</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I should state that this balance sheet is more for <b><i>my</i></b> benefit. I wanted to see where the numbers went.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\"> &#91;TABLE=&quot;border: 0, cellspacing: 0&quot;&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD=&quot;width: 113&quot;&#93;Attributes (7/5/3)&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD=&quot;width: 98&quot;&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD=&quot;width: 86&quot;&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD=&quot;width: 86&quot;&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;