;TD&#93;Subterfuge +1&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;-2&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Etiquette +1&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;-2&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;0&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Merits&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Mitanu's Tongue&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;-2&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Flaws&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Intolerance (Deadbeat Dads)&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;1&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;TR&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;Dark Secret&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93; &#91;/TD&#93; &#91;TD&#93;1&#91;/TD&#93; &#91;/TR&#93; &#91;/TABLE&#93;</pre> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edited the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306482#post306482\">edit</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-12-2014, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T21:37:04-08:00","id":310898,"title":"","content":"On the road, so here's a quick reply- Abilities are 13/9/5, not 13/7/5. Thats why you''re short, Bashir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:00:39-08:00","id":310924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=310898#post310898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the road, so here's a quick reply- Abilities are 13/9/5, not 13/7/5. Thats why you''re short, Bashir.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll pardon me while I produce a fresh, head-shaped indentation in my desk, okay? I'd like to use the excuse that it's a poster presentation at the university, but even then, I should be more thorough.<br /> <br /> Drive carefully. I'll fix it. And yes, I changed the kinfolk's story to fit your needs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edited: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306482#post306482\">Edited</a> the editing of the edit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-13-2014, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T13:07:55-08:00","id":311581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=309461#post309461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Jim</u><br /> Also, since we seem to be pretty close to starting now, can I ask how we're going to roll dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't trust online dice rollers, so everyone's going to have to come to my house in New Jersey every time we need to make a roll.<br /> <br /> ...No? Bad plan?<br /> <br /> In seriousness, many rolls I can and will make myself. Anything that I would normally roll behind a screen (such as a Per+Alertness roll) I will do off list and simply tailor my descriptions accordingly. I will occasionally let you know when I'm doing this, to make you nervous. ;-)<br /> <br /> When you guys need to roll, we will be using the <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Invisible Castle</a> site. Simply go to the Roll Dice page, enter in your character name and what dice you are rolling (i.e. &quot;8d10&quot;). When the roll is complete, you will be able to see the results, and you can copy the URL into the post so I can verify (usually in a spoiler tag), like so:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4715957/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4715957/</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As long as you use the same character name, I can easily verify the rolls by looking them up. You don't even have to make an account with Invisible Castle (though you can if you want to, of course).<br /> <br /> <u>Bashir</u><br /> <br /> Looks good. You still need to put the merit in, but aside from that, I think you're good to go.<br /> <br /> The last thing to do for your character is my part- I need to type up a personalized background information post and send it to you by PM. This is basically some information that your character has based on his background, Sept and Tribe, delivered in an IC format from a particular NPC int he setting. Like the background information presented in the first two posts of the recruitment thread, your character can consider this general knowledge, but whether he believes all of it is up to him (and you). Consider the source and the circumstances, and know that I am telling you flat out OOC that some of it is true, some of it is false and most of it is incomplete.<br /> <br /> I am going to start on that this evening and hope to get it to you late tonight or, failing that, tomorrow morning before I go to work.<br /> <br /> <u>Everyone</u><br /> <br /> I think all that's left on the character sheets is for Bashir to finish up as noted above for Jon, and for James to finish up a few things on Scott, like appearance. Once that's finished, I'll move the character sheets in spoiler tags to the second post in this thread. This will allow us to have easy access to them without having to search through the thread whenever we need to reference them. Now, once I make the move, those will be the official versions of the character sheet, meaning that when you spend xp, I'll make the changes as needed. It's just a convenience thing; it's too easy to get confused if multiple versions of the character sheet are floating around. So, everyone please take a minute to proofread your character sheets and make any minor changes that you want to make.<br /> <br /> I'll also take the opportunity to add in the free rites that I am choosing for everyone who purchased the Rituals knowledge (and of course I'll post that info here).<br /> <br /> When all that is said and done, we'll be ready to start. I'll put the posting guidelines here (and copy them to the first message in this thread for easy reference), and then I'll start the IC thread.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any last minute questions, concerns or issues before we get started?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T13:16:57-08:00","id":311610,"title":"","content":"The editing of my edit is my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=306482#post306482\">edition</a>.<br /> <br /> And at nearly midnight in Helsinki, I sleep. See you all tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T17:38:24-08:00","id":311794,"title":"","content":"*Raises hand* I do! I have a question!<br /> <br /> You said that the merit Supporter is really overpowered. Fair enough, I don't mind you rewritting it as long as it carries the same meaning, but have you thought of a houserule for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T22:34:53-08:00","id":314269,"title":"","content":"Does anyone remember those Coterie and Pack diagrams that showed the inner thoughts of a character towards the other members of the group? Just to have a little fun before the game starts, here's Jon's very naive views. They will very much change, likely on the first day!<br /> <br /> Jon:<i> How did I get here?</i><br /> <br /> Scott: <i>His martial arts are cool. I'm sure he has to be, what, yellow belt by now?</i><br /> Geoff: <i>When life gives you lemons, don't make lemonade. Make life take the lemons back! GET MAD!</i><br /> Val: <i>Jesus, I thought I had a tough enough upbringing.</i><br /> Echoes: <i>Speak up. I can't hear you.</i><br /> Hannah: <i>Very honorable. It's true what they say. A Lannister always repays his debts.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T06:37:52-08:00","id":314419,"title":"","content":"Oh god, he just Cave Johnsoned me.<br /> <br /> Alright, let's try it.<br /> <br /> Geoff : <i>This pack is just a walking ticking bomb. There's gonna be some serious fireworks, and I'll guess I'll have to do some damage control.</i><br /> <br /> Hannah :<i> I'm watching you. Don't even think of going all royalty on me.</i><br /> Scott :<i> Must be sad being the only one of your tribe around here, but I'm glad you're with us.</i><br /> Val : <i>What the hell is going on with you?!</i><br /> Echoes : <i>She kinda reminds me of some of the kids at the center... If only she wasn't Red Talon.</i><br /> Jon : <i>Yeah, keep being passive-aggressive with a group of Garou, it surely will end well.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-17-2014, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:37:46-08:00","id":314726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=311794#post311794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Raises hand* I do! I have a question!<br /> <br /> You said that the merit Supporter is really overpowered. Fair enough, I don't mind you rewritting it as long as it carries the same meaning, but have you thought of a houserule for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you for reminding me. Yes, I have decided. The text of the merit now reads as follows:<br /> <br /> You inspire all around you to greater efforts. Whether by speaking, writing or leading by example, you give anyone who works with you reason to go on and hope of success. You gain +1 die to all social rolls, or +2 if the roll involves someone you are helping or have helped directly in the past, and you give any group effort +1 to its total dice pool.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone remember those Coterie and Pack diagrams that showed the inner thoughts of a character towards the other members of the group? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember those things, though I never really used them for PCs before. Not a bad idea, Bashir. :-) Those looked pretty funny.<br /> <br /> Anyway, moving on, the character sheets all appear to be done (except for Scott's garou astrological sign, which we don't strictly need to start off and I don't want to delay us any longer), and I have just sent Jon's private character background to Bashir via PM. It seems like...<br /> <br /> drumroll, please...<br /> <br /> ...we're finally ready!! Yaaaaaay!!! :-D<br /> <br /> I want to give Bashir a little time to digest his background info, and everyone else one last chance to ask any final questions or make any final changes before we start, so my plan is to put up the posting guidelines tomorrow (and move the character sheets to their new home), then start IC roleplay in its own thread on Wednesday.<br /> <br /> I'm excited. Are you excited? I'm excited. :-)<br /> <br /> I know there have been some delays getting to this point, and for that I apologize, but now that we're finally ready, I'm glad we all stuck through it. I've been looking forward to this for quite a while, and I'm eager to begin.<br /> <br /> -Jim<br /> <br /> P.S.- Just for my own peace of mind, everyone please take a moment to check in so we can make sure we're all still accounted for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:59:56-08:00","id":314741,"title":"","content":"Supporter sounds good!<br /> <br /> And yay for checking in!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:14:23-08:00","id":314746,"title":"","content":"I'm here! And I am humbled by the history you wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:33:02-08:00","id":314764,"title":"","content":"When I was reading my background info, I had a big happy smile on my face because I loved his NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:56:58-08:00","id":314775,"title":"","content":"Checking in, and happy to start =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T18:18:58-08:00","id":314981,"title":"","content":"Still here. ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T18:38:08-08:00","id":314986,"title":"","content":"Please enter a message with at least 10 characters D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T10:32:54-08:00","id":315513,"title":"","content":"I'm here, there and in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T14:49:33-08:00","id":316545,"title":"","content":"I did one of the chart things too, seemed fun.<br /> <br /> Hannah: I can't believe these guys, they've all got potential, but no spines. Someone needs to teach them to strut.<br /> <br /> Geoff: I've never met a nice guy who wasn't a closet freak, sorry I'm not buying it.<br /> Scott: So you're like a kung fu Werewolf monk? You've got to be fucking kidding me...<br /> Val: Why do I get the feeling you're going to get us killed, and you don't even care?<br /> Echoes: Oh Em Gee! It's like a puppy and a little sister at the same time, let me do your hair! Or fur! Or hair!<br /> Jon: I once heard, in the past, you were a tribe of loyal Betas. Live up to that expectation Shadow Lord...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:48:20-08:00","id":316594,"title":"","content":"You know, I was afraid to be struck by the good guy syndrome, but it's nice to see that the rest of the pack don't trust me. \\o/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T20:06:38-08:00","id":316883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=316594#post316594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I was afraid to be struck by the good guy syndrome, but it's nice to see that the rest of the pack don't trust me. \\o/</div> </div> </div> </div>The games that were the most fun for me were the ones where the coterie did not trust each other at all at the start. As the characters got developed and everyone found the &quot;usefulness&quot; of the others, not to mention the character development, the games would swing into high gear awesomeness.<br /> <br /> I do find it hilarious that the <i>Red Talon</i> is the one closest to having good guy syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T20:13:21-08:00","id":316884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=316883#post316883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it hilarious that the <i>Red Talon</i> is the one closest to having good guy syndrome.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the white socks. It's all about the socks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T00:26:46-08:00","id":317079,"title":"","content":"Val: Life if a joke, all things show it. I thought so once; now I know it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Geoff: I know, I felt it too. But don't speak, just kiss me. <br /> <br /> Scott: Thiruvalluvar says 'The seat of life is love, anyone who does not have it is only a mass of bones encased by skin'. Yes, I think you understand me. <br /> <br /> Echoes: Oh lord, it's a talking wolf! Burn it! <br /> <br /> Jon: Bela Lugosi called, he <i>vants </i>his hair back. <br /> <br /> Hannah: Once, she asked me how to spell 'orange'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T14:33:30-08:00","id":321056,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm going to copy these to the first post in this thread for easy reference later, but for now, here are the posting guidelines.<br /> <br /> <u>Posting Guidelines and Other General Rules</u><br /> <br /> 1. Please keep the IC thread In Character, and confine OOC comments and questions to the Out of Character thread as much as possible. If it is necessary to put OOC information in the IC thread (such as the results of a roll), please put it in a spoiler tag and clearly label it as OOC.<br /> <br /> 2. When you guys need to roll dice, we will be using the <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/\" target=\"_blank\">Invisible Castle</a> site. Make sure you use the same character name every time you roll, to make it easier for me to look it up. When posting the results of the roll, post the results and the link in a spoiler tag. You won't always know the difficulty of the roll, so it's often best to just copy and paste the die results rather than just saying how many successes you think you got. Also, remember that many rolls will be done by me behind my ST screen, so you'll just find out the effect of the action, not the number of successes you did or didn't roll. This is almost always going to be the case for things like Alertness or Investigation rolls.<br /> <br /> 3. This game constitutes a single chronicle which will (hopefully) run from your characters' rite of passage through to the Apocalypse. It will be broken up into a series of four stories, after each of which we can sit down as a group and decide whether we want to end the chronicle there (after which I will write an epilogue to wrap up some plot threads), or whether we are having enough fun to continue into the next story of the chronicle. Each story will be [loosely] organized into chapters and interludes. A chapter will cover about as much play as could be accomplished in a long tabletop gaming session (more or less), and will be done primarily on this list. Interludes cover the time between chapters, and will be more flexible since most will be either one-on-one between me and one player, or done in smaller groups if some of the characters will be spending time together during interludes. Interludes can be handled by blue-booking, direct RP through PM or posts or, if circumstances permit, direct real time RP via a chat client like AIM. We'll take each interlude as it comes. As for scenes, the length of a scene is highly subjective and variable, and largely unimportant except where certain powers have a duration of one scene. In such cases, I'll let you guys know when a scene ends.<br /> <br /> 4. Each chapter will start with a single post by me introducing the initial scene. Once I have that post out, you are all free to respond to it, and each other. Please include in your first post a brief description of what your character looks like at the time, including what they are wearing. It doesn't have to be long (especially later on as we all become more familiar with the characters), but I find this is important to help us immerse ourselves. Generally speaking I will let the scene flow as it will, but occasionally I will slow things down if some PCs are having trouble posting frequently enough to keep up and they are being left behind.<br /> <br /> 5. When you post, remember that you only control your own character. Do not post the actions, words or thoughts of NPCs without my express permission, and do not ever post the actions, words or thoughts of the other PCs under any circumstances. You may also not make gross changes to the setting or environment without my express permission. For all these things, use common sense. If the scene is in a bar, you can assume that there is, say, a glass on the bar without asking my permission. You could also break said glass. You could talk to the bartender. You could not answer for the bartender; the bartender is an NPC, and I will answer for her. You could not assume that there is a hanging chandelier for your character to swing from- that is pretty unusual scenery for a bar. If the scene was in a fancy ballroom, however, assuming a chandelier would be just fine. In general, just use common sense and good judgment, and I'll let you know if you go too far. If you need to do anything that requires a roll (or that you think requires a roll), feel free to mention OOC what you think you should be rolling, and any modifiers that you think should apply. I'll let you know what to roll.<br /> <br /> 6. You guys can generally respond to each other in RP as much as you like; unless you are trying to do something that requires a roll, or involves the reactions of an NPC or something like that, you do not usually need to wait for me. The other exception is if I ask you guys to slow things down to allow another PC or group of PCs time to catch up. We'll try to avoid these kinds of disruptions, but unfortunately in a PbP setting they sometimes crop up.<br /> <br /> 7. Under normal circumstances, I would never post an action for your character. Even if they are being mind controlled in some way, I would almost always simply tell you off-list generally what the character must do and let you describe it IC (and such circumstances will be rare). However, just to expedite matters, I will occasionally make basic assumptions. For example, once the group makes the decision to go from point A to point B, rather than go through the tedium of letting everyone describe their characters getting into the cars, buckling their seatbelts and driving across town, I would move the scene along by simply typing &quot;The characters gather into their vehicles and drive across town without incident,&quot; then go on to describe the new scene.<br /> <br /> 8. IC posting is done in prose, as if writing a story, preferably in the present tense. So, you could post like this:<br /> <br /> Mari steps into the club, looking around. After taking in her surroundings, she walks up to the bar and addresses the bartender. &quot;I'm looking for information about a biker who was in here recently.&quot; She flashes a wad of cash, adding &quot;I can pay well for any help you could offer &quot;<br /> <br /> You would NOT post like this:<br /> <br /> I have Mari walk into the club and make a Perception+Alertness roll. Then I have her walk up to the bartender, ask for information about that biker guy from Chapter 2 and offer a bribe.<br /> <br /> The idea is that, when put together, our collective IC roleplay should read like a story (more or less). I'm not a grammar or spelling Nazi, and don't worry if you change tense once in a while. I'm not an English Major, after all, and I know that not everyone here speaks English as a first language. ;-)<br /> <br /> 9. Generally speaking, you should not be posting the thoughts or emotions of your character overtly. You can describe or imply them through your characters words, actions or body language, or use basic adjectives, as in &quot;Mari angrily throws her arm across the bar, scattering the glasses while she growls at the uncooperative bartender.&quot; However, it's usually not appropriate to post the IC private thoughts of your character in a thread. Blue booking for Interludes is an exception to this rule; there is a lot more latitude in terms of writing style there.<br /> <br /> 10. If, for whatever reason, you know you won't be able to post for a period of time, please let us know so that we aren't all waiting for you. The object of the game is to have fun, not to interfere in our lives. The nice thing about a PbP game is that you can check in from day to day as you have time. :-)<br /> <br /> 11. Experience will be awarded at the end of every chapter, and in smaller amounts at the end of every interlude. Interlude awards will vary wildly depending on numerous factors. Chapter awards will have a certain base number, which can be as few as one xp and as high as I see fit, based on the length of the chapter and how much xp I feel everyone needs to progress to keep pace with the story. Everyone will receive the base xp at the end of each chapter, plus certain additional awards at my discretion based on various factors. Everyone who played their character especially well will get an extra XP. Everyone who's character accomplished an important personal goal during the chapter will get an extra XP. That sort of thing. In addition, at the end of every chapter, I will allow all of you players to vote by secret ballot (via PM) on who was the best roleplayer during that chapter, doing the most to increase the fun of the game. You can't vote for yourselves, and I will not reveal the final vote count. However, whoever wins the vote at the end of each chapter will get an extra XP.<br /> <br /> 12. Except under certain rare circumstances, XP can only be spent during interludes. The main exception will be if the characters learn a gift from a spirit during play, which would be purchased right away. Any increase in a trait via XP will need to be justified, and greater justification will be needed for greater increases. In general, a trait can only be increased by one dot at a time, though I may make exceptions to this rule in extraordinary circumstances. If you can't justify the increase of a trait by the events that happened in a chapter (for example, if you want to increase your character's melee ability, but your character didn't actually use a melee weapon during the entire last chapter), all or part of an interlude can be used for training or other such justification (that's part of what they're for, after all). I'm usually pretty flexible on these issues.<br /> <br /> 13. With the exception of Totem (which costs a flat 3xp per dot), Backgrounds can't be increased through XP. They will fluctuate through roleplay. If you want to work on increasing a particular background in an interlude, let me know and we can try to work something out, depending on exact circumstances.<br /> <br /> 14. This is an adult game. We will be dealing with adult themes at times within the context of the game. It is not my goal to make anyone feel uncomfortable; we are all here to have a good time, after all. However, it is my goal to make you think. I don't sugar-coat my games, and I especially don't sugar coat my villains. Murder, torture, kidnapping, rape, mind control and other such things are all possibilities in the game. Sometimes these things happen to random NPCs. Sometimes these things happen to NPCs your characters care about. Sometimes these things happen to player characters. Sometimes these things are perpetrated by player characters. If there is anything in particular that makes you uncomfortable or would ruin your enjoyment of the game, talk to me about it. Like I said, it's not my goal to make people uncomfortable, but I don't run games for children. Again, I encourage you to speak to me directly, and in private, if you feel discomfited by any of these possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T17:33:13-08:00","id":321205,"title":"","content":"And we're live. The IC Thread is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/321065-ic-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse\">here</a>, and the first IC post setting the scene for the start of your characters' rite of passage is ready to go. Go ahead and everybody start with your first post introducing yourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T21:36:01-08:00","id":321401,"title":"","content":"Hey Jim, I see that we're live in an IC thread. I had thought that it would be a play-by-email game. Email would be significantly more convenient for me to read and reply to posts throughout the day. I'm also not sure how comfortable I am publicly posting in, as point 14 says, a game with &quot;adult themes&quot;. Would there be any issue with using email to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:23:59-08:00","id":321555,"title":"","content":"It was always my intention that this be a PbP game. PBEM games, while similar in style and pacing, require more effort on the part of the ST to keep records of all posts and to keep the chronology straight. A PbP game in a forum makes my life considerably easier by maintaining continuity of posts and an archive. So, I don't want to change to a PBEM game.<br /> <br /> However, you do raise a good point with regards to privacy. I would be willing to switch to a forum that would allow us to play privately, if that is what everyone wants to do. What do all of you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:41:38-08:00","id":321587,"title":"","content":"I think the whole point of White Wolf (and Onyx Path) games was that it embraced more mature themes. If we can say words like fuck, shit, and cunt in character or not targeting someone OOCly, without being censored, it's fine. However, I respect folks' decisions, so everyone feels comfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:49:36-08:00","id":321592,"title":"","content":"I'm okay. No one knows who the hell I am anyway. I do want James to feel comfortable though. Is there a reason why you don't want to post in a public forum? If you're worried about being identified or something like that, I'm sure it wouldn't be an issue, it's not like we know your adress or something (or do we...?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T02:44:48-08:00","id":321605,"title":"","content":"Just take comfort that it's pretty much guaranteed this won't be Werewolf: Fifty Shades of Gray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T03:11:03-08:00","id":321614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=321605#post321605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just take comfort that it's pretty much guaranteed this won't be Werewolf: Fifty Shades of Gray.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?! But I thought this was going to be a steamy and furry erotic novel with Puppy Love! D:<br /> <br /> Ahem. In all seriousness : I'm with Josh on this one. Staying here would make it easier for me because I already have another PbP on this forum, but honestly, I don't care if we play it here or on another forum. Although, I never tried PBEM games, and I'm not sure I'll like it. But do whatever you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-25-2014, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","na