aguely like you imagined him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:22:13-08:00","id":329131,"title":"","content":"I was going with a slightly darker hair color, but it's really neat too. This is the first time someone actually drawed a character of mine, so I'm especially overjoyed. ^^<br /> <br /> And I must say, I love the wolves t-shirt for him, Jon and Echoes. So ironic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:22:14-08:00","id":329132,"title":"","content":"I fully concur. I really, really like how you did Jon's homid form, too. Captures that nerd-hipster kind of look I imagined. Great work on everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:47:14-08:00","id":329166,"title":"","content":"That's seriously awesome! Thanks a ton. I'm glad you made Hannah's Chrinos look insane and caked with blood.<br /> <br /> Invisable Castle seems to be fine now. Yesterday it was just a white page that said I could buy the domain name if I wanted. All I was going to do was roll Empathy to see if I could pick up on Stir understanding the directions relatively well.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:05:20-08:00","id":329264,"title":"","content":"I should ask what protocol people want to use? I mean, during my studies at the end of this period, I'm often alt+tabbing between whatever paper I have to read, to my browser to refresh the pages, so I often am able to jump in and respond to post after post. I'm a bit overzealous in playing this game, and I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> I think for dice rolls, maybe use the BBCode link? <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731073/\" target=\"_blank\">10d10=51</a>, or replace the Number with the pose you want to roll for?<br /> <br /> Such as <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731073/\" target=\"_blank\">(Stamina to Change, no Primal Urge, Diff 6, Homid)</a><br /> <br /> I dunno. Going crazy. Lack of sleep. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 12-03-2014, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:47:43-08:00","id":329410,"title":"","content":"It's already been said, but yeah, they're awesome! You really captured Echo there. :-D Once I stop procrastinating with my own art, I'll def draw you something in return.<br /> <br /> As for posting, if it's alright, would you guys mind giving everyone at least a day (unless something demands an immediate response, like someone spitting in your face or something) to reply after the ST has before skipping? :-o<br /> <br /> With dice, I just stick everything under a spoiler, usually with the BBcode link if I know what the difficulty is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T16:10:15-08:00","id":329615,"title":"","content":"I don't mind doing dice however, even if we all use different formats, so long as it's clear there was a roll.. I'll try to keep my rolls pretty close to my intended action though so it never get's confusing as to why I rolled. Other than that, I'll try to slow down posting, sorry.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T19:24:11-08:00","id":329806,"title":"","content":"I should have added that the reason I wanted a different format is purely an aesthetic one. I'd be reading a great post, then WHAM! lots of dice roll information. Ruins my immersion.<br /> <br /> But now that I reflect on it, it's no different than my groups RL. &quot;I swing my axe for...&quot; *dice roll*...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T20:12:40-08:00","id":329830,"title":"","content":"I tried something different to fit the rolls seamlessly into the narrative. What do you think?<br /> <br /> Also : it's my very first roll ever of Werewolf! I hope I didn't already screw this up. x)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:48:37-08:00","id":329871,"title":"","content":"Those drawings look great, Josh. :-) Thank you for putting so much time into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=329264#post329264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should ask what protocol people want to use? I mean, during my studies at the end of this period, I'm often alt+tabbing between whatever paper I have to read, to my browser to refresh the pages, so I often am able to jump in and respond to post after post. I'm a bit overzealous in playing this game, and I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> I think for dice rolls, maybe use the BBCode link? <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731073/\" target=\"_blank\">10d10=51</a>, or replace the Number with the pose you want to roll for?<br /> <br /> Such as <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731073/\" target=\"_blank\">(Stamina to Change, no Primal Urge, Diff 6, Homid)</a><br /> <br /> I dunno. Going crazy. Lack of sleep. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I... ummm... don't really understand the tech stuff. What is BBCode exactly?<br /> <br /> I don't really care how the rolls appear in the posts as long as it isn't obtrusive; that's why I went with spoiler tags. However, I want to be able to actually see the roll in the post; I don't want to have to follow the link for each one. I really do trust you guys; I only intend to verify the rolls with the link on a spot-check basis. Especially since I will often be looking from my phone, making having to go over to Invisible Castle to see the results of every roll inconvenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I tried something different to fit the rolls seamlessly into the narrative. What do you think?<br /> <br /> Also : it's my very first roll ever of Werewolf! I hope I didn't already screw this up. x) </div> </div> </div>It's a fine idea, Flo, but it makes things a little difficult for me as I have to keep linking back and forth. The best way, for me, is for everyone to post the results of the roll (by which I mean the actual numbers you rolled on each die, not the number of successes you think you got based on what you think the difficulty is) in a spoiler tag with a url (you don't even have to turn it into a link if you do. You can just copy-paste the whole thing from Invisible Castle. If this is immersion breaking for you guys, feel free to stick them all the way at the end of the post. For example:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">4d10 \u2192 [10,6,2,7] <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/</a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or, to make things even simpler, just copy-paste the entire entry:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Die roll for Geoff Bolen</b><br /><br /> Rolled on: Dec. 3, 2014, 8:15 p.m.<br /> 4d10 \u2192 [10,6,2,7] = (25)<br /> <br /> [<a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/\" target=\"_blank\">link to roll</a>] [<a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1527446\" target=\"_blank\">link to character</a>]<br /> <b>Formatted Versions</b><br /><br /> Link <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/</a> HTML &lt;a href=&quot;http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/&quot;&gt;4d10=25&lt;/a&gt; Character <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1527446\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1527446</a> Castle Forum [roll=Geoff Bolen]#4731569[/roll] BBCode <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4731569/\" target=\"_blank\">4d10=25</a> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> Whatever works as long as all the info is there and we don't need to change pages to find out the result- just to verify if I feel the need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=329050#post329050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a reminder guys, but Jim said not to post too much of our character's thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Thank you for bringing this up, James. I know this may seem a little odd to you guys, but posts that include lengthy portions of the characters' thoughts are very jarring. Think of it like this- if we were all together, sitting around a table and playing this game, would everyone be able to see into your characters' thoughts? Nope. They'd hear what your characters say, and they would have the actions that you describe, but they would not know what the character was REALLY thinking, under most circumstances. When we're sitting around a table, we have to infer what everyone else's character is thinking and feeling based on the described actions.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, we can simply read every PC's innermost thoughts and feelings like a first person narrative... it takes away a lot of the uncertainty of personal interaction.<br /> <br /> There are exceptions to this rule. Obviously Mindspeak and similar abilities, or if you're narrating an internal dialogue, such as the character having a mental conversation with a past life or some such (though, naturally, half that conversation would be me). The other big exception will be blue booking during interludes- stylistically, you guys will be free to write those in any style you'd like.<br /> <br /> But, during play, it's not a good idea to include lengthy portions that detail the character's inner thoughts, especially verbatim internal monologues. A little bit is OK once in a while, and if we're in a situation where a character gets separated from the rest of the party and has no one to have meaningful interaction with for a period of time I will relax this considerably, but when everyone's together, try to confine what you write to what the other characters can experience with their own senses (which, remember, usually includes smell since we're talking about werewolves here, which does give some additional latitude).<br /> <br /> I understand the desire to express as much of the characters and their motivations as possible. But remember, while we are telling a story, we are <i>not</i> writing a novel. This is a cooperative storytelling experience, and part of that cooperative experience includes misunderstandings and misinterpretations which are muted or stifled when everyone knows OOC what every other character is thinking.<br /> <br /> Tone. Inflection. Gestures. Body Language. Scent. Facial Expression. Tail Position. Gaze. Breathing. All of these (and many more) are tools you can use to express what is going on inside your characters' heads without spelling it out (and that's not even counting good old fashioned speech).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sFBhR4QcBtE\" target=\"_blank\">I think the Robot Devil put it best, if you'll indulge me by watching this clip. :-)</a><br /> <br /> -Jim<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:05:48-08:00","id":329879,"title":"","content":"Actually, for an example of what I'm talking about, let me take a selection from one of Bashir's posts (hope you don't mind me putting you on the spot, Bashir).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/321065-ic-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=329096#post329096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jon could hear it all in his head now. All the complaining no matter what road they take.<i> It's too cold out here. It's too wet and icy in the canoe. Why are there so many empty packets of strawberry cheesecake trail mix and cans of Dr. Peppers back here?</i> And he must not forget about being trapped in a car with a wolf that smells like... that.<br /> <br /> Jon didn't like where any of this was going. He glanced briefly over to the elders. He was about to ask for advice, but he then stopped. <i>No. No running to the &quot;adults&quot; for help.</i> After choking back his words, he turned to Val and responded, &quot;Well, we can take my car. I mean, I could fit all six of us in there. Bit cramped. Also, the heater only has two settings: off, and <i>subtle</i>. But if we're going to be inconspicuous, do you think the Diplomat is the way to go? No, I'm honestly asking your opinion.&quot; Though maybe he wasn't, as Jon cocked his head to the side, a pained look on his face as he tried to indicate Echoes. On one hand, he genuinely wanted to respect her. On the other, would being trapped in a closed car be good on the olfactory senses?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I want to avoid. We can all see exactly what Jon was thinking just by reading. Think about other ways that these things could have been expressed. Bashir did a good job of giving descriptions of what Jon was doing, his expressions and gestures, but then goes on to explain exactly what each of those gestures meant, leaving us no room for ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Let's take the last three sentences especially. Bashir details exactly what Jon's feelings are about Echoes and why. Wouldn't it be more interesting if we had to figure it out for ourselves from Jon's actions? For example... &quot;Jon cocked his head to the side, a pained look on his face as he tried to indicate Echoes. He reached out one hand a little, gesturing for her to include herself in the conversation, but with the other hand he rubbed his nose and sniffed slightly without seeming to realize what he was doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not trying to re-write anyone's posts, I'm just trying to give an example of how these inner thoughts and feelings could potentially be expressed without verbatim dictation of those thoughts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/321065-ic-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=329096#post329096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jon kept his back to the Barbie doll while giving his opinion to the others, &quot;I think we should walk it, as she suggests. Though I for one will give the 'as wolves' thing a pass. I've only tried it once, and I'm still finding my legs. Or all four. I think we should do what we feel we do best. If we aren't in our best form, we may end up fucking everything up...&quot; He stretched his words to emphasize them, &quot;...<i>on our first miiiiission.</i> I've got some old blankets in the trunk. They need to be washed, though. That could keep you warm, I think.&quot;<br /> <br /> A hand thrusts into his jacket pocket and pulled out a packet of strawberry cheesecake trail mix. Jon opened it and crunched down on a couple of the oat cluster pieces. <i>Breakfast of champions</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part, on the other hand, was perfect. Jon turns his back on Hannah, but we're left to interpret for ourselves what he means by that gesture. Bashir provides emphasis for Jon's words by explaining Jon's tone and inflection, drawing out the words, rather than simply saying what he was emphasizing and why.<br /> <br /> Do you guys get what I mean now?<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 12-04-2014, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T22:43:52-08:00","id":329899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=329879#post329879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, for an example of what I'm talking about, let me take a selection from one of Bashir's posts (hope you don't mind me putting you on the spot, Bashir).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I take responsibility for encouraging the thought processes. Leading, even if unconsciously, by example. I've read too many authors that do stream-of-conscious writing. It's influenced my prosaic style. I'm making an effort to curb that. I mean, I don't do it in any of my scientific papers. I think. Great, now I'm going to go back and reread all my past reports. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This part, on the other hand, was perfect. Jon turns his back on Hannah, but we're left to interpret for ourselves what he means by that gesture. Bashir provides emphasis for Jon's words by explaining Jon's tone and inflection, drawing out the words, rather than simply saying what he was emphasizing and why. </div> </div> </div>I will say I read a paper on certain animal behaviors, so that inspired me to be more... um... open-to-interpretationesque? English is difficult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T05:58:40-08:00","id":330050,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'll try to work on my writing then. It's just that I'm used to do this in PbP, and I'm terrible at descriptions, be it in French or in English, and I'm way better with dialogue, so it's almost like a reflex for me to put some insight commentary from my character into my posts. I'll do my best to limit that from now on.<br /> <br /> And okay, I'll write the dice rolls as such now. I just discovered how to make this spoiler tag, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T06:38:46-08:00","id":330084,"title":"","content":"Josh, that is some really awesome art. I like the way that you drew Scott. Thanks for taking the time to draw the whole pack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:22:24-08:00","id":330283,"title":"","content":"I can't remember if I mentioned this before, but you guys can always ask me for more detail about a scene. If my description doesn't include some detail of what your characters' might be able to see and hear that you want to know, just ask and I'll fill it in.<br /> <br /> Remember, I try to get the feel of these games as close to being at a tabletop together as possible, so don't hesitate to ask me OOC questions in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:20:00-08:00","id":330872,"title":"","content":"I'm so glad everyone liked their picture. I may draw some other things, like banes or formori we encounter, or notable NPCs or stuff like that. I think it's always cool to have a visual reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T00:23:11-08:00","id":330874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=330872#post330872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so glad everyone liked their picture. I may draw some other things, like banes or formori we encounter, or notable NPCs or stuff like that. I think it's always cool to have a visual reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need a more detailed description on an NPC, let me know. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T01:15:28-08:00","id":330903,"title":"","content":"OK, I need clarification. Bashir's post implies that he can see the man. Have you guys moved up to where everyone can see him, or are you still far back enough that only Echoes can see him? Remember, she's using heightened senses; when she saw him, all the rest of the PCs could only see the light from his cigarette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T04:29:19-08:00","id":330981,"title":"","content":"I thought we left Val behind, considering he was trying to follow us on two legs :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T04:42:22-08:00","id":330985,"title":"","content":"Strike two on my behalf. I corrected it to say he arrived with everyone standing around. Not using perception, just wondering why everyone stopped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:52:52-08:00","id":331534,"title":"","content":"As far as I was concerned only Echoes could see anything besides the cigarette glow, and we were all hanging back a bit.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:59:48-08:00","id":331539,"title":"","content":"I'm also going to start using this account for these threads. Seems to make sense to me anyway. Does anyone know how I'd link the post with my character sheet right into the signature on here?<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hannah Dawnstar<br /> Ahround, Homid, Silver Fang<br /> Rage Across the Delaware Valley<br /> <br /> Character Sheet:","edited":{"userid":4450,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4450-hannah_dawnstar","user":"Hannah_Dawnstar","date":". 12-05-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4450-hannah_dawnstar","name":"Hannah_Dawnstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4450_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T22:28:46-08:00","id":331956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/321065-ic-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=331567#post331567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He still muttered for him : &quot;Next time, I'll dedicate my jacket too...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember the house rule- no Rite of Talisman Dedication in my game. Within reason, everything shifts with the character unless it is dramatically appropriate for the clothes to end up all shredded (like an intense frenzy or whatever). I hate messing around with what is dedicated and what isn't.<br /> <br /> I once had an ST who was a stickler about that sort of thing, so I ended up having my character in that game stop wearing socks and underwear so he wouldn't have to dedicate them as a form of peaceful protest. Anyway, ever since then I've said to hell with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T22:42:29-08:00","id":331962,"title":"","content":"Oh, they way I understood it, I thought you meant &quot;this rite still exists, but I'm not going to keep track of what's dedicated and what's not. It's for you to choose appropriately.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll edit it then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T00:00:38-08:00","id":332007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=331962#post331962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, they way I understood it, I thought you meant &quot;this rite still exists, but I'm not going to keep track of what's dedicated and what's not. It's for you to choose appropriately.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll edit it then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry about the misunderstanding then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T06:42:27-08:00","id":332932,"title":"","content":"If anybody was waiting on me, Scott is just going to wait and see right now. He's not convinced that this guy isn't just a random butcher or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T08:15:16-08:00","id":332969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hannah_Dawnstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=331539#post331539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how I'd link the post with my character sheet right into the signature on here?<br /> <br /> -Mark</div> </div> </div> </div>Use this, without the *:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\"> &#91;*url=http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=289277#post289277&#93;Character Sheet&#91;/url&#93;</pre> </div>Speaking of sheets, have our rites been picked? :-o<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T17:47:13-08:00","id":333593,"title":"","content":"Jim pointed out I'm not suppose to have more than one forum account, so nix an IC account. If the mods see this, whoops, feel free to delete the other account, I'm not going to use it. Regardless, thanks for telling me how to make that work Eve.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T01:03:50-08:00","id":333890,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry about that, I just didn't want to see you get banned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stir of Echoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=332969#post332969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of sheets, have our rites been picked? :-o</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh! I knew I forgot something! Don't worry, I'll get to it ASAP, next time I have a day off and time to consult the books to confirm my choices (well before they come up in the game). Probably... Thursday-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":". 12-08-2014, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T03:56:47-08:00","id":334082,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering, how is rolling dice going to work? Not post-wise or website-wise, but when do we do it? I'm used to dice being rolled when the ST asks for it. I hadn't rolled to shapeshift because Scott would of just continued to try it a hundred times until he got it, so I figured it wasn't appropriate. But I would prefer not to keep making assumptions in how Jim handles his game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T19:09:56-08:00","id":334731,"title":"","content":"The only reason I rolled for Hannah to transform is that on a botch its possible to get stuck for awhile, which at this age and experience into the characters life as Garou seems pretty fitting. I also tend to look at a dice roll as the ultimate stated intention, like in my last roll I wanted to provide a diversion for the pack's sneaking. I didn't know if it would work or not, and it didn't seem super obvious it ought to, but it was my intention, so I rolled. That's my philosophy anyway.<br /> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T07:49:42-08:00","id":338065,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, sorry I've been incommunicado for a few days, but work has been absolutely insane. I'd intended to take today to catch up, but I just got called in again. I am supposed to be free tomorrow afternoon and evening, so it is my intent to post then. If I get stuck working another double, then I'll stay up after I get home at midnight tomorrow night and post before I go to bed, come hell or high water.<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:42:17-08:00","id":339243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathmatchFM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=334082#post334082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was wondering, how is rolling dice going to work? Not post-wise or website-wise, but when do we do it? I'm used to dice being rolled when the ST asks for it. I hadn't rolled to shapeshift because Scott would of just continued to try it a hundred times until he got it, so I figured it wasn't appropriate. But I would prefer not to keep making assumptions in how Jim handles his game.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=334731#post334731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason I rolled for Hannah to transform is that on a botch its possible to get stuck for awhile, which at this age and experience into the characters life as Garou seems pretty fitting. I also tend to look at a dice roll as the ultimate stated intention, like in my last roll I wanted to provide a diversion for the pack's sneaking. I didn't know if it would work or not, and it didn't seem super obvious it ought to, but it was my intention, so I rolled. That's my philosophy anyway.<br /> <br /> -Mark</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the most part, simple things like transformation in a non-critical situation can be handwaved unless I say otherwise. I didn't want to say anything because I wanted to let everyone have a chance to try out the dice roller and such on simple mechanics with little consequence before we start getting into the heavy stuff. So, for example, shape changing when at the meeting with the elders didn't really need a roll unless I said otherwise. However, shape changing when preparing to confront the mysterious smelly man should be rolled, because the situation could (theoretically) turn bad at any moment.<br /> <br /> Now, all that being said, if you guys want to roll something, it's rare that I'll stop you. Botches can be quite fun, after all. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T15:49:05-08:00","id":344189,"title":"","content":"Hm...Guys? It's getting cold in this forest...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T17:49:29-08:00","id":344277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=344189#post344189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...Guys? It's getting cold in this forest...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to give everyone a chance to reply, if they wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T04:07:42-08:00","id":344552,"title":"","content":"I hope no one is waiting on me! Scott may chime in, but I haven't seen the right opportunity yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-d