/> <br /> -Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T17:24:26-08:00","id":356110,"title":"","content":"One quick thing, but I don't believe Scott ever introduced himself as &quot;Scott&quot;. He just said he was &quot;the Bridge-Between-the-People&quot;, so Hannah would probably call him &quot;Bridge&quot; like Geoff did. Likely confusing since I call him &quot;Scott&quot; when I describe him.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I'm sure sure if you've caught Scott's point (probably because he says everything five times more complicated than it needs to be), but he's not kicking Val out, he's telling Val that if he wants to stay, he has to stay of his own will, and if he doesn't want to be a member of this pack, then he should leave. <br /> <br /> Essentially, a pack should be made up of people who want to be in a pack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3789-deathmatchfm","name":"DeathmatchFM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T23:46:54-08:00","id":357292,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. I hope I'm not delaying things too much. I figure Jon is one who tends to wait for openings to act.<br /> <br /> Staying out of the dispute unless he gets dragged in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T07:32:03-08:00","id":357454,"title":"","content":"Well, that was exciting. ;-) I just want to wait to be sure Val is going to proceed with the group, then I'll move us along with another post.<br /> <br /> Once we get moving again, will Echoes still be taking the lead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T14:04:35-08:00","id":357726,"title":"","content":"Yes, if we're all okay with that.<br /> <br /> And apologies for my silence this past week, the holidays were a bit crazy here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T21:33:22-08:00","id":358034,"title":"","content":"I see no problem with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:14:53-08:00","id":358419,"title":"","content":"Well what did you think Val was going to do? He's like a 12 year old, tell him to do something, and he does the opposite. And this might be a little to academic, but remember Val, like most of the pack, come from a post-modern, post-industrial society. Now, they're thrust into a pre-modern, tribal culture, which is highly insular and xenophobic. Naturally, there'll be adjustment issues. The idea of belonging to a pack, of regarding near-strangers as brothers and sisters would be quite alien. Most likely only Echoes would be at ease within such an environment. So while I can appreciate Scott's view, I hope you can see Val's side of things too. He's got reasons for being obnoxious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T17:58:09-08:00","id":358680,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the late answer, I'm studying for my finals right now.<br /> <br /> Edit : just to clarify something. If Echoes wants to take the lead, geoff wil let here. He's just trying to get the group started, but if anyone pass him and go faster, he'll try to match his speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:14:31-08:00","id":358860,"title":"","content":"Good luck with the exams Flo! Or should I say bon chance? I hope they go well for you : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T05:37:27-08:00","id":359021,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's bonne chance, since chance is a feminine noun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But still, thanks.<br /> <br /> Quick question : what do pazu and chalo mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T09:07:24-08:00","id":359219,"title":"","content":"As you can probably gather, my French is 'tres horrible'. Pazu is Sanskrit for 'beasts' and chalo is Hindi for 'come on/let's go!' Very useful word if you're ever in India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:59:50-08:00","id":361025,"title":"","content":"Invisible Castle is down again.<br /> <br /> While we wait for it to come back up, could we use <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as an alternative? I'd like to have Echo take a closer look at the trail (with a focus on smell). It works much the same way:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://sheetgen.dalines.net/wiki/WikiDiceRoller?hash=76deb51f\" target=\"_blank\">Echo rolled <b>8</b> dice to &quot;<i>perception + alertness</i>&quot; (no rerolls) (1s substracted) 9,2,3,6,7,9,1,2 </a><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T06:58:04-08:00","id":361265,"title":"","content":"Stupid website. Yeah, that's fine, we'll go with that roll.<br /> <br /> In reference to the description- Stir of Echoes actually got a fair bit of information through that magic nose of hers. Unfortunately, she has insufficient knowledge of humans to properly interpret all of it. This will change over time, as she has more interactions with human society.<br /> <br /> An example: the &quot;unnatural fragrance&quot; that she can't identify, any of the homids would simply register as &quot;aftershave.&quot; Or, if they had enough successes, &quot;Old Spice.&quot; Echoes, however, doesn;t know what aftershave or old spice are so, even though she got enough successes on her per+awareness roll to identify the fragrance, her background and experience are not sufficient to actually do so.<br /> <br /> Make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T00:51:28-08:00","id":362214,"title":"","content":"So guys, I've been wanting to draw some more werewolf related stuff, and I've been thinking of doing everyone's mentors (not in that way!...well, maybe Steve Bolen...) I've got a pretty good idea of what Sunchaser looks likes (if you don't mind that artistic license Jim : P) But don't have a clue about anyone else. I'm also not sure if everyone <i>has </i>a mentor, but everyone had a sort of sponsor for the rite of passage, so maybe I can draw them? I want to draw them in homid form (Except for Sunset Howl, who'll be in lupus/hispo). However, if you want your mentor to be in crinos/glabro whatever instead, just say so.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure who has the descriptions of their mentor/contact etc. but if you could give them to me, I'd be grateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T02:18:53-08:00","id":362240,"title":"","content":"Got it. :-D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure who has the descriptions of their mentor/contact etc. but if you could give them to me, I'd be grateful. </div> </div> </div>From what I know, Sunset Howl is a reddish wolf with at least one prominent scar across her muzzle. That's all I know, I'm afraid. D; But thanks, it's seriously awesome of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T04:44:47-08:00","id":362330,"title":"","content":"You're quite welcome, Eve. Drawing for an audience is pretty good motivation though, so it's not entirely unselfish : p. And red wolf with a scar gives me plenty of room to work with. Perhaps she may end up as the infamous 'Pimp Wolf' whispered of in the darkest Garou legends...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:06:33-08:00","id":362512,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Jon's initiators would be &quot;mentors&quot;. It might be better if it were &quot;whoever he tolerates (and is tolerated by) the most&quot;. Although it would be interesting to see how &quot;Dad&quot; is interpreted.<br /> <br /> But seriously, awesome of you. No need to go through the trouble on my side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:52:16-08:00","id":362565,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's a really cool idea! I shall draw 'Dad'...Seeing as his description's been kept deliberately vague, it'll be fun deciding on a look for him. Expect the unexpected. ; ) And it's no trouble at all, I just wish I could do more. If I had the ability, I'd convert our adventure into comic form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:55:31-08:00","id":362568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/288755-ooc-rage-across-the-delaware-valley-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=362214#post362214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've been thinking of doing everyone's mentors (not in that way!...well, maybe Steve Bolen...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Get off my uncle! D: No, NOT LIKE THAT NO--<br /> <br /> Ahem. That'd be swell! I'm awfully bad at physical description though...<br /> Steve is 38, about 240 lb and 6'2, which makes for a quite sturdy man. Like his nephew, he's rather tall and broad-shouldered, with a rather angular, with a broken nose that he never really wanted to reset, thinking that it gives him a look of rugged handsomeness, which goes well his smirk of cockiness. He has a full beard, short brown hair. As for clothes, well, the ones that Jim gave him during the introductory post will fit perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:58:19-08:00","id":362570,"title":"","content":"Actually, the vagueness about &quot;Dad&quot; is something that Bashir and I need to discuss at some point. I was fine with it to a certain extent during character creation, since we were trying to get the game off the ground and we had enough information to get started with, but it can't continue indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.t